Since the beginning of the [[Gaza war]] on [[October 7 attacks|7 October 2023]], the Israeli military and authorities [[Israeli war crimes|committed numerous war crimes]], such as the [[collective punishment]] of the [[Palestinians|Palestinian people]], attacks on civilians in densely populated areas (including [[Israeli bombing of the Gaza Strip|bombings]] of [[Attacks on health facilities during the Gaza war|hospitals and medical facilities]], [[Attacks on refugee camps in the Gaza war|refugee camps]], [[Attacks on schools during the Israeli invasion of Gaza|schools and educational institutions]], and [[2023 Israeli airstrikes on municipal services in the Gaza Strip|municipal services]]); the [[Torture during the Gaza war|torture]] and executions of civilians; [[Sexual and gender-based violence against Palestinians during the Israel–Hamas war|sexual violence]] including rape; and [[Gaza genocide|genocide]]. Further war crime charges against Israel include [[Gaza Strip evacuations|forced evacuations]], mistreatment and torture of [[Mass detentions in the Gaza war|Palestinian prisoners]], and the destruction of [[Destruction of cultural heritage during the Israeli invasion of the Gaza Strip|cultural heritage]]. Humanitarian organizations such as [[Human Rights Watch]], [[Amnesty International]], [[B'tselem]], and [[Oxfam]], as well as human rights groups and experts, including the [[Independent International Commission of Inquiry on the Occupied Palestinian Territory|UN Independent International Commission of Inquiry]] and [[United Nations special rapporteur]]s, have documented these actions.<ref>{{bulletedlist|{{cite web |last1=Murphy |first1=Matt |title=Israel, Hamas accused of war crimes in new UN report |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cl55gzp7vn9o |website=BBC News |date=12 June 2024 |access-date=13 June 2024}}|{{cite web|title=Israel/Palestine: Devastating Civilian Toll as Parties Flout Legal Obligations|url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/10/09/israel/palestine-devastating-civilian-toll-parties-flout-legal-obligations|website=[[Human Rights Watch]]|date=9 October 2023|access-date=13 October 2023|archive-date=9 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231009202840/https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/10/09/israel/palestine-devastating-civilian-toll-parties-flout-legal-obligations|url-status=live}}|{{cite web|title=Revenge policy in motion; Israel committing war crimes in Gaza|url=https://www.btselem.org/press_releases/20231010_revenge_policy_in_motion_israel_committing_war_crimes_in_gaza|website=[[B'tselem]]|access-date=12 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022010521/https://www.btselem.org/press_releases/20231010_revenge_policy_in_motion_israel_committing_war_crimes_in_gaza|url-status=live}}|{{cite news|last1=Robertson|first1=Nick|title=UN experts condemn attacks on civilians in Israel, Gaza as 'war crimes'|url=https://thehill.com/policy/international/4251899-un-civilians-israel-gaza-war-crimes/|work=[[The Hill (newspaper)|The Hill]]|access-date=12 October 2023|archive-date=12 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231012140640/https://thehill.com/policy/international/4251899-un-civilians-israel-gaza-war-crimes/|url-status=live}}|{{cite news|last1=Speri|first1=Alice|title=Israel Responds to Hamas Crimes by Ordering Mass War Crimes in Gaza|url=https://theintercept.com/2023/10/09/israel-hamas-war-crimes-palestinians/|work=[[The Intercept]]|access-date=12 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022010546/https://theintercept.com/2023/10/09/israel-hamas-war-crimes-palestinians/|url-status=live}}|{{cite web |title=Northern Gaza is being erased – global leaders must act now to end Israel's atrocities |url=https://www.oxfam.org/en/press-releases/urgent-joint-statement-northern-gaza-being-erased-global-leaders-must-act-now-end |website=Oxfam International |access-date=17 October 2024}}|{{cite news |last1=Nashed |first1=Mat |last2= |date=2024-04-17 |title=The thousands of Palestinians Israel arrests, tortures, holds even in death |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/4/17/the-thousands-of-palestinians-israel-arrests-tortures-hold-even-in-death |website=Al Jazeera |language=en |access-date=2024-06-14}}|{{cite web |last1=Pillay |first1=Navi |title=Presentation by the Commission of Inquiry on the Occupied Palestinian Territory, including East Jerusalem, and in Israel |url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/news/2024/06/commission-inquiry-occupied-palestinian-territory-concludes-israeli-authorities-and#:~:text=with%20international%20law.-,In%20relation%20to%20Israel's%20military%20operations%20and%20attacks%20in%20Gaza,extermination%2C%20intentionally%20directing%20attacks%20against |website=OHCHR |publisher=United Nations |access-date=21 June 2024}}}}</ref>

Israel has faced legal charges for its conduct in the war. At the [[International Court of Justice]], Israel was [[South Africa's genocide case against Israel|charged with committing genocide in Gaza]].<ref name="Powell 2024 g408">{{cite web |last=Powell |first=Anita |title=South Africa to Take Israel to Top UN Court on Genocide Claim in Gaza |website=[[Voice of America]] |date=January 5, 2024 |url=https://www.voanews.com/a/south-africa-to-take-israel-to-top-un-court-on-genocide-claim-in-gaza-/7427539.html |access-date=January 6, 2024 |archive-date=6 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240106225145/https://www.voanews.com/a/south-africa-to-take-israel-to-top-un-court-on-genocide-claim-in-gaza-/7427539.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1= |first1= |last2= |date=2024-06-06 |title=Which countries have joined South Africa's case against Israel at the ICJ? |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/6/6/which-countries-have-joined-south-africas-case-against-israel-at-the-icj |website=Al Jazeera |language=en |access-date=2024-06-14 |quote=South Africa brought its case against Israel in December, accusing it of committing genocide against Palestinians in Gaza. The death toll from Israel’s war there, which began in October, has surpassed 36,500, according to health officials in the besieged and bombarded territory.}}</ref> In May 2024, the [[International Criminal Court]] (ICC) issued arrest warrants against Israeli prime minister [[Benjamin Netanyahu]] and Israeli defence minister [[Yoav Gallant]] for war crimes and [[crimes against humanity]], including [[Gaza Strip famine|using starvation]] as a [[Starvation (crime)|weapon of war]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Bubola |first1=Emma |title=What to Know About the I.C.C. Prosecutor's Request for Warrants for Israeli and Hamas Leaders |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/05/20/world/middleeast/icc-arrest-warrants-israel-hamas.html |website=The New York Times |access-date=13 June 2024}}</ref>

While Israel has faced international condemnation for its alleged war crimes, it has also maintained continued [[United States support for Israel in the Gaza war|support from the United States]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Schneider |first1=Elena |title=Biden: What's happening in Gaza 'is not genocide' |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2024/05/20/biden-gaza-not-genocide-israel-00159020 |website=Politico |date=20 May 2024 |access-date=13 June 2024}}</ref> In October 2023, U.S. Secretary of State [[Antony Blinken]] indicated the [[Biden administration]] had no [[Red line (phrase)|red lines]] for Israeli actions where it would stop military support.<ref>{{cite web |title=White House says 'not drawing red lines for Israel' |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/white-house-says-not-drawing-red-lines-for-israel/ |website=The Times of Israel |access-date=28 October 2023 |archive-date=27 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231027225035/https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/white-house-says-not-drawing-red-lines-for-israel/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Liptak |first=Kevin |date=2024-05-30 |title=How Joe Biden's red line on Israel went from a 'parlor game' to a murky millstone |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2024/05/30/politics/joe-biden-red-line-israel/index.html |access-date=2025-03-03 |website=CNN |language=en}}</ref> As Israel's largest supplier of weapons, the U.S. has been accused of complicity in Israel's war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Kane |first1=Alex |title=Building the Case for US Complicity |url=https://jewishcurrents.org/us-complicity-israeli-war-crimes |website=Jewish Currents |access-date=13 June 2024}}</ref>

== Proportionality and distinction ==
[[File:Damage in Gaza Strip during the October 2023.jpg|thumb|Palestine Tower destroyed in Gaza, October 2023.]]

Israel's adherence to the principles of [[Distinction (law)|distinction]] and [[Proportionality (law)#International humanitarian law|proportionality]], as required by the [[Law of war|laws of war]], has been questioned.<ref name=":03">{{#invoke:cite|news|date=14 October 2023 |title=Is Israel acting within the laws of war? |newspaper=[[The Economist]] |url=https://www.economist.com/is-israel-acting-within-the-laws-of-war-in-gaza |access-date=2 January 2024}}</ref><ref name=":13">{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Erlanger |first=Steven |date=13 December 2023 |title=Under Rules of War, 'Proportionality' in Gaza Is Not About Evening the Score |work=[[The New York Times]] |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/13/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-proportionality-law-of-war.html |access-date=2 January 2024 |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> The former principle requires armies to distinguish between [[legitimate military target]]s and [[Protected persons|protected civilians]].<ref>{{Citation |last=Melzer |first=Nils |chapter=The Principle of Distinction Between Civilians and Combatants |date=2014-06-02 |title=The Oxford Handbook of International Law in Armed Conflict |pages=296–331 |editor-last=Clapham |editor-first=Andrew |chapter-url=https://academic.oup.com/edited-volume/43487/chapter/363759932 |access-date=2025-03-03 |edition=1 |publisher=Oxford University Press |language=en |doi=10.1093/law/9780199559695.003.0012 |isbn=978-0-19-955969-5 |editor2-last=Gaeta |editor2-first=Paola|chapter-url-access=subscription }}</ref> The latter principle requires that when attacking a legitimate military target the expected harm caused to civilians or civilian objects must be proportionate and not excessive (disproportionate) in relation to the military advantage anticipated.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Goldman |first=Robert |date=2023-11-09 |title=What is the rule of proportionality, and is it being observed in the Israeli siege of Gaza? |url=https://theconversation.com/what-is-the-rule-of-proportionality-and-is-it-being-observed-in-the-israeli-siege-of-gaza-217321 |access-date=2025-03-03 |website=The Conversation |language=en-US}}</ref>

[[Human Rights Watch]] has stated that the overall civilian death toll, and Israel's use of powerful weapons in Gaza's densely populated neighbourhoods, raised "serious questions" about the legality of Israel's conduct.<ref name=":13" /> Human Rights Watch further argued that a higher proportion of casualties among women and children is indicative of a lack of proportionality, demonstrating what they describe as "a disregard toward Palestinian lives".<ref name=":13" /> [[Amnesty International]] accused Israel of war crimes. In a report they published they analyzed five incidents between 7 and 12 October where the Israeli Defence Forces (IDF) targeted residential areas in Gaza. It found that in several cases the IDF struck targets with no evidence of military activity and that these attacks were "indiscriminate" in nature. Anonymous IDF officials cited in a report by ''[[+972 Magazine]]'' indicated a "loosening of constraints" in the [[rules of engagement]], and that in numerous cases the IDF struck targets despite no evidence of military activity. The report claims that the rationale behind such attacks was "to harm Palestinian civil society" and, according to one source cited by the report, to "lead civilians to put pressure on Hamas".<ref name="972yuval" />

Experts cited by ''[[The Washington Post]]'' argue that certain Israeli airstrikes show that Israel has a tolerance for civilian casualties "orders of magnitude greater" than that of the [[Operation Inherent Resolve|US in its war against ISIS]].<ref>{{cite news |title=As Gaza death toll soars, secrecy shrouds Israel's targeting process |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/11/05/israel-strike-targets-gaza-civilians-hamas/ |newspaper=The Washington Post |access-date=17 February 2024 |archive-date=26 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231226140439/https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/11/05/israel-strike-targets-gaza-civilians-hamas/ |url-status=live}}</ref> United Nations (UN) officials and human rights groups have argued that Israel has not done enough to protect civilians.<ref name=":13" /> In March 2024, the UN said that more children were killed in Gaza in four months than in four years of all the wars around the world combined.<ref name="Nataliya">{{cite web |first=Nataliya |last=Vasilyeva |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2024/03/13/children-killed-gaza-united-nations-wars-worldwide/ |title=More children killed in Gaza in four months than in four years of worldwide wars, says UN |work=The Telegraph |date=13 March 2024 |access-date=17 March 2024 |archive-date=13 March 2024 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20240313165714/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2024/03/13/children-killed-gaza-united-nations-wars-worldwide/ |url-status=live}}</ref> [[Philippe Lazzarini]], head of the UN's agency for Palestinian refugees, declared: "This war is a war on children".<ref name="Nataliya" />

[[File:Damage in Gaza Strip during the October 2023 - 23.jpg|thumb|Three men carry a dead woman to the [[Indonesia Hospital]] in [[Jabalia refugee camp]], October 2023.]]

Emanuela-Chiara Gillard, an associate fellow at [[Chatham House]], argued that, given the size and nature of the [[October 7 attacks]], Israel has the [[Right of self-defense|right of self-defence]] that could include its stated military aim of destroying Hamas. She added that Hamas has threatened to repeat its assault and eradicate the state of Israel.<ref name=":13" /> According to ''[[The Economist]]'', the [[Law of war|law of armed conflict]] and [[international humanitarian law]] grant Israel flexibility when it comes to taking military action against Hamas, but in its view, Israel's "definition of military targets is being stretched to breaking-point".<ref name=":03" />

Amichai Cohen, an Israeli lawyer, alleges that Israel does not deliberately target civilians but that Hamas's tactics make it hard to take action without affecting civilians.<ref name=":03" /> Jill Goldenziel, an American law professor, argued that if Israel conducted every strike legally and with utmost precision, civilian casualties in war would still remain. She stated that the goal of a proportionality analysis is to decide whether attacks are excessive.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Goldenziel |first=Jill |title=Proportionality Doesn't Mean What You Think It Means In Gaza |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/jillgoldenziel/2023/10/31/proportionality-doesnt-mean-what-you-think-it-means-in-gaza/ |access-date=2 January 2024 |website=[[Forbes]]}}</ref> Israeli security officials state that their proportionality criteria in this conflict are unchanged and that they receive legal advice in relation to strikes.<ref name=":13" /> Other Israeli officials, speaking anonymously, acknowledged that Israel has struck "private residences and public structures, like the Gaza Parliament and the [[Islamic University of Gaza|Islamic University]]", which would not previously have been considered valuable enough to justify the risk to civilian life.<ref name=":13" />

In April 2024, [[Human Rights Watch]] found that Israel violated international law by [[Engineer's Building strike and massacre|launching an airstrike on an apartment building]] in Gaza, killing 106 people, including 54 children, as there were no viable military targets in the area.<ref name="HRW040424"/>

In June 2024, the [[Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights|UN Human Rights Office]] described possible violations of the rules of proportionality and distinction during the [[Nuseirat refugee camp massacre]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Keaten |first1=Jamey |title=UN says Israeli forces and Palestinian armed groups may have committed war crimes in a deadly raid |url=https://apnews.com/article/israel-palestinians-hamas-gaza-un-nuseirat-raid-40a3e17012915c409e8a5d50475dd122?taid=66681b2467dd9a0001d16ef7&utm_campaign=TrueAnthem&utm_medium=AP&utm_source=Twitter |website=Associated Press |date=11 June 2024 |access-date=17 June 2024}}</ref> Later the same month, the UN Human Rights Office released a report on six Israeli attacks in which the IDF may have "systematically violated the principles of distinction, proportionality, and precautions in attack".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Tétrault-Farber |first1=Gabrielle |last2=Farge |first2=Emma |title=Israel may have violated laws of war in Gaza, UN rights office says |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israel-may-have-violated-laws-war-gaza-campaign-un-rights-office-says-2024-06-19/ |website=Reuters |access-date=20 June 2024}}</ref> Following the [[Al-Tabaeen school attack]], Tariq Kenney-Shawa, a policy fellow at [[Al-Shabaka, The Palestinian Policy Network|Al-Shabaka]] suggested the attack violated the laws of proportionality.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Salhani |first1=Justin |title=Israel, civilian deaths and the question of proportionality |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/8/12/israel-civilian-deaths-and-the-question-of-proportionality |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=24 August 2024}}</ref> In response to an Israeli social media campaign that stated "there are no innocent civilians" in Gaza, Mark Kersten, a professor at [[University of the Fraser Valley]], stated, "It is exactly what [[Atrocity crime|atrocity]] perpetrators say".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Ingram |first1=David |title=Israeli government sparks outcry with X videos saying 'there are no innocent civilians' in Gaza |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/social-media/israel-posts-video-saying-are-no-innocent-civilians-gaza-rcna157111 |website=NBC News |date=14 June 2024 |access-date=27 June 2024}}</ref> In June 2024, a [[Independent International Commission of Inquiry on the Occupied Palestinian Territory|UN Commission of Inquiry]] found the scale of Israel's killing of Palestinians constituted a [[Crimes against humanity|crime against humanity]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Farge |first1=Emma |title='Immense' scale of Gaza killings amount to crime against humanity, UN inquiry says |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/immense-scale-gaza-killings-amount-crime-against-humanity-un-inquiry-says-2024-06-12/ |website=Reuters |access-date=4 July 2024}}</ref>

By August 2024, data from Gaza indicated the war was one of the deadliest of the twenty-first century.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Hasson |first1=Nir |title=The Numbers Show: Gaza War Is One of the Bloodiest in the 21st Century |url=https://www.haaretz.com/middle-east-news/palestinians/2024-08-14/ty-article-magazine/.premium/the-death-toll-in-gaza-is-bad-even-compared-to-the-wars-in-ukraine-iraq-and-myanmar/00000191-50c6-d6a2-a7dd-d1decf340000 |website=Haaretz |access-date=18 August 2024}}</ref> [[Pope Francis]] suggested Israel's attacks on Lebanon and Gaza were disproportionate.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Winfield |first1=Nicole |title=Pope Francis suggests Israel's actions in Gaza and Lebanon are disproportionate and immoral |url=https://apnews.com/article/pope-israel-lebanon-hezbollah-72b592696627d1a671e7419e98e354b6?taid=66f9a034589661000183462a&utm_campaign=TrueAnthem&utm_medium=AP&utm_source=Twitter |website=Associated Press |date=29 September 2024 |access-date=6 October 2024}}</ref>

== Indiscriminate attacks ==
{{main|Bombing of the Gaza Strip|Attacks on religious sites during the Israeli invasion of Gaza}}

{{further|Attacks on health facilities during the Gaza war|Israeli airstrikes on municipal services in the Gaza Strip}}
{{see also|Tel al-Sultan massacre}} 
[[File:An aerial view showing destruction in Rafah after Israeli forces withdrawal and as the ceasefire took hold, Gaza Strip.jpg|thumb|Aerial view showing the destruction of [[Rafah]] in January 2025]]

In the first two days of the war, the [[Israeli Air Force]] attacked 1,500 targets in Gaza. [[Ynet]] reported that Netanyahu then demanded to know why they hadn't hit 5,000, saying "I'm not interested in targets ... Take down houses, bomb with everything you have."<ref>{{Cite news |last=ברנע |first=נחום |date=2025-03-20 |title=המלחמות של הרצי הלוי |url=https://www.ynet.co.il/yedioth/article/yokra14303894 |access-date=2025-03-23 |work=Ynet |language=he}}</ref> In the first week of the war, the Israeli Defense Forces (IDF) carried out 6,000 airstrikes across Gaza, killing over 3,300 civilians and injuring over 12,000 people.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Abdel-Baqui |first1=Omar |title=Israeli Air Force Says It Has Dropped 6,000 Bombs on Gaza |url=https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/israel-hamas-war-gaza-strip/card/israeli-air-force-says-it-has-dropped-6-000-bombs-on-gaza-QK1aSnupiGqytMVO86PU |newspaper=WSJ |access-date=22 October 2023 |archive-date=19 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231019112444/https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/israel-hamas-war-gaza-strip/card/israeli-air-force-says-it-has-dropped-6-000-bombs-on-gaza-QK1aSnupiGqytMVO86PU |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last1=Ott|first1=Haley|first2=Tucker|last2=Reals|first3=Kerry|last3=Breen|title=Israel-Hamas war: More airstrikes on Gaza today as aid remains stuck in Egypt; Israeli troops told to "be ready" to invade|url=https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/israel-hamas-war-palestinians-biden-speech-after-gaza-hospital-blast/|access-date=20 October 2023|agency=[[CBS News]]|date=19 October 2023|archive-date=19 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231019235338/https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/israel-hamas-war-palestinians-biden-speech-after-gaza-hospital-blast/|url-status=live}}</ref> The strikes hit specifically protected locations, including hospitals, markets, refugee camps, mosques, educational facilities, and entire neighbourhoods.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Baker|first1=Elise|title=Hamas's actions are war crimes. Israel should not respond with further war crimes.|url=https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/hamas-israel-war-crimes/|access-date=19 October 2023|work=[[The Guardian]]|date=16 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022011548/https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/hamas-israel-war-crimes/|url-status=live}}</ref> A group of [[UN special rapporteur]]s asserted that Israel's airstrikes are indiscriminate and amount to [[collective punishment]]. They stated that these airstrikes are "absolutely prohibited under international law and amounts to a war crime".<ref name="UN experts">{{cite news|title=UN experts say Israel's strikes on Gaza amount to 'collective punishment'|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/un-experts-say-israels-strikes-gaza-amount-collective-punishment-2023-10-12/|work=[[Reuters]]|access-date=13 October 2023|archive-date=12 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231012232721/https://www.reuters.com/world/un-experts-say-israels-strikes-gaza-amount-collective-punishment-2023-10-12/|url-status=live}}</ref>

During two airstrikes on 10 and 22 October 2023, the IDF used [[Joint Direct Attack Munitions]] in attacks described by Amnesty International as ''"either direct attacks on civilians"'' or ''"indiscriminate attacks".''<ref>{{cite web |title=US-made munitions killed 43 civilians in two documented Israeli air strikes in Gaza – new investigation |url=https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/israelopt-us-made-munitions-killed-43-civilians-two-documented-israeli-air-strikes-gaza-new-investigation#:~:text=US%2Dmade%20Joint%20Direct%20Attack,new%20investigation%20into%20those%20strikes. |website=ReliefWeb |date=6 December 2023 |publisher=Amnesty International |access-date=6 December 2023 |archive-date=24 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324114804/https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/israelopt-us-made-munitions-killed-43-civilians-two-documented-israeli-air-strikes-gaza-new-investigation-enar#:~:text=US%2Dmade%20Joint%20Direct%20Attack,new%20investigation%20into%20those%20strikes. |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Hammer |first1=Matthias |title=U.S. Military Equipment Traced to Possible War Crimes in Gaza, Report Finds |url=https://time.com/6342821/israel-airstrike-us-military-war-crimes/ |website=Time Magazine |date=5 December 2023 |access-date=6 December 2023 |archive-date=12 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231212141927/https://time.com/6342821/israel-airstrike-us-military-war-crimes/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On 24 October, UN Secretary-General [[António Guterres]] called for an immediate [[ceasefire]], after stating Israel had committed "clear violations" of international humanitarian law.<ref>{{cite web |title='Clear violations' of international law in Gaza: UN chief |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/10/23/israel-hamas-war-live-hundreds-killed-israeli-strikes-gaza?update=2434460 |website=[[Al Jazeera]] |access-date=24 October 2023 |archive-date=24 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231024213223/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/10/23/israel-hamas-war-live-hundreds-killed-israeli-strikes-gaza?update=2434460 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 13 November 2023, Israel shelled the Gaza Reconstruction Committee, leading three Arab states to condemn the attack, with [[Jordan]] calling it "a heinous war crime to add to Israel's criminal record."<ref>{{cite web |title=Oman, Saudi Arabia and Jordan condemn Israeli shelling of Qatari organisation in Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/13/israel-hamas-war-live-gazas-two-largest-hospitals-shut-amid-nonstop-raids?update=2483900 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=14 November 2023 |archive-date=24 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324114637/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/13/israel-hamas-war-live-gazas-two-largest-hospitals-shut-amid-nonstop-raids?update=2483900 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 12 January 2024, the spokesperson for the [[Office of the U.N. High Commissioner for Human Rights]] stated Israel's attacks were failing to account for distinction, proportionality and precautions, thus leaving Israel exposed to liability for war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Tétrault-Farber |first1=Gabrielle |title=UN deplores Israel's 'systematic' refusal to grant access to north Gaza |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/un-deplores-israels-systematic-refusal-grant-access-north-gaza-2024-01-12/#:~:text=%22We%27ve%20repeatedly%20highlighted%20Israel%27s,for%20Human%20Rights%20(OHCHR). |website=Reuters |access-date=13 January 2024}}</ref>

In February 2024, the IDF bombed and destroyed the Belgium government's Gaza development office.<ref>{{cite web |title=Belgium Summons Israeli Ambassador After Agency Hit In Gaza |url=https://www.barrons.com/news/belgium-summons-israeli-ambassador-after-agency-hit-in-gaza-72785245 |website=Barron's |publisher=Agence France Presse |access-date=4 February 2024 |archive-date=4 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240204012359/https://www.barrons.com/news/belgium-summons-israeli-ambassador-after-agency-hit-in-gaza-72785245 |url-status=live }}</ref> In response, Belgium summoned the Israeli ambassador and condemned the "destruction of civilian infrastructure" as a violation of international law.<ref>{{cite web |title=Belgium summons Israeli ambassador and strongly condemns bombing of Belgian development agency Enabel |url=https://diplomatie.belgium.be/en/news/belgium-summons-israeli-ambassador-and-strongly-condemns-bombing-belgian-development-agency-enabel |website=Kingdom of Belgium |date=2 February 2024 |access-date=4 February 2024 |archive-date=4 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240204012400/https://diplomatie.belgium.be/en/news/belgium-summons-israeli-ambassador-and-strongly-condemns-bombing-belgian-development-agency-enabel |url-status=live }}</ref>{{efn|Two weeks after the bombing, the Belgian Minister of Development Cooperation [[Caroline Gennez]] stated Israel had still not responded to a request for an investigation.<ref>{{cite web |title=Belgium receives no clarification from Israel on Gaza building bombing |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/12/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israel-planning-rafah-assault-as-talks-continue?update=2703330 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=14 February 2024 |archive-date=14 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240214025432/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/12/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israel-planning-rafah-assault-as-talks-continue?update=2703330 |url-status=live }}</ref>}} On 6 February, the UN stated an Israeli assault on [[Rafah]] could lead to war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |title=War crimes fears over Israeli ground invasion of Rafah |url=https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/02/1146242 |website=UN News |date=6 February 2024 |publisher=United Nations |access-date=7 February 2024 |archive-date=7 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240207054343/https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/02/1146242 |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 22 March 2024, Al Jazeera released a video retrieved from an Israeli drone showing four unarmed Palestinians in [[Khan Yunis|Khan Younis]] who were killed by Israeli air attacks. Two were killed instantly, and the others were killed while trying to stumble and crawl away.<ref name="Al Jazeera 2024 f955">{{cite web | title=Gaza drone video shows killing of Palestinians in Israeli air attack | website=Al Jazeera | date=22 March 2024 | url=https://www.aljazeera.com/program/newsfeed/2024/3/22/gaza-drone-video-shows-killing-of-palestinians-in-israeli-air-attack | access-date=23 March 2024 | archive-date=22 March 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240322170319/https://www.aljazeera.com/program/newsfeed/2024/3/22/gaza-drone-video-shows-killing-of-palestinians-in-israeli-air-attack | url-status=live }}</ref> Al-Jazeera reported that "it is clear from the pictures that these Palestinians were unarmed and posed no threat to anything or anyone".<ref name="The Jerusalem Post 2024 p344">{{cite web | title=IDF probes video of 'unarmed' Palestinians gunned down by drone in Gaza | website=The Jerusalem Post | date=22 March 2024 | url=https://www.jpost.com/israel-hamas-war/article-793273 | access-date=23 March 2024 | archive-date=22 March 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240322184042/https://www.jpost.com/israel-hamas-war/article-793273 | url-status=live }}</ref> This footage was described by the UN's special rapporteur [[Francesca Albanese]] as a part of the "colossal amount of evidence" of war crimes committed in Gaza by Israel. According to the IDF, they had encountered militants in civilian clothes retrieving previously hidden weapons in that area.<ref name="The Telegraph 2024 a516">{{cite web | title=Israel to investigate drone attack on unarmed Palestinians | website=The Telegraph | date=22 March 2024 | url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2024/03/22/israel-drone-attack-palestine-gaza/ | access-date=24 March 2024 | archive-date=24 May 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240524132805/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2024/03/22/israel-drone-attack-palestine-gaza/ | url-status=live }}</ref>

Amnesty International called Israel's indiscriminate attacks illegal and a violation of international law. Secretary General of Amnesty International [[Agnès Callamard]] said the 16-year-old "illegal [[Blockade of the Gaza Strip|blockade]] has made Gaza the world's biggest open-air prison", and the international community must now act to avert it from becoming a giant cemetery.<ref>{{cite web |title=Damning evidence of war crimes as Israeli attacks wipe out entire families in Gaza |url=https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2023/10/damning-evidence-of-war-crimes-as-israeli-attacks-wipe-out-entire-families-in-gaza/ |website=Amnesty International |date=20 October 2023 |access-date=7 February 2024 |archive-date=20 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231020141613/https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2023/10/damning-evidence-of-war-crimes-as-israeli-attacks-wipe-out-entire-families-in-gaza/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Human Rights Watch reported that Israel has completely shut down communications and put lives at risk in Gaza by carrying out relentless airstrikes and damage to the main communications infrastructure, electricity cuts, fuel blockades, and deliberate shutdowns through technical measures. [[Deborah Brown]], senior technology researcher at Human Rights Watch, said a deliberate shutdown, or restriction of Internet access, is a human rights violation and can be deadly during a crisis. A complete disruption of communications, such as that experienced in Gaza, can provide cover for crimes and impunity, while further undermining humanitarian efforts and putting lives at risk.<ref>{{cite web |title=Gaza: Communications Blackout Imminent Due to Fuel Shortage |url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/11/15/gaza-communications-blackout-imminent-due-fuel-shortage#:~:text=(Jerusalem)%20%E2%80%93%20The%20Israeli%20government's,Human%20Rights%20Watch%20said%20today. |website=Human Rights Watch |date=18 December 2023 |access-date=7 February 2024 |archive-date=7 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240207091621/https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/11/15/gaza-communications-blackout-imminent-due-fuel-shortage#:~:text=(Jerusalem)%20%E2%80%93%20The%20Israeli%20government's,Human%20Rights%20Watch%20said%20today. |url-status=live }}</ref>

Following reports about Israel's use of [[AI-assisted targeting in the Gaza Strip|automated systems for target selection]], experts in international humanitarian law stated they were alarmed by accounts that the IDF authorized killing up to 20 uninvolved civilians for getting a single militant, even if they were low-ranking or had low military importance.<ref>{{cite news |last1=McKernan |first1=Bethan |last2=Davies |first2=Harry |title='The machine did it coldly': Israel used AI to identify 37,000 Hamas targets |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/03/israel-gaza-ai-database-hamas-airstrikes |website=The Guardian |date=3 April 2024 |access-date=12 April 2024 |archive-date=24 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240524132931/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/03/israel-gaza-ai-database-hamas-airstrikes |url-status=live }}</ref> In May 2024, Amnesty International called for war crimes investigations into three Israeli airstrikes that had killed 44 civilians.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israeli air strikes that killed 44 civilians further evidence of war crimes – new investigation |url=https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2024/05/israel-opt-israeli-air-strikes-that-killed-44-civilians-further-evidence-of-war-crimes-new-investigation/ |website=Amnesty International |date=26 May 2024 |access-date=5 June 2024}}</ref> The same month, following the [[May 2024 Al-Mawasi refugee camp attack|Al-Mawasi refugee camp attack]], Finnish Foreign Minister [[Elina Valtonen]] stated that the orders of the [[International Court of Justice]] (ICJ) and international humanitarian law must be respected.<ref>{{cite web |title=Finland 'devastated' by deaths from Israel's attack on Rafah tent camp |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/5/28/israels-war-on-gaza-live-intense-israeli-artillery-shelling-across-rafah?update=2932450 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=5 June 2024}}</ref> In June 2024, [[UNRWA]] chief [[Philippe Lazzarini]] termed the destruction of UNRWA's Gaza headquarters as "blatant disregard of international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite web |title=Unrwa head says agency's headquarters in Gaza was 'turned into a battlefield' |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jul/15/israel-gaza-war-live-khan-younis-hamas-mohammed-deif?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66951f3c8f08ee3616ac6bec#block-66951f3c8f08ee3616ac6bec |website=The Guardian | date=15 July 2024 |access-date=25 July 2024 | last1=Lowe | first1=Yohannes }}</ref> In June 2024, [[Doctors Without Borders]] suggested Israel was violating international humanitarian law, stating, "We can no longer accept the statement that Israel is taking 'all precautions'".<ref>{{cite web |title=Latest massacres in Gaza illustrate the complete dehumanisation of Palestinians |url=https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/latest-massacres-gaza-illustrate-complete-dehumanisation-palestinians-enar |website=ReliefWeb |date=11 June 2024 |publisher=Doctors Without Borders |access-date=21 June 2024}}</ref> The [[European Union]] warned Israel in August 2024 that "targeting critical life-saving infrastructure constitutes a war crime".<ref>{{cite web |title=Gaza: Statement by the High Representative on the destruction of critical civilian infrastructure and worsening humanitarian situation |url=https://www.eeas.europa.eu/eeas/gazastatement-high-representative-destruction-critical-civilian-infrastructure-and-worsening_en |website=The Diplomatic Service of the European Union |publisher=European Union |access-date=17 August 2024}}</ref> The IDF stated it would investigate whether there was a breach of international law following an army commanders' order to destroy a water reservoir in Rafah.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Kubovich |first1=Yaniv |title=Israeli Army Commanders Gave Order to Blow Up Rafah Reservoir. IDF Suspects Breach of Int'l Law |url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2024-07-29/ty-article/.premium/idf-commanders-gave-order-to-blow-up-rafah-reservoir-army-suspects-breach-of-intl-law/00000190-fd90-d5ef-a5fe-ff9ec3ea0000 |website=Haaretz |access-date=17 August 2024}}</ref>{{efn|Mark Zeitoun, the director of [[Geneva Water Hub]], stated the destruction of the Canada water reservoir was "certainly a breach of international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Stockwell |first1=Billy |last2=Haq |first2=Sana Noor |title=Children are drinking from puddles and wading through sewage pools, as Israel pummels water systems in Gaza |url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/08/23/middleeast/israel-gaza-water-shortages-heatwave-crisis-intl/index.html |website=CNN |date=23 August 2024 |access-date=12 September 2024}}</ref>}}

===Refugee camps===
{{main|Attacks on refugee camps in the Gaza war}}
{{see also|Nuseirat refugee camp massacre}}
[[File:חורבות בית לאהיא חרבות ברזל.jpg|thumb|Damaged buildings in the Gaza Strip on 12 November 2023]]

On 9 October 2023, the IDF carried out a mass-casualty airstrike on the [[Jabalia camp market airstrike|Jabalia refugee camp market]].<ref name=":0" /> The attack resulted in the deaths of over sixty civilians and extensive damage to the market.<ref name=":0">{{Cite news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/09/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-market-air-strike-jabaliya.html|title=Israeli Airstrike Hits Marketplace in Gazan Refugee Camp, Killing Dozens|first1=Raja|last1=Abdulrahim|first2=Ameera|last2=Harouda|date=9 October 2023|work=[[The New York Times]] |access-date=9 October 2023 |archive-date=9 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231009155140/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/09/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-market-air-strike-jabaliya.html |url-status=live}}</ref> As a result of Israeli airstrikes in other areas, displaced individuals sought refuge in the camp, causing the market to be densely populated at the time of the strike.<ref>{{Cite news|last1=Abdulrahim|first1=Raja|last2=Harouda|first2=Ameera|date=9 October 2023|title=Israeli Airstrike Hits Marketplace in Gazan Refugee Camp, Killing Dozens|language=en-US|work=[[The New York Times]]|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/09/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-market-air-strike-jabaliya.html |access-date=9 October 2023|issn=0362-4331 |archive-date=9 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231009145027/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/09/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-market-air-strike-jabaliya.html |url-status=live}}</ref> An airstrike on 31 October 2023 that killed 106 civilians near the [[Nuseirat rescue and massacre|Nuseirat refugee camp]] was deemed an apparent war crime by Human Rights Watch.<ref name="HRW040424">{{cite web |title=Gaza: Israeli Strike Killing 106 Civilians an Apparent War Crime |url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2024/04/04/gaza-israeli-strike-killing-106-civilians-apparent-war-crime |website=Human Rights Watch |date=4 April 2024 |access-date=16 April 2024 |archive-date=13 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240513053930/https://www.hrw.org/news/2024/04/04/gaza-israeli-strike-killing-106-civilians-apparent-war-crime |url-status=live }}</ref> On 1 November, following two airstrikes on the [[Jabalia refugee camp airstrikes|Jabalia refugee camp]], the United Nations Human Rights Office stated, "We have serious concerns that these are disproportionate attacks that could amount to war crimes."<ref>{{cite web |title=UN Human Rights office says Jabalia strikes 'could amount to war crimes' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/1/israel-hamas-war-live-anger-grows-over-israeli-attack-on-gaza-refugee-camp?update=2455756 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=1 November 2023 |archive-date=24 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324114757/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/1/israel-hamas-war-live-anger-grows-over-israeli-attack-on-gaza-refugee-camp?update=2455756 |url-status=live }}</ref>

On the same day, the IDF carried out an airstrike on the densely populated [[Al-Shati refugee camp]].<ref>{{Cite news|last1=Abdulrahim|first1=Raja|last2=Harouda|first2=Ameera|date=9 October 2023|title=Israeli Airstrikes Hit Marketplace and Mosques in Gaza, Killing Dozens|language=en-US|work=[[The New York Times]]|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/09/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-market-air-strike-jabaliya.html|access-date=11 October 2023|issn=0362-4331|archive-date=9 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231009155140/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/09/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-market-air-strike-jabaliya.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Palestinian media reported that this strike resulted in numerous civilian casualties and the destruction of four mosques, including the al-Gharbi mosque, Yassin mosque, and al-Sousi mosque, all of which were confirmed destroyed by satellite footage.<ref>{{Cite news|date=7 October 2023|title=Maps: Tracking the Attacks in Israel and Gaza|language=en|url=https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/10/07/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-maps.html|access-date=11 October 2023|work=[[The New York Times]]|archive-date=10 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231010211135/https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/10/07/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-maps.html|url-status=live}}</ref> The airstrikes in the Al-Shati camp were described as a ''"massacre against an entire neighborhood"'' by the [[Ministry of Health (Palestine)|Ministry of Health]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://english.wafa.ps/Pages/Details/138060|title=Masscre of Shati refugee camp|date=9 October 2023|work=wafa English|access-date=21 October 2023|archive-date=9 November 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231109195512/https://english.wafa.ps/Pages/Details/138060|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|last=Dahman|first=Ibrahim|date=8 October 2023|title='Nowhere to go': Ordinary Palestinians live in fear as Israel retaliates against Hamas|url=https://www.cnn.com/2023/10/08/middleeast/palestine-israel-hamas-gaza-conflict-intl/index.html|access-date=11 October 2023|work=[[CNN]]|language=en|archive-date=10 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231010233124/https://www.cnn.com/2023/10/08/middleeast/palestine-israel-hamas-gaza-conflict-intl/index.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

On 24 December 2023, 68 people were killed in an [[Israeli attacks on Al-Maghazi refugee camp|airstrike on the Al-Maghazi refugee camp]]. According to ''Al Jazeera'', the vast majority of victims were civilians. They also noted that the camp was one of the areas the IDF had previously told Gazans to evacuate to. Hamas called the attack a "massacre" and a "war crime".<ref>{{cite web |title='Massacre' as Israel steps up Gaza bombardment for Christmas |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/12/25/israeli-forces-massacre-at-least-70-people-in-gazas-maghazi-refugee-camp |website=aljazeera.com |publisher=Al Jazeera |access-date=29 December 2023 |archive-date=28 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231228233945/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/12/25/israeli-forces-massacre-at-least-70-people-in-gazas-maghazi-refugee-camp |url-status=live }}</ref> Israel later determined that incorrect munitions were used in the attack and expressed regret that non-combatants were harmed.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Improper munition said cause of high death toll in strike on Gaza's Maghazi |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/improper-munition-said-cause-of-high-death-toll-in-strike-on-gazas-maghazi/ |website=[[The Times of Israel]] |access-date=29 December 2023 |archive-date=29 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231229014443/https://www.timesofisrael.com/improper-munition-said-cause-of-high-death-toll-in-strike-on-gazas-maghazi/ |url-status=live  |issn=0040-7909}}</ref>

===Schools and shelters===
{{further|Attacks on schools during the Israeli invasion of Gaza}}
{{see also|Al-Sardi school attack|Al-Tabaeen school attack}}

On 17 October 2023, an Israeli airstrike hit a [[UNRWA]] school sheltering 4,000 refugees in the [[Maghazi (camp)|Al-Maghazi refugee camp]], killing six and injuring dozens. [[Philippe Lazzarini]], the UNRWA Commissioner-General, called it "outrageous" and said that it showed "a flagrant disregard for the lives of civilians".<ref>{{cite web|title=Gaza: UNRWA School Sheltering Displaced Families is Hit|url=https://www.unrwa.org/newsroom/official-statements/gaza-unrwa-school-sheltering-displaced-families-hit|website=unrwa.org|date=17 October 2023|access-date=19 October 2023|archive-date=18 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231018043659/https://www.unrwa.org/newsroom/official-statements/gaza-unrwa-school-sheltering-displaced-families-hit|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|title=At least 6 people killed in Israeli air strike on UNRWA school in Gaza|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/least-6-people-killed-israeli-air-strike-unrwa-school-gaza-2023-10-17/|access-date=19 October 2023|work=[[Reuters]]|date=17 October 2023|archive-date=17 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231017164355/https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/least-6-people-killed-israeli-air-strike-unrwa-school-gaza-2023-10-17/|url-status=live}}</ref> The UN accused Israel of lethally bombing three of its shelters on 2 November 2023.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Regan |first1=Helen |title=Airstrikes blast UN shelters, official says, as Israel announces complete encirclement of Gaza city |url=https://www.cnn.com/2023/11/02/middleeast/israel-gaza-hamas-war-jabalya-camp-strike-intl-hnk/index.html |website=CNN |date=2 November 2023 |access-date=25 January 2024 |archive-date=2 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231102070827/https://www.cnn.com/2023/11/02/middleeast/israel-gaza-hamas-war-jabalya-camp-strike-intl-hnk/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref> On 27 December 2023, the UN stated Israel had killed 142 UN employees in Gaza thus far.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Cornish |first1=Chloe |title=Israel-UN relations plunge to new low as Gaza war rages |url=https://www.ft.com/content/c5104a4d-3468-4cda-9e00-0cbb6fa5520c?shareType=nongift |website=Financial Times |date=27 December 2023 |access-date=27 December 2023 |archive-date=27 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231227203050/https://www.ft.com/content/c5104a4d-3468-4cda-9e00-0cbb6fa5520c?shareType=nongift |url-status=live }}</ref> On 12 January 2024, the UN Secretary-General for Human Rights stated that at least 319 internally displaced persons were killed and 1,135 injured in UNRWA shelters.<ref name="auto">{{cite web |title=ASG Brands Kehris briefs Security Council on situation in Israel and the Occupied Palestinian Territory |url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/statements-and-speeches/2024/01/asg-brands-kehris-briefs-security-council-on-situation-israel-occupied-palestinian-territory |website=United Nations |publisher=OHCHR |access-date=13 January 2024 |archive-date=13 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240113003219/https://www.ohchr.org/en/statements-and-speeches/2024/01/asg-brands-kehris-briefs-security-council-on-situation-israel-occupied-palestinian-territory |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 24 January 2024, the UN accused Israel of firing two tank shells into a refugee facility in Khan Younis, killing nine people and wounding 75.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Yazbek |first1=Hiba |title=U.N. Shelter in Besieged Gaza City Is Struck, and at Least 9 Die |work=The New York Times |date=25 January 2024 |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/24/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-shelter-strike.html |access-date=25 January 2024 |archive-date=25 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240125010522/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/24/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-shelter-strike.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=UN shelter reportedly hit as fighting escalates in southern Gaza |url=https://abcnews.go.com/International/live-updates/israel-gaza-hamas-war/un-shelter-reportedly-hit-as-fighting-escalates-in-southern-gaza-106633309?id=106553905 |website=ABC News |access-date=25 January 2024 |archive-date=25 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240125021810/https://abcnews.go.com/International/live-updates/israel-gaza-hamas-war/un-shelter-reportedly-hit-as-fighting-escalates-in-southern-gaza-106633309?id=106553905 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Nine killed in direct hit on UNRWA shelter in Gaza |url=https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/01/1145837 |website=UN News |date=24 January 2024 |publisher=United Nations |access-date=25 January 2024 |archive-date=25 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240125013117/https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/01/1145837 |url-status=live }}</ref> Israel denied bombing the facility.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Al-Mughrabi |first1=Nidal |title=Israel denies attack on UN refuge in Gaza that drew rebuke from Washington |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/plan-one-month-gaza-truce-makes-progress-israel-hits-khan-younis-2024-01-24/#:~:text=The%20agency%27s%20head%20Philippe%20Lazzarini,of%20war%2C%22%20Lazzarini%20said. |website=Reuters |access-date=25 January 2024}}</ref>{{efn|The following day, Thomas White, the affairs director of UNRWA, stated, "This is not an isolated incident. This is happening all across Khan Younis and has been a pattern in other parts of Gaza."<ref>{{cite web |title=UNRWA official: Israeli assurances 'not followed up' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/1/25/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israel-kills-9-in-un-shelter-sparking-outrage?update=2648979 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=26 January 2024 |archive-date=26 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240126022953/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/1/25/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israel-kills-9-in-un-shelter-sparking-outrage?update=2648979 |url-status=live }}</ref>}} Thomas White, a senior UN official in Gaza, called the attack part of "a consistent failure to uphold the fundamental principles of international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite web |title=Senior UN official in Gaza: civilians trapped amid intensified attacks in Khan Youni |url=https://www.ochaopt.org/content/senior-un-official-gaza-civilians-trapped-amid-intensified-attacks-khan-younis |website=UNOCHA |date=25 January 2024 |publisher=United Nations |access-date=26 January 2024 |archive-date=25 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240125205713/https://www.ochaopt.org/content/senior-un-official-gaza-civilians-trapped-amid-intensified-attacks-khan-younis |url-status=live }}</ref> The [[Palestinian Ministry of Education]] reported that 65 UN schools in Gaza had been damaged or destroyed, which the [[Save the Children]]'s director for Palestine called "beyond unconscionable".<ref>{{cite web |title=How Israel has destroyed Gaza's schools and universities |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/1/24/how-israel-has-destroyed-gazas-schools-and-universities |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=25 January 2024 |archive-date=6 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240206045355/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/1/24/how-israel-has-destroyed-gazas-schools-and-universities |url-status=live }}</ref>

In June 2024, the [[Minister of Foreign Affairs (Jordan)|Foreign Ministry of Jordan]] condemned the [[Al-Sardi school attack]], stating, "These actions and crimes… contradict all human and moral values and represent war crimes against the international community as a whole."<ref>{{cite web |title=Jordan: Israeli attack contradicts 'all human and moral values' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/6/6/israels-war-on-gaza-live-relentless-israeli-strikes-kill-102-palestinians?update=2956414 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=15 June 2024}}</ref> In response to the Al-Sardi school attack, UNRWA chief [[Philippe Lazzarini]] stated that attacking UN buildings showed a "blatant disregard of international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Shotter |first1=James |title=Dozens killed in Israeli strike on UN school in Gaza |url=https://www.ft.com/content/bb17ecbf-8f47-4168-940f-51b754598c88?shareType=nongift |website=Financial Times |date=6 June 2024 |access-date=16 June 2024}}</ref> Following the [[Al-Tabaeen school attack]] in August 2024, the foreign ministry of Jordan called it a "a flagrant violation of international law and of all humanitarian values," while the government of Turkey stated it was a "crime against humanity".<ref>{{cite web |title=Egypt: 'Deliberate Killing' of Gazans Shows Israel Lacks Political Will to End War |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240810113356/https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2024-08-10/ty-article/egypt-deliberate-killing-of-gazans-shows-israel-lacks-political-will-to-end-war/00000191-3b1a-dc30-aff3-7f1affb10000|archive-date=10 August 2024|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2024-08-10/ty-article/egypt-deliberate-killing-of-gazans-shows-israel-lacks-political-will-to-end-war/00000191-3b1a-dc30-aff3-7f1affb10000 |website=Haaretz |publisher=Reuters |access-date=10 September 2024 |author1=Haaretz }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Turkey Brands Gaza School Strike A 'New Crime Against Humanity' |url=https://www.barrons.com/news/turkey-brands-gaza-school-strike-a-new-crime-against-humanity-ministry-64f4f787 |website=Barron's |publisher=Agence France Presse |access-date=10 September 2024}}</ref> In September 2024, an Israeli airstrike [[September 2024 Al-Jawni School attack|killed six UN employees]] at a shelter for displaced people, leading UN secretary general Antonio Guterres to call it a "dramatic violation" of international humanitarian law.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Shotter |first1=James |title=Israeli air strikes kill 6 UN staff at Gaza school sheltering homeless |url=https://www.ft.com/content/6760d8ea-f11f-4681-b71a-2dac03a0db2b |website=Financial Times |date=12 September 2024 |access-date=15 September 2024|url-access=subscription}}</ref>

Analyses by [[CNN]], ''[[The New York Times]]'', and [[Sky News]] all found that Israel had bombed areas it had previously told civilians to evacuate to.<ref>{{cite web |last1=van der Merwe |first1=Ben |last2=Olive |first2=Michelle Inez |last3=Enokido-Lineham |first3=Simon |title=Israel said Gazans could flee to this neighbourhood - then it was hit |url=https://news.sky.com/story/israel-said-gazans-could-flee-to-this-neighbourhood-then-it-was-hit-13034936 |website=Sky News |access-date=22 December 2023 |archive-date=22 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231222002011/https://news.sky.com/story/israel-said-gazans-could-flee-to-this-neighbourhood-then-it-was-hit-13034936 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=":1" /><ref name=":2" /> ''The New York Times'' found that Israel had dropped 2,000-pound bombs in areas where civilians were ordered to evacuate to.<ref name=":1">{{cite news |last1=Stein |first1=Robin |last2=Willis |first2=Haley |last3=Jhaveri |first3=Ishaan |last4=Miller |first4=Danielle |last5=Byrd |first5=Aaron |last6=Reneau |first6=Natalie |title=Visual Evidence Shows Israel Dropped 2,000-Pound Bombs Where It Ordered Gaza's Civilians to Move for Safety |work=The New York Times |date=22 December 2023 |url=https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/100000009208814/israel-gaza-bomb-civilians.html?smid=url-share |access-date=22 December 2023 |archive-date=22 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231222184304/https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/100000009208814/israel-gaza-bomb-civilians.html?smid=url-share |url-status=live }}</ref> CNN stated it had verified at least three locations Israel bombed after telling civilians it was safe to go there.<ref name=":2">{{cite web |last1=Tacchi |first1=Jake |title=Israel struck some areas it directed civilians to in Gaza, CNN analysis shows |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2023/12/21/middleeast/israel-strikes-evacuation-zones-gaza-intl-cmd/index.html |website=CNN |date=21 December 2023 |access-date=22 December 2023 |archive-date=22 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231222001352/https://edition.cnn.com/2023/12/21/middleeast/israel-strikes-evacuation-zones-gaza-intl-cmd/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref> An [[NBC News]] investigation found Palestinians were killed in airstrikes in seven areas that the military had designated as safe zones.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.nbcnews.com/news/world/palestinians-killed-israeli-strikes-safe-zones-exclusive-nbc-report-rcna148008|title=NBC News investigation reveals Israel strikes on Gaza areas it said were safe|date=26 April 2024|website=NBC News|access-date=28 April 2024|archive-date=24 May 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240524132917/https://www.nbcnews.com/news/world/palestinians-killed-israeli-strikes-safe-zones-exclusive-nbc-report-rcna148008|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Places of worship===
{{main|Attacks on religious sites during the Israeli invasion of Gaza}}
{{further|Church of Saint Porphyrius airstrike}}
[[File:Damage in Gaza Strip during the October 2023 - 16.jpg|upright=1|thumb|A mosque destroyed by an Israeli airstrike, [[Khan Younis]], 8 October 2023]]
Under the [[Rome Statute]], it is a war crime to intentionally attack [[Place of worship|places of worship]] in non-international conflicts, as long as they are not "used by a party to a conflict for acts harmful to the enemy".<ref>{{cite web|title=Attacks against protected objects|url=https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/Documents/Countries/CF/Mapping2003-2015/Factsheet9-EN.pdf|website=UN OHCHR|access-date=14 October 2023|archive-date=14 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231014233030/https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/Documents/Countries/CF/Mapping2003-2015/Factsheet9-EN.pdf|url-status=live}}</ref> On 19 October, the Israeli Air Force damaged the [[Church of Saint Porphyrius airstrike|Church of Saint Porphyrius]] in an attack which targeted a nearby command-and-control center, according to the Israeli military.<ref name=theart>{{Cite web |last=Ditmars |first=Hadani |date=20 October 2023 |title=Historic Greek Orthodox church in Gaza hit by deadly missile strikes|url=https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2023/10/20/third-oldest-church-in-the-world-struck-by-missiles-in-gaza |access-date=22 October 2023 |website=The Art Newspaper - International art news and events |archive-date=23 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023193556/https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2023/10/20/third-oldest-church-in-the-world-struck-by-missiles-in-gaza |url-status=live }}</ref> Hundreds of [[Palestinian Christians|Christians]] and Muslims were sheltering in the church and the strike killed 16 people.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Al-Mughrabi|first1=Nidal|title=Hamas frees U.S. hostages Judith and Natalie Raanan held in Gaza|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/biden-seek-billions-military-aid-israel-invasion-gaza-nears-2023-10-20/|website=Reuters|date=20 October 2023|access-date=21 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022011549/https://www.reuters.com/world/biden-seek-billions-military-aid-israel-invasion-gaza-nears-2023-10-20/|url-status=live}}</ref> The [[Greek Orthodox Patriarchate of Jerusalem]] condemned it as "a war crime that cannot be ignored".<ref>{{cite web|title=The Patriarchate of Jerusalem condemns Israeli airstrikes targeting humanitarian institutions in Gaza|url=https://en.jerusalem-patriarchate.info/blog/2023/10/20/the-patriarchate-of-jerusalem-condemns-israeli-airstrikes-targeting-humanitarian-institutions-in-gaza/|website=Patriarchate of Jerusalem|date=20 October 2023|access-date=21 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022011550/https://en.jerusalem-patriarchate.info/blog/2023/10/20/the-patriarchate-of-jerusalem-condemns-israeli-airstrikes-targeting-humanitarian-institutions-in-gaza/|url-status=live}}</ref> Following an investigation, Amnesty International stated the church strike was indiscriminate and should be investigated as a war crime.<ref>{{cite web |title='Nowhere safe in Gaza': Unlawful Israeli strikes illustrate callous disregard for Palestinian lives |url=https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2023/11/israel-opt-nowhere-safe-in-gaza-unlawful-israeli-strikes-illustrate-callous-disregard-for-palestinian-lives/ |website=Amnesty International |date=20 November 2023 |access-date=20 November 2023 |archive-date=20 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231120105540/https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2023/11/israel-opt-nowhere-safe-in-gaza-unlawful-israeli-strikes-illustrate-callous-disregard-for-palestinian-lives/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 16 December 2023, the [[Latin Patriarchate of Jerusalem]] stated the Israeli army had [[Killing of Naheda and Samr Anton|killed two women]] sheltering at the [[Holy Family Church, Gaza|Holy Family Parish]], stating, "They were shot in cold blood inside the premises of the Parish, where there are no belligerents."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Berger |first1=Miriam |title=IDF kills two women taking shelter at Gaza church, Catholic authorities say |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/12/16/women-killed-at-holy-family-parish-gaza-israel/ |newspaper=The Washington Post |access-date=17 December 2023 |archive-date=17 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231217012816/https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/12/16/women-killed-at-holy-family-parish-gaza-israel/ |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Pope Francis]] described the Israeli attack on the church as [[terrorism]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Pullella |first1=Philip |title=Pope Francis deplores Israeli killings of civilians in Gaza church |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/pope-francis-deplores-israeli-killings-civilians-gaza-church-2023-12-17/ |website=Reuters |access-date=18 December 2023}}</ref>

===Residential areas===
An independent United Nations expert said that both Israel's widespread bombing of homes and civilian sites in Gaza and the indiscriminate firing of rockets by Hamas are "war crimes". Balakrishnan Rajagopal stated Israeli strikes had destroyed or damaged 45% of homes in the Palestinian territory, causing "enormous cost in human lives". The UN Special Rapporteur stated  targeting of residential areas is strictly prohibited under international law. He further stated that engaging in military actions with the knowledge that it will result in the deliberate destruction of civilian residences and infrastructure, leading to the uninhabitability of entire cities, constitutes a violation of international law.<ref>{{Cite news|title= 'War crimes' in Gaza and Israel, Palestinian death toll climbs, Blinken opposes Israeli reoccupation|url= https://www.euronews.com/2023/11/08/israeli-troops-in-heart-of-gaza-city-us-warns-against-gaza-occupation-cemeteries-now-full|work=Euronews|date=8 November 2023|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20240226161303/https://www.euronews.com/2023/11/08/israeli-troops-in-heart-of-gaza-city-us-warns-against-gaza-occupation-cemeteries-now-full |access-date=12 February 2024|archive-date=26 February 2024}}</ref>

A ''[[+972 Magazine]]'' investigation found the Israeli army had expanded authorization for bombing non-military targets.<ref name="972yuval">{{cite web |last1=Abraham |first1=Yuval |title='A mass assassination factory': Inside Israel's calculated bombing of Gaza |url=https://www.972mag.com/mass-assassination-factory-israel-calculated-bombing-gaza/ |website=+972 Magazine |date=30 November 2023 |access-date=1 December 2023 |archive-date=3 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231203003813/https://www.972mag.com/mass-assassination-factory-israel-calculated-bombing-gaza/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Research conducted by Dr. Yagil Levy at the [[Open University of Israel]] confirmed the ''+972'' report, stating Israel was "deliberately targeting residential blocks to cause mass civilian casualties".<ref>{{cite news |last1=Borger |first1=Julian |title=Civilians make up 61% of Gaza deaths from airstrikes, Israeli study finds |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/09/civilian-toll-israeli-airstrikes-gaza-unprecedented-killing-study#:~:text=Haaretz%20published%20an%20analysis%20by,airstrikes%20hovered%20at%20about%2040%25. |website=The Guardian |date=9 December 2023 |access-date=10 December 2023 |archive-date=9 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231209212750/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/09/civilian-toll-israeli-airstrikes-gaza-unprecedented-killing-study#:~:text=Haaretz%20published%20an%20analysis%20by,airstrikes%20hovered%20at%20about%2040%25. |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 31 October 2023, an [[Engineer's Building airstrike|Israeli airstrike hit Al-Muhandeseen Tower]] (the 'Engineers Tower'), a six-story apartment building in Gaza City, killing at least 106 civilians, including 34 women and 54 children.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Robertson |first1=Nick |title=Deadly Israeli strike on residential building 'apparent war crime': Human Rights Watch |url=https://thehill.com/policy/international/4574714-deadly-israeli-strike-on-residential-building-apparent-war-crime-human-rights-watch/ |website=thehill.com |date=4 April 2024 |publisher=The Hill |access-date=4 April 2024}}</ref> About 350 civilians were in and around the building, including 150 seeking shelter after being moved out of other parts of the city. Without warning, at about 2:30pm, four missiles struck the building within 10 seconds, completely demolishing it. At the time of the attack, children were playing soccer outside the building, and residents and sheltering civilians were charging their phones in the building's ground-floor grocery store.<ref>{{cite web |title=Rights group says Israeli strike on Gaza building killed 106 in apparent war crime |url=https://apnews.com/article/israel-gaza-airstrike-hamas-war-palestinians-344bd8da0254e83eedd7245a593823d0#:~:text=The%20Oct.%2031%20attack%20was,homes%20elsewhere%20in%20the%20territory. |website=Associated Press | date=4 April 2024 |access-date=4 April 2024}}</ref> The watchdog [[Airwars]] reported 133 to 164 civilians were killed, including 36 women and 67 to 77 children.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://airwars.org/civilian-casualties/ispt0784-october-31-2023/ |website=[[Airwars]] |access-date=4 April 2024 |title=ISPT0784 – October 31, 2023|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20251017154245/https://airwars.org/civilian-casualties/ispt0784-october-31-2023/ |archive-date=17 October 2025 }}</ref> On 4 April 2024, following an investigation, Human Rights Watch stated they found no evidence of a military target in the vicinity at the time of the attack, making the strike "unlawfully indiscriminate under the laws of war."<ref>{{cite web |title=Gaza: Israeli Strike Killing 106 Civilians an Apparent War Crime |url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2024/04/04/gaza-israeli-strike-killing-106-civilians-apparent-war-crime |website=hrw.org |date=4 April 2024 |publisher=Human Rights Watch |access-date=4 April 2024}}</ref>

===Lebanon===
{{Main|Israel–Hezbollah conflict (2023–present)}}
On 5 November 2023, an Israeli airstrike hit a car near [[Aynata|Ainata, Lebanon]], killing three children and their grandmother, and injuring their mother. The Israeli military admitted to striking the vehicle.<ref name="APNews Ainata">{{cite web |title=A woman and 3 children are killed by an Israeli airstrike in south Lebanon, local officials say |url=https://apnews.com/article/lebanon-israel-hezbollah-civilians-killed-hamas-03a050045c6bf3f87e12086b63b40a1c |website=apnews.com |date=5 November 2023 |publisher=AP News |access-date=16 November 2023 |archive-date=16 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231116221133/https://apnews.com/article/lebanon-israel-hezbollah-civilians-killed-hamas-03a050045c6bf3f87e12086b63b40a1c |url-status=live }}</ref> Human Rights Watch stated that their killings should be investigated as an apparent war crime.<ref name="HRW Ainata">{{cite web |title=Lebanon: Israeli Strike an Apparent War Crime |url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/11/14/lebanon-israeli-strike-apparent-war-crime |website=hrw.org |date=14 November 2023 |publisher=Human Rights Watch |access-date=16 November 2023 |archive-date=16 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231116013206/https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/11/14/lebanon-israeli-strike-apparent-war-crime |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Najib Mikati]], Lebanon's caretaker prime minister, called the attack a "heinous crime" and said that Lebanon would file a complaint to the [[United Nations Security Council|UN Security Council]].<ref name="APNews Ainata" /> Following an [[Israeli airstrike on the Iranian consulate in Damascus]], the [[Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Emigrants (Lebanon)|Lebanese Foreign Ministry]] called it a "breach of international law and a serious violation of the [[Vienna Convention on Consular Relations|Vienna agreements for diplomatic and consular relations]]".<ref>{{cite web |title=Lebanon denounces Israeli attack on Iranian consulate in Syria |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/2/israels-war-on-gaza-live-five-aid-workers-killed-after-delivering-food?update=2812320 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=10 April 2024 |archive-date=10 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240410043941/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/2/israels-war-on-gaza-live-five-aid-workers-killed-after-delivering-food?update=2812320 |url-status=live }}</ref> The UN Human Rights Office said the attack "violated the prohibition on the use of armed force against another state".<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel and Iran must de-escalate conflict to protect human rights, warn UN experts |url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2024/04/israel-and-iran-must-de-escalate-conflict-protect-human-rights-warn-un |website=United Nations |publisher=United Nations Human Rights Office of the High Commissioner |access-date=19 April 2024 |archive-date=16 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240416172525/https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2024/04/israel-and-iran-must-de-escalate-conflict-protect-human-rights-warn-un |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Humanitarian aid===
{{see also|Humanitarian aid during the Gaza war#Killing of aid workers}}

The Gaza war has been deadliest conflict for United Nations workers in world history.<ref>{{cite web |date=17 December 2023 |title=Complete communication blackout for four days and counting makes aid distribution in Gaza near impossible |url=https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/complete-communication-blackout-four-days-and-counting-makes-aid-distribution-gaza-near-impossible |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240312025733/https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/complete-communication-blackout-four-days-and-counting-makes-aid-distribution-gaza-near-impossible |archive-date=12 March 2024 |access-date=18 December 2023 |website=ReliefWeb |publisher=Save the Children}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Atay Alam |first1=Hande |date=14 November 2023 |title=UN mourns the deaths of more than 100 aid workers in Gaza, the highest number killed in any conflict in its history |url=https://www.cnn.com/2023/11/14/middleeast/united-nations-staff-deaths-gaza-intl-hnk/index.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231218234353/https://www.cnn.com/2023/11/14/middleeast/united-nations-staff-deaths-gaza-intl-hnk/index.html |archive-date=18 December 2023 |access-date=18 December 2023 |website=CNN}}</ref> By March 2024, at least 196 UN relief workers had been killed and more than 150 facilities attacked in the Gaza Strip.<ref>{{cite web |title=UNRWA spokeswoman says aid operation ongoing at targeted Rafah aid centre |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/14/israels-war-on-gaza-live-rafah-attack-coming-soon-despite-pressure?update=2771982 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240316233035/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/14/israels-war-on-gaza-live-rafah-attack-coming-soon-despite-pressure?update=2771982 |archive-date=16 March 2024 |access-date=16 March 2024 |website=Al Jazeera}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Nichols |first1=Michelle |title=UN chief to Israel: 196 aid workers have been killed, why? |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/un-chief-hopes-israel-quickly-effectively-boost-gaza-aid-access-2024-04-05/ |access-date=9 April 2024 |website=Reuters}}</ref>

Following the death of one of their aid workers — the fifth American aid worker killed in Gaza — the [[American Near East Refugee Aid]] released a statement: "We demand an independent investigation into his death, which threatens our team’s ability to function safely and deliver aid to civilians facing starvation".<ref>{{cite web |title=US charity demands independent probe into staff member's killing in Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/10/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israel-is-restricting-lifesaving-aid-unrwa?update=2762711 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=13 March 2024 |archive-date=13 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240313013414/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/10/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israel-is-restricting-lifesaving-aid-unrwa?update=2762711 |url-status=live }}</ref> In March 2024, Israel bombed a United Nations food distribution center, killing one UN staff member and wounding 22 others.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Besheer |first1=Margaret |title=UN: Israeli Strike on Gaza Food Distribution Center Kills 1, Injures 22 |url=https://www.voanews.com/a/un-israeli-strike-on-gaza-food-distribution-center-kills-1-injures-22-/7526237.html |website=VOA |date=13 March 2024 |access-date=15 March 2024 |archive-date=15 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240315025604/https://www.voanews.com/a/un-israeli-strike-on-gaza-food-distribution-center-kills-1-injures-22-/7526237.html |url-status=live }}</ref>{{efn|In reaction to news of the bombing, the US Secretary of State said that Israel should not bomb "clearly marked" humanitarian facilities.<ref>{{cite web |title=Blinken comments on Israeli attack on UNRWA facility |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/13/israels-war-on-gaza-live-netanyahu-vows-to-finish-the-job-in-rafah?update=2770945 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=16 March 2024 |archive-date=16 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240316015538/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/13/israels-war-on-gaza-live-netanyahu-vows-to-finish-the-job-in-rafah?update=2770945 |url-status=live }}</ref>}} It was one of the UN's last remaining distribution centers, leading the organization's humanitarian aid chief [[Martin Griffiths]] to state that aid teams "must be protected".<ref>{{cite web |title=Scenes of the aftermath of Israeli bombing of UNRWA distribution centre |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/13/israels-war-on-gaza-live-netanyahu-vows-to-finish-the-job-in-rafah?update=2770768 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=16 March 2024 |archive-date=16 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240316030642/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/13/israels-war-on-gaza-live-netanyahu-vows-to-finish-the-job-in-rafah?update=2770768 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Gaza: Aid missions constantly under threat, warns UN humanitarian chief |url=https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/03/1147516 |website=UN News |date=14 March 2024 |publisher=United Nations |access-date=16 March 2024 |archive-date=16 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240316030319/https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/03/1147516 |url-status=live }}</ref>

A ''New York Times'' investigation showed six Western aid groups had humanitarian sites hit by Israeli strikes, even though the locations were shared with the IDF.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/100000009393031/aid-groups-gaza-israel.html|title=Video: 'We're Aware of the Location': Aid Groups in Gaza Coordinated With I.D.F. but Still Came Under Fire|first1=Haley|last1=Willis|first2=Robin|last2=Stein|first3=Ainara|last3=Tiefenthäler|first4=Natalie|last4=Reneau|first5=Aaron|last5=Byrd|first6=Anushka|last6=Patil|work=The New York Times|date=25 April 2024|via=NYTimes.com|access-date=27 April 2024|archive-date=27 April 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240427133552/https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/100000009393031/aid-groups-gaza-israel.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.newarab.com/news/aid-groups-gaza-targeted-israel-despite-coordination|title=Aid groups in Gaza targeted by Israel despite coordination|first=Anam|last=Alam|date=26 April 2024|website=New Arab|access-date=27 April 2024|archive-date=27 April 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240427133556/https://www.newarab.com/news/aid-groups-gaza-targeted-israel-despite-coordination|url-status=live}}</ref> In April 2024, Belgium recalled its ambassador to Israel after an [[Enabel]] aid worker and his son were killed by an Israel airstrike. The Belgian Foreign Minister [[Hadja Lahbib]] reacted by stating, "Bombing civilian areas and populations is contrary to international law."<ref>{{cite web |title=Belgium Summons Israeli Ambassador Over Aid Worker's Death |url=https://www.barrons.com/news/belgium-summons-israeli-ambassador-over-aid-worker-s-death-5194499d |website=Barron's |publisher=Agence France Presse |access-date=30 April 2024 |archive-date=30 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240430002425/https://www.barrons.com/news/belgium-summons-israeli-ambassador-over-aid-worker-s-death-5194499d |url-status=live }}</ref> The [[Quincy Institute for Responsible Statecraft|Quincy Institute]] found fourteen incidents where Israel attacked humanitarian aid workers, despite being identified as civilians.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Semler |first1=Stephen |title=Is Israel intentionally attacking aid workers? |url=https://responsiblestatecraft.org/israel-hamas-war-gaza/ |website=Responsible Statecraft |access-date=17 September 2024}}</ref>

====Flour massacre====
{{main|Flour massacre}}
On 29 February 2024, more than 100 people seeking aid were killed in [[Gaza City]] during an incident that became known as the [[flour massacre]].<ref>{{cite web |title='Massacre': Dozens killed by Israeli fire in Gaza while collecting food aid |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/2/29/dozens-killed-injured-by-israeli-fire-in-gaza-while-collecting-food-aid |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=1 March 2024 |archive-date=29 February 2024 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20240229194025/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/2/29/dozens-killed-injured-by-israeli-fire-in-gaza-while-collecting-food-aid |url-status=live }}</ref> Belgian Deputy Prime Minister [[Petra de Sutter]] stated the massacre was a "flagrant violation of international humanitarian law".<ref name=":11">{{Cite news |title='Heinous': Deadly Israeli attack on Gaza aid-seekers condemned |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/2/29/heinous-deadly-israeli-attack-on-gaza-aid-seekers-condemned |access-date=29 February 2024 |work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]] |language=en |archive-date=29 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240229160619/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/2/29/heinous-deadly-israeli-attack-on-gaza-aid-seekers-condemned |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Josep Borrell]] stated it was a serious violation of international humanitarian law.<ref>{{cite web |title=Deaths of Palestinians seeking aid 'unacceptable': EU top diplomat |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/1/israels-war-on-gaza-live-mass-shooting-of-aid-seekers-condemned-globally?update=2741209 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=1 March 2024 |archive-date=1 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240301014654/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/1/israels-war-on-gaza-live-mass-shooting-of-aid-seekers-condemned-globally?update=2741209 |url-status=live }}</ref>  The [[Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Turkey)|Turkish Ministry of Foreign Affairs]] called the attack a [[crime against humanity]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Turkey says Israel committed 'yet another crime against humanity' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/29/israels-war-on-gaza-live-mass-killing-of-children-in-slow-motion-ngo?update=2741016 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=1 March 2024 |archive-date=29 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240229220536/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/29/israels-war-on-gaza-live-mass-killing-of-children-in-slow-motion-ngo?update=2741016 |url-status=live }}</ref> The [[Foreign Ministry (Oman)|Omani Foreign Ministry]] called the attack a violation of international law.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israeli attack on aid seekers continuation of 'extermination' policy: Oman |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/29/israels-war-on-gaza-live-mass-killing-of-children-in-slow-motion-ngo?update=2740937 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=1 March 2024 |archive-date=1 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240301000318/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/29/israels-war-on-gaza-live-mass-killing-of-children-in-slow-motion-ngo?update=2740937 |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Amnesty International]] announced it was launching an investigation.<ref>{{cite web |title=Amnesty says investigating deadly Israeli attack on aid seekers |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/29/israels-war-on-gaza-live-mass-killing-of-children-in-slow-motion-ngo?update=2741141 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=1 March 2024 |archive-date=1 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240301161839/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/29/israels-war-on-gaza-live-mass-killing-of-children-in-slow-motion-ngo?update=2741141 |url-status=live }}</ref> The United Nations Human Rights Office also called for an investigation, stating it had "recorded at least 14 incidents involving shooting and shelling of people gathered to receive desperately needed supplies".<ref>{{cite web |title=UN Human Rights Office strongly deplores killing of at least 112 Palestinians during food aid distribution in Gaza City |url=https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/un-human-rights-office-opt-un-human-rights-office-strongly-deplores-killing-least-112-palestinians-during-food-aid-distribution-gaza-city-enar#:~:text=From%20mid%2DJanuary%20to%20the,a%20majority%20of%20these%20incidents |website=ReliefWeb |date=March 2024 |publisher=OHCHR |access-date=4 March 2024 |archive-date=4 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240304061538/https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/un-human-rights-office-opt-un-human-rights-office-strongly-deplores-killing-least-112-palestinians-during-food-aid-distribution-gaza-city-enar#:~:text=From%20mid%2DJanuary%20to%20the,a%20majority%20of%20these%20incidents |url-status=live }}</ref>

====World Central Kitchen drone strikes====
{{main|World Central Kitchen aid convoy attack}}

On 1 April 2024, an [[World Central Kitchen aid convoy attack|Israeli drone fired three consecutive missiles]] at three cars belonging to the [[World Central Kitchen]] (WCK), killing seven aid workers who had been distributing food in the northern [[Gaza Strip|Gaza]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Talmazan |first=Yuliya |date=2 April 2024 |title=Israeli strike kills 7 aid workers in Gaza, World Central Kitchen halts operations |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/news/world/world-central-kitchen-says-israeli-strike-kills-7-workers-halts-aid-rcna145976 |access-date=2 April 2024 |website=NBC News |language=en |archive-date=2 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240402171915/https://www.nbcnews.com/news/world/world-central-kitchen-says-israeli-strike-kills-7-workers-halts-aid-rcna145976 |url-status=live }}</ref> The president of [[Refugees International]] called the killings "part of a clear pattern" and a war crime.<ref>{{cite web |title='A clear war crime': President of Refugees International on killed aid workers |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/2/israels-war-on-gaza-live-five-aid-workers-killed-after-delivering-food?update=2813502 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=9 April 2024 |archive-date=9 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240409205955/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/2/israels-war-on-gaza-live-five-aid-workers-killed-after-delivering-food?update=2813502 |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Doctors Without Borders]] stated the killings were an example of how "international humanitarian law is not respected".<ref>{{cite web |title=Aid workers 'part of collective punishment faced by Gaza civilians' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/2/israels-war-on-gaza-live-five-aid-workers-killed-after-delivering-food?update=2813109 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=10 April 2024 |archive-date=10 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240410014950/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/2/israels-war-on-gaza-live-five-aid-workers-killed-after-delivering-food?update=2813109 |url-status=live }}</ref> The [[Polish Foreign Ministry]] stated, "Poland objects to the disregard for international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite web |title=Poland's Foreign Ministry reacts to killing of Polish aid volunteer |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/2/israels-war-on-gaza-live-five-aid-workers-killed-after-delivering-food?update=2812388 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=10 April 2024 |archive-date=10 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240410040545/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/2/israels-war-on-gaza-live-five-aid-workers-killed-after-delivering-food?update=2812388 |url-status=live }}</ref> The [[Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Cyprus)|Cyprus Foreign Ministry]] stated, "[International humanitarian law] principles are absolute: humanitarian aid workers must always be respected and protected."<ref>{{cite web |title=Cyprus condemns killings of World Central Kitchen workers |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/2/israels-war-on-gaza-live-five-aid-workers-killed-after-delivering-food?update=2812164 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=10 April 2024 |archive-date=10 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240510124442/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/2/israels-war-on-gaza-live-five-aid-workers-killed-after-delivering-food?update=2812164 |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Ben Saul]], a UN special rapporteur, stated, "It could well be a violation of international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite web |title=Targeting of aid workers a violation of international humanitarian law: Expert |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/2/israels-war-on-gaza-live-five-aid-workers-killed-after-delivering-food?update=2812143 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=10 April 2024 |archive-date=10 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240410045323/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/2/israels-war-on-gaza-live-five-aid-workers-killed-after-delivering-food?update=2812143 |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Jose Andres]], the founder of World Central Kitchen, stated Israel needed "to stop this indiscriminate killing."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Frazier |first1=Kierra |title=José Andrés calls on Israel to 'stop killing civilians and aid workers' after airstrike kills staff |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2024/04/03/jose-andres-world-central-kitchen-gaza-00150314 |website=Politico |date=3 April 2024 |access-date=10 April 2024 |archive-date=10 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240410051117/https://www.politico.com/news/2024/04/03/jose-andres-world-central-kitchen-gaza-00150314 |url-status=live }}</ref>

====Gaza aid distribution massacres ====
{{main|2025 Gaza Strip aid distribution killings}}

On 27 May 2025, the [[Gaza Humanitarian Foundation]] (GHF), an American and Israeli-backed organization, began distributing aid in [[Tel al-Sultan]], Rafah. Thousands of Palestinians gathered, leading to chaotic scenes.<ref>{{cite web|date=27 May 2025|title= Faced with hunger, Palestinians crowd a controversial aid centre in Gaza|url= https://www.aljazeera.com/gallery/2025/5/27/photos-thousands-of-palestinians-crowd-a-controversial-aid-centre-in-gaza|website=Al Jazeera|access-date=3 June 2025}}</ref> Reports emerged of Israeli tanks opening fire on the crowd, resulting in at least three deaths and 48 injuries. The IDF claimed they fired warning shots to control the situation, while a UN spokesperson indicated that most injuries were due to gunfire from the IDF. The next days saw escalating violence.<ref>{{cite web|title= Israeli forces open fire a kilometer away from Gaza aid site, killing 3, health officials say|url= https://apnews.com/article/israel-palestinians-hamas-war-news-ceasefire-aid-06-02-2025-13980028c67e29262ee9fd85371e0630#|website=Associated Press|date=3 June 2025|author1=Mohammad Jahjouh|author2=Wafaa Shurafa|author3=Samy Magdy|access-date=3 June 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=27 May 2025|title= 'Deliberate massacre' in Gaza as starving Palestinians seek Israeli-US aid|url= https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/5/27/heartbreaking-chaos-in-gaza-as-starving-palestinians-seek-us-israeli-aid|website=Al Jazeera|access-date=3 June 2025}}</ref> On 31 May, three Palestinians were killed while attempting to reach the aid center. By 1 June, it was reported that 32 civilians were killed and over 250 wounded at the aid site. The Palestine Red Crescent Society confirmed retrieving at least 23 bodies and numerous injured individuals from the area.<ref>{{cite web|date=1 June 2025|title= Israel kills 32 starving Palestinians in latest US aid point 'massacre'|url= https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/israel-kills-32-starving-palestinians-latest-us-aid-point-massacre|website=Middle East Eye|author1=Maha Hussaini|author2=Mohammed al-Hajjar|access-date=3 June 2025}}</ref> By 2 June, at least 75 civilians were killed and more than 400 others were injured by Israeli forces.<ref>{{cite web|date=1 June 2025|title= Palestinians gunned down while trying to reach food aid site in Gaza, hospital says|url= https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jun/01/palestinians-gunned-down-while-trying-to-reach-food-aid-site-in-gaza-hospital-says|website=The Guardian|author1=Lorenzo Tondo|author2=Malak A. Tantesh|access-date=3 June 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=2 June 2025|title= Israeli forces kill three starving Palestinians queuing for food, raising death toll of aid seekers to 75|url= https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/israel-kills-starving-palestinians-seeking-aid-southern-gaza|website=Middle East Eye|last=Aladam|first=Mera|access-date=3 June 2025}}</ref> By 12 June, at least 223 Palestinians were killed and more than 1,800 others were injured while trying to reach the aid distribution centers.<ref>{{cite web|date=12 June 2025|last1=Gritten|first1=David|last2=Usher|first2=Sebastian|title= Dozens of Palestinians killed while seeking aid in Gaza, hospitals say |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c1mg4ld5951o|website=BBC News|access-date=12 June 2025}}</ref>

These incidents have drawn international condemnation. UN Secretary-General António Guterres called for an independent investigation into the shootings.<ref>{{cite web|date=2 June 2025|title= UN chief calls for probe into killings near Gaza aid distribution centre|url= https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20250602-un-chief-calls-for-probe-into-killings-near-gaza-aid-distribution-centre|website=France 24|access-date=3 June 2025}}</ref> The head of UNRWA, [[Philippe Lazzarini]], condemned the US-backed aid model in Gaza, saying it is a “distraction from atrocities” and "a waste of resources".<ref>{{cite web|title= US-backed Gaza aid model 'distraction from atrocities', UNRWA chief says|url= https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/5/28/us-backed-gaza-aid-model-distraction-from-atrocities-unrwa-chief-says|website=Al Jazeera|date=28 May 2025|access-date=3 June 2025}}</ref>

=== 18 March attacks ===
{{main| March 2025 Israeli attacks on the Gaza Strip}}

On 18 March 2025, Israel bombed Gaza, further violating<ref name="The Intercept Israel Ceasefire Violations">{{cite web |last1=Valdez |first1=Jonah |title=Israel Violated the Ceasefire from the Start |url=https://theintercept.com/2025/03/19/israel-gaza-ceasefire-hamas/ |website=The Intercept |date=19 March 2025 |access-date=20 March 2025}}</ref><ref name="BBC Israeli Ceasefire Violations" />{{efn|The IDF killed over 140 during the ceasefire, according to the Gaza Health Ministry.}} and ending a two-month ceasefire agreement with Hamas, and beginning a significant military operation. The Israeli airstrikes killed at least 404 Palestinians, including 183 children and 94 women, according to Gaza’s Health Ministry, making them the deadliest since the conflict began in 2023.<ref>{{cite web|last1= MacKenzie|first1= James|last2= Al-Mughrabi|first2= Nidal|last3= Rose|first3= Emily|last4= Al-Mughrabi|first4= Nidal|title= Israel warns more to come as airstrikes kill over 400 in Gaza after two months of truce |url= https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israeli-military-conducts-strikes-hamas-targets-gaza-army-says-2025-03-18/|website=Reuters|date= 18 March 2025|access-date=19 March 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title= Death toll rises to 413 as Israeli airstrike continues: health authorities |url= https://english.news.cn/20250318/d90ee78ccfce4cf9a85361fd23645333/c.html|website=Xinhua|access-date=18 March 2025}}</ref> Human Rights Watch stated that Israeli military forces caused deaths and unnecessary suffering of Palestinian patients while occupying hospitals in the Gaza Strip, amounting to war crimes. They further said that Israeli forces denied water and electricity to the sick and wounded, mistreated and forcibly displaced patients and health workers, and destroyed medical facilities.<ref name="HRW Ceasefire Violation Medical War Crimes">{{cite web |title=Gaza: Israeli Military War Crimes While Occupying Hospitals |url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2025/03/20/gaza-israeli-military-war-crimes-while-occupying-hospitals |website=hrw.org |date=20 March 2025 |publisher=Human Rights Watch |access-date=20 March 2025}}</ref>

Amnesty International condemned the attacks, stating, "Israel's genocide and its unlawful air strikes have already caused unprecedented humanitarian suffering in Gaza. Today, we are back to square one. Since 2 March, Israel has re-imposed a total siege on Gaza blocking the entry of all humanitarian aid, medicine, and commercial supplies, including fuel and food, in flagrant violation of international law. Israel has also cut off electricity to Gaza's main operational desalination plant. And today the Israeli military has once again started issuing mass 'evacuation' orders displacing Palestinians."<ref name="Amnesty Israel Breaks Ceasefire Unilateral">{{cite web |title=Israeli air strikes kill over 400 Palestinians across Gaza following unilateral resumption of mass attacks |url=https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2025/03/israeli-air-strikes-kill-over-400-palestinians-across-gaza-following-unilateral-resumption-of-mass-attacks/ |date=18 March 2025 |publisher=Amnesty International |access-date=20 March 2025}}</ref> The United Nations reported that one of its staff members was killed, and five others were injured in a strike on a UN guesthouse in Gaza. UN Secretary-General António Guterres called for an investigation, emphasizing the protection of UN premises under international law.  The [[Arab League]] condemned the attacks, labeling them as acts of genocide and ethnic cleansing, and urged the UN and the United States to take action against Israel.<ref>{{cite news|title= Israel launches ground operation to reoccupy corridor which splits Gaza in half|url= https://www.euronews.com/2025/03/19/israel-launches-ground-operation-to-reoccupy-corridor-which-splits-gaza-in-half|website=Euronews|access-date=19 March 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Bulgarian working for UN died in Gaza Strip, foreign ministry says|url= https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/bulgarian-national-working-un-died-gaza-strip-foreign-ministry-says-2025-03-19/|website=Reuters|date= 19 March 2025|access-date=19 March 2025}}</ref>

== Ceasefire violations by the IDF ==
{{main|January 2025 Gaza war ceasefire#Violations and deviations by Israel|Gaza peace plan#Violations and deviations}}

Since the implementation of the [[January 2025 Gaza war ceasefire|ceasefire]] between Israel and Hamas on 19 January 2025, the IDF bombed and shelled Gaza and the West Bank, and shot people in a number of incidents, violating the agreement.<ref>{{Cite news|title=In violation of Gaza ceasefire, Israel kills man, wounds others in Rafah|url=https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20250123-in-violation-of-gaza-ceasefire-israel-kills-man-wounds-others-in-rafah/|date=23 January 2025|work=Middle East Monitor}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|title= Hundreds flee Jenin amid Israel's deepening West Bank crackdown|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jan/23/people-flee-jenin-amid-israel-deepening-west-bank-crackdown|work=The Guardian|date=23 January 2025}}</ref> According to the Gaza Ministry of Health, the IDF killed over 140 people in two months during the ceasefire.<ref name="BBC Israeli Ceasefire Violations">{{cite web |last1=Nader |first1=Emir |title=Why has Israel bombed Gaza and what next for ceasefire deal? |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cq6yp5d5v9jo |website=bbc.com |date=18 March 2025 |publisher=BBC |access-date=18 March 2025}}</ref> ''The Intercept'' reported that Israeli forces 150 killed during this period, including civilians, journalists, and aid workers, in addition to cutting electricity and blocking the entry of food and fuel, likely constituting war crimes.<ref name="The Intercept Israel Ceasefire Violations" />

== Summary executions ==
{{See also|Executions and assassinations during the Gaza war}}
[[Summary execution]] refers to the killing of persons who are not actively taking part in hostilities, even if otherwise they are combatants. It includes killing unarmed, surrendering or wounded people instead of giving the benefit of a [[Right to a fair trial|fair trial]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=September 2007 |title=State of Anarchy: Rebellion and Abuses against Civilians: &nbsp; Applicable legal standards |url=https://www.hrw.org/reports/2007/car0907/5.htm |access-date=2025-03-14 |website=Human Rights Watch}}</ref> Regarding summary executions in Gaza, [[Middlesex University]] professor [[William Schabas]] stated, "It's not really important to demonstrate that they're civilians. Summary executions even of fighters, even of combatants is a war crime."<ref>{{cite web |title='Summary execution is a war crime' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/1/19/israels-war-on-gaza-live-us-support-for-israel-ironclad-despite-rebuff?update=2634326 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240119165218/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/1/19/israels-war-on-gaza-live-us-support-for-israel-ironclad-despite-rebuff?update=2634326 |archive-date=19 January 2024 |access-date=20 January 2024 |website=Al Jazeera}}</ref>

[[OHCHR]] stated on 20 December it had received allegations of Israeli soldiers summarily killing at least eleven unarmed men in [[Rimal]].<ref>{{cite web |title=UN Human Rights Office - OPT: Unlawful killings in Gaza City |url=https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/un-human-rights-office-opt-unlawful-killings-gaza-city |website=ReliefWeb |date=20 December 2023 |publisher=OHCHR |access-date=21 December 2023 |archive-date=24 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231224110520/https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/un-human-rights-office-opt-unlawful-killings-gaza-city |url-status=live }}</ref> ''Al Jazeera'' reported the number summary execution of 15 people during an apartment raid. The execution was witnessed by the families of the men.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Video shows aftermath of a summary execution of 15 men in a Gaza apartment |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/program/newsfeed/2024/1/18/video-shows-aftermath-of-a-summary-execution-of-15-men-in-a-gaza-apartment |access-date=20 January 2024 |website=Al Jazeera |language=en |archive-date=20 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240120020001/https://www.aljazeera.com/program/newsfeed/2024/1/18/video-shows-aftermath-of-a-summary-execution-of-15-men-in-a-gaza-apartment |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Euro-Mediterranean Human Rights Monitor|Euro-Med Monitor]] stated they believe this is part a pattern of "systematic" killing. They added that "In at least 13 of field executions, we corroborated that it was arbitrary on the part of the Israeli forces."<ref name="Al Jazeera 2024 g408">{{cite web | title=Palestinians accuse Israeli forces of executing 19 civilians in Gaza | website=Al Jazeera | date=20 January 2024 | url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/1/20/palestinians-accuse-israeli-forces-of-executing-19-civilians-in-gaza | access-date=18 April 2024 | archive-date=16 April 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240416111102/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/1/20/palestinians-accuse-israeli-forces-of-executing-19-civilians-in-gaza | url-status=live }}</ref> On 26 December 2023, Euro-Med Monitor submitted a file to the [[International Criminal Court]] and the UN that documented dozens of cases of summary executions carried out by Israeli forces, and called for an investigation.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20231226-euro-med-submits-findings-on-israeli-army-executions-in-gaza-to-icc-un-calling-them-genocide/|title=Euro-Med submits findings on Israeli army executions in Gaza to ICC, UN, calling them 'genocide' – Middle East Monitor|date=26 December 2023 |access-date=13 February 2024|archive-date=4 January 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240104213949/https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20231226-euro-med-submits-findings-on-israeli-army-executions-in-gaza-to-icc-un-calling-them-genocide/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.commondreams.org/news/israeli-executions|title=Watchdog Submits Evidence of Israeli Executions of Gaza Civilians to UN, ICC|website=www.commondreams.org|access-date=13 February 2024|archive-date=13 February 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240213151431/https://www.commondreams.org/news/israeli-executions|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.alquds.com/en/posts/105179|title=جريدة القدس|access-date=13 February 2024|archive-date=24 March 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324114657/https://www.alquds.com/en/posts/105179|url-status=live}}</ref>

In March 2024, video of an Israeli soldier bragging about killing an elderly deaf man hiding under his bed was released. The [[Council on American-Islamic Relations]] condemned the killing as an execution and war crime.<ref>{{cite web |title=Video of Israeli soldier bragging about killing elderly Palestinian condemned |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/9/israels-war-on-gaza-live-ceasefire-by-ramadan-looking-tough-biden-says?update=2761177 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=10 March 2024 |archive-date=9 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240309183750/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/9/israels-war-on-gaza-live-ceasefire-by-ramadan-looking-tough-biden-says?update=2761177 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Palestinian killed by Israeli soldier identified as elderly deaf man |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/10/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israel-is-restricting-lifesaving-aid-unrwa?update=2762212 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=13 March 2024 |archive-date=13 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240313021719/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/10/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israel-is-restricting-lifesaving-aid-unrwa?update=2762212 |url-status=live }}</ref> The Israeli military stated they would begin a probe into the incident.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Khan |first1=Laura |title=Israeli military to probe killing of unarmed, elderly and disabled Palestinian |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/11/israels-war-on-gaza-live-ramadan-begins-with-no-end-to-israels-siege?update=2764061 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=14 March 2024 |archive-date=14 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240314213254/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/11/israels-war-on-gaza-live-ramadan-begins-with-no-end-to-israels-siege?update=2764061 |url-status=live }}</ref>

Defense officials told ''[[Haaretz]]'' that the Israeli army had created [[kill zone]]s in Gaza, in which any person who crossed an "invisible line" was killed.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Kubovich |first1=Yaniv |title=Israel Created 'Kill Zones' in Gaza. Anyone Who Crosses Into Them Is Shot |url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2024-03-31/ty-article-magazine/.premium/israel-created-kill-zones-in-gaza-anyone-who-crosses-into-them-is-shot/0000018e-946c-d4de-afee-f46da9ee0000 |website=Haaretz |date=31 March 2024 |access-date=6 April 2024 |archive-date=1 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240401001912/https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2024-03-31/ty-article-magazine/.premium/israel-created-kill-zones-in-gaza-anyone-who-crosses-into-them-is-shot/0000018e-946c-d4de-afee-f46da9ee0000 |url-status=live }}</ref> Israeli soldiers gave testimony to ''+972 Magazine'' stating soldiers were given authorization to shoot Palestinian civilians at will.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Ziv |first1=Oren |title='I'm bored, so I shoot': The Israeli army's approval of free-for-all violence in Gaza |url=https://www.972mag.com/israeli-soldiers-gaza-firing-regulations/ |website=+972 Magazine |date=8 July 2024 |access-date=13 July 2024}}</ref>

=== Children ===
Mark Perlmutter, an American doctor working in Gaza, stated Israeli snipers were deliberately targeting children. He stated "No toddler gets shot twice by mistake by the 'world's best sniper.' And they're dead-center shots."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Smith |first1=Tracy |title=Children of Gaza |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/children-of-gaza/ |website=CBS News |date=21 July 2024 |access-date=3 August 2024}}</ref> In a letter addressed to US President Joe Biden, a group of American doctors and nurses returning from Gaza stated, "Every one of us on a daily basis treated pre-teen children who were shot in the head and chest".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Akbarzai |first1=Sahar |title='We cannot remain silent about what we saw.' US doctors who volunteered in Gaza demand ceasefire in letter to White House |url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/07/26/world/open-letter-45-us-physicians-gaza/index.html |website=CNN |date=26 July 2024 |access-date=18 August 2024}}</ref>

In October 2024, ''The New York Times'' reported compiled testimony from 44 doctors, nurses, and paramedics who treated multiple cases of [[Effect of the Gaza war on children in the Gaza Strip|preteen children]] with gunshot wounds to the head or chest in Gaza. The Israeli army reacted to the experiences of these health care workers with a statement that did not directly confirm whether investigations into the shootings of children had been conducted or if any soldiers faced disciplinary action for firing at them.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/10/09/opinion/gaza-doctor-interviews.html|title=65 Doctors, Nurses and Paramedics: What We Saw in Gaza|last=Sidhwa|first=Feroze|date=9 October 2024|work=[[The New York Times]]|archive-url=https://archive.today/20241012012500/https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/10/09/opinion/gaza-doctor-interviews.html|archive-date=12 October 2024|url-status=live|access-date=12 October 2024}}</ref> In response to claims alleging that the report was based on "fabricated evidence", ''The New York Times'' issued a statement defending the integrity of the piece, emphasizing that it had undergone rigorous editing and verification, including consultations with experts and the use of supporting photographs, which they deemed "too horrific for publication."<ref>*{{cite web|url=https://www.newarab.com/news/nyt-rebuts-claims-fake-images-gaza-children-shot-head|title=NYT rebuts pro-Israeli denial of scans showing Gaza children shot in head by soldiers|date=16 October 2024|work=[[The New Arab]]|archive-url=https://archive.today/20241022011857/https://www.newarab.com/news/nyt-rebuts-claims-fake-images-gaza-children-shot-head|archive-date=22 October 2024|url-status=live|access-date=22 October 2024}}
*{{cite web|url=https://www.thewrap.com/new-york-times-stands-by-report-child-gunshot-wounds-gaza/|title=New York Times Stands By Report of Child Gunshot Wounds in Gaza: 'Rigorously Edited' and Double-Vetted|last=Dickey|first=Josh|date=16 October 2024|work=[[The Wrap]]|archive-url=https://archive.today/20241022013025/https://www.thewrap.com/new-york-times-stands-by-report-child-gunshot-wounds-gaza/|archive-date=22 October 2024|url-status=live|access-date=22 October 2024}}</ref> In an interview with ''[[Mother Jones (magazine)|Mother Jones]]'', Dr. Feroze Sidhwa explained the circumstances of the children's death, stating, "On the occasion when the child survived long enough and there was family... to ask what happened—they would say, the kids were just playing. I never heard from a family that they were in a crossfire".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Hurwitz |first1=Sophie |title=The Doctor Who Saw Children Shot in the Head in Gaza—and Tried to Tell the World |url=https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2024/10/feroze-sidhwa-new-york-times-children-gaza-shot-in-head-israel-palestine-doctor/ |website=Mother Jones |access-date=31 October 2024}}</ref>

In June 2026, [[Srinivasan Muralidhar]], chairman of the [[Independent International Commission of Inquiry on the Occupied Palestinian Territory]] under the United Nations, stated that Israeli forces have continued to commit genocide in Gaza by deliberately targeting and killing Palestinian children, citing a report published by the commission.<ref>{{Cite web|date=23 June 2026|title= Israel continues to commit genocide, atrocity crimes by deliberately targeting Palestinian children, UN independent commission finds|url= https://news.un.org/en/story/2026/06/1167790|website=UN News|access-date=27 June 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title= Israel continues to commit genocide and other atrocity crimes by deliberately targeting Palestinian children|url= https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2026/06/israel-continues-commit-genocide-and-other-atrocity-crimes-deliberately|website=Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights|date=23 June 2026|access-date=27 June 2026}}</ref> In response, Israeli officials dismissed the report and denied that Israel is committing a genocide, as well as calling the report as "a propaganda piece as outrageous as its previous ones."<ref>{{Cite news|title= U.N. inquiry finds Israel still committing genocide, which Israel denies|url= https://www.ms.now/news/u-n-inquiry-finds-israel-still-committing-genocide-which-israel-denies|work=[[MS NOW]]|date=24 June 2026|last=Salam|first=Erum|access-date=27 June 2026}}</ref>

=== Mass graves ===
{{main|Gaza Strip mass graves|Israeli razing of cemeteries and necroviolence against Palestinians}} 
A [[mass grave]] with 283 bodies was uncovered in April 2024 at Khan Younis's [[Nasser Hospital|Nasser medical complex]] in Gaza City. Further mass graves with several hundreds of bodies were found in the courtyard of Al-Shifa Hospital.<ref>{{cite web |title=Nearly 300 bodies found in mass grave at Gaza hospital, authorities say |url=https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/gaza-khan-younis-israel-war-1.7181040 |access-date=22 April 2024 |website=Cbc.ca |archive-date=22 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240422175944/https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/gaza-khan-younis-israel-war-1.7181040 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Nearly 200 bodies found in mass grave at hospital in Gaza's Khan Younis |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/4/21/nearly-200-bodies-found-in-mass-grave-at-hospital-in-gazas-khan-younis |access-date=23 April 2024 |website=Al Jazeera |language=en |archive-date=22 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240422210426/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/4/21/nearly-200-bodies-found-in-mass-grave-at-hospital-in-gazas-khan-younis |url-status=live }}</ref> Reports indicated that some of the bodies were found with their hands and feet tied.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Salman |first1=Abeer |last2=Dahman |first2=Ibrahim |last3=Lister |first3=Tim |date=22 April 2024 |title=Nearly 300 bodies found in mass grave at Gaza hospital, says Gaza Civil Defense |url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/04/22/middleeast/khan-younis-nasser-hospital-mass-grave-intl/index.html |access-date=23 April 2024 |website=CNN |language=en |archive-date=24 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240424055513/https://www.cnn.com/2024/04/22/middleeast/khan-younis-nasser-hospital-mass-grave-intl/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Mass Burials At Al-shifa Hospital |url=https://forensic-architecture.org/investigation/mass-burials-at-al-shifa-hospital |access-date=2025-03-14 |website=Forensic Architecture}}</ref> Following the discovery of the mass graves, UN human rights chief [[Volker Türk]] called for an independent investigation on the intentional killing of civilians by the Israeli Defense Forces. He stated the "intentional killing of civilians, detainees, and others who are [[hors de combat]] is a war crime."<ref>{{Cite web |date=23 April 2024 |title=Mass graves in Gaza show victims' hands were tied, says UN rights office {{!}} UN News |url=https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/04/1148876 |access-date=23 April 2024 |website=news.un.org |language=en |archive-date=24 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240424005326/https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/04/1148876 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Gritten |first1=David |title=UN rights chief 'horrified' by mass grave reports at Gaza hospitals |url=https://sg.news.yahoo.com/un-rights-chief-horrified-mass-181544829.html |website=Yahoo! News |date=24 April 2024 |publisher=BBC News |access-date=4 May 2024 |archive-date=4 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240504232721/https://sg.news.yahoo.com/un-rights-chief-horrified-mass-181544829.html |url-status=live }}</ref> A spokesperson for the [[U.N. High Commissioner for Human Rights]] described the discoveries, stating, "Some of them had their hands tied, which of course indicates serious violations of international human rights law and international humanitarian law, and these need to be subjected to further investigations".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Farge |first1=Emma |title=UN rights chief 'horrified' by mass grave reports at Gaza hospitals |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/un-rights-chief-horrified-by-mass-grave-reports-gaza-hospitals-2024-04-23/ |website=Reuters |access-date=24 April 2024 |archive-date=23 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240423182757/https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/un-rights-chief-horrified-by-mass-grave-reports-gaza-hospitals-2024-04-23/ |url-status=live }}</ref> [[William Schabas]], a Canadian expert on international human rights law, stated mass graves have "always been an indication that war crimes have been committed".<ref>{{cite web |title=Mass graves 'an indication that war crimes have been committed' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/21/israels-war-on-gaza-live-mother-child-among-killed-in-new-rafah-strike?update=2851884 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=24 April 2024 |archive-date=24 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240424023955/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/21/israels-war-on-gaza-live-mother-child-among-killed-in-new-rafah-strike?update=2851884 |url-status=live }}</ref>

=== Assassinations ===
Following the [[assassination of Ismail Haniyeh]], the [[Iraqi foreign ministry]] stated the killing was a "flagrant violation of international law and a threat to security and stability in the region".<ref>{{cite web |title=Iraq Says Hamas Chief Killing Could Threaten Region's Stability |url=https://www.barrons.com/news/iraq-says-hamas-chief-killing-could-threaten-region-s-stability-68a0ad6a?refsec=topics_afp-news |website=Barron's |publisher=Agence France Presse |access-date=18 August 2024}}</ref>

==Abuse and humiliation of detainees==
{{main|Torture during the Gaza war}}

{{See also|Palestinians in Israeli custody|Mass detentions in the Gaza war}}

Multiple pieces of video evidence depicting the [[Cruel, inhuman or degrading treatment|degrading treatment]] of Palestinian detainees has surfaced. One of the videos show Israeli soldiers in the occupied West Bank who were dragging and assaulting detainees after surrounding them. Many of the detainees had been stripped naked, having both their arms and feet bound, and beaten with the butts of rifles and trampled. Euro-Mediterranean Human Rights Monitor described this as a "flagrant violation of international laws related to the protection of civilians".<ref>{{cite web |date=1 November 2023 |title=Egregious acts of torture, abuse committed by Israeli army against Palestinian civilians in the West Bank |url=https://euromedmonitor.org/en/article/5906 |work=Euromed}}</ref>

Further video evidence shows Israeli soldiers transporting Palestinians from [[Ofer Prison]], all of whom are blindfolded and stripped completely naked.<ref>{{cite web|url= https://arn.ps/post/277763.html | title= ت الاحتلال ينقل أسرى من سجن عوفر وهم عراة |work=Ajeel}}</ref> In another video uploaded by an Israeli soldier, a blindfolded and bound Palestinian is shown kneeling on the ground. The soldier taunts him in Arabic, telling him "صباح الخير يا قحبة" (Good morning, whore) before repeatedly kicking and spitting on him.<ref>{{cite web |title=IDF soldiers film themselves abusing, humiliating West Bank Palestinians|date=1 November 2023 |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/idf-soldiers-film-themselves-abusing-humiliating-west-bank-palestinians/amp/ |work=The Times of Israel|first=Gianluca|last=Pacchiani|access-date=24 November 2023}}</ref> Human Rights Watch director, Omar Shakir, stated the blindfolding and stripping of Palestinian detainees represented a war crime.<ref>{{cite web |title=HRW says inhumane treatment of Palestinian detainees amounts to 'war crime' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/12/11/israel-hamas-war-live-who-decries-catastrophic-situation-in-gaza?update=2550195 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=12 December 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Both sides of the Israeli-Hamas war are being accused of war crimes|url=https://www.npr.org/2023/11/12/1212534838/both-sides-of-the-israeli-hamas-war-are-being-accused-of-war-crimes|access-date=12 February 2024|publisher=NPR|last=Northam|first=Jackie|date=12 November 2023}}</ref>

On 20 December 2023, [[Amnesty International]] called for an investigation into [[Mass detentions in the Gaza war|mass detentions]], disappearances, inhumane treatment, and detainee deaths.<ref name="detainees from Gaza"/> In February 2024, the ''BBC'' published a report detailing documented instances of Israeli soldiers abusing and humiliating Palestinian detainees. According to [[Mark Ellis (lawyer)|Mark Ellis]], an expert on [[International criminal law|international criminal tribunals]], the report showed possible violations of laws regarding [[Prisoner of war|prisoners of war]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Thomas |first1=Merlyn |title=Israeli soldier videos from Gaza could breach international law, experts say |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-68249962 |website=BBC |date=9 February 2024 |access-date=15 February 2024}}</ref> After the Israeli military dismissed one of the reservists shown in the video, Sir [[Geoffrey Nice]], an expert on war crimes, stated a wider investigation was needed beyond the dismissal.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Thomas |first1=Merlyn |title=Israel to act on soldier misconduct after BBC investigation |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-68277124 |website=BBC |date=12 February 2024 |access-date=15 February 2024}}</ref> In March 2024, the United Nations stated that Israel had detained and tortured its employees in Gaza, extracting [[forced confession]]s.<ref>{{cite web |title=UN Agency For Palestinians Says Israel Authorities Tortured Detained Staff |url=https://www.barrons.com/news/un-agency-for-palestinians-says-israel-authorities-tortured-detained-staff-e55739f8 |website=Barron's |publisher=Agence France Presse |access-date=6 March 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Diamond |first1=Jeremy |title=UN agency accuses Israel of detaining, coercing staffers into false confessions about ties to Hamas |url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/03/04/middleeast/un-israel-confessions-allegations-intl/index.html |website=CNN |date=4 March 2024 |access-date=6 March 2024}}</ref> A [[Bellingcat]] analysis found instances of a collection of images and videos showing the IDF degrading Palestinian detainees. [[Queen’s University Belfast]] war crimes professor Luke Moffett stated these showed potential war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Tirawi |first1=Younis |title=Social Media Posts Show Off Blindfolded and Bound Palestinian Detainees |url=https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2024/03/05/social-media-posts-show-off-blindfolded-and-bound-palestinian-detainees/ |website=Bellingcat |date=5 March 2024 |access-date=8 March 2024}}</ref> CNN reported of an Israeli military base in the [[Negev desert]] that functions as a detention center for Palestinians who are exposed to inhumane treatment.<ref name="u077">{{cite web | last=Qiblawi | first=Tamara | title=Israeli whistleblowers detail horror of shadowy detention facility for Palestinians | website=CNN | date=10 May 2024 | url=https://edition.cnn.com/2024/05/10/middleeast/israel-sde-teiman-detention-whistleblowers-intl-cmd/index.html | access-date=11 May 2024 | archive-date=10 May 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240510233624/https://edition.cnn.com/2024/05/10/middleeast/israel-sde-teiman-detention-whistleblowers-intl-cmd/index.html | url-status=live }}</ref> In July 2024, Amnesty International stated Israel needed to end the [[Administrative detention|indefinite detention]] of Palestinian prisoners without trial, stating it was a "flagrant violation of international law".<ref>{{cite web |title=Amnesty calls for end to Israel's 'incommunicado' detention of Gazans |url=https://www.newarab.com/news/israel-prison-incommunicado-detention-palestinians-must-end |website=The New Arab |access-date=20 July 2024}}</ref>

===Sexual violence===
{{main|Sexual and gender-based violence against Palestinians during the Gaza war}}

On February 19, 2024, a group of [[United Nations special rapporteur]]s published a report calling for an investigation into violations against Palestinian women and girls in Gaza and the West Bank by Israeli forces.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Borger |first=Julian |date=22 February 2024 |title=Claims of Israeli sexual assault of Palestinian women are credible, UN panel says |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/feb/22/claims-of-israeli-sexual-assault-of-palestinian-women-are-credible-un-panel-says |access-date=3 April 2024 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240410160540/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/feb/22/claims-of-israeli-sexual-assault-of-palestinian-women-are-credible-un-panel-says |archive-date=10 April 2024}}</ref> The report presented evidence of [[wartime sexual violence]] committed against them during the Gaza conflict, detailing how they endured inhumane treatment by the IDF, including being denied essential items such as menstrual products, food, and medicine. They were also subjected to physical abuse, including severe beatings, sexual assaults, threats of rape, and other forms of sexual violence.<ref>{{cite news |date=19 February 2024 |title=UN experts warn of Israeli violations against Palestinian women, girls |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/2/19/un-experts-warn-of-israeli-violations-against-palestinian-women-girls |work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]] |access-date=20 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240410143556/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/2/19/un-experts-warn-of-israeli-violations-against-palestinian-women-girls |archive-date=10 April 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=19 February 2024 |title=Rights experts call for probe into alleged violations against Palestinian women and girls |url=https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/02/1146667 |work=United Nations News |publisher=[[United Nations Department of Global Communications]] |access-date=20 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240317080119/https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/02/1146667 |archive-date=17 March 2024}}</ref> In addition, female detainees were stripped and searched by male Israeli soldiers.<ref name="ohchr.org">{{cite press release |date=19 February 2024 |title=Israel/oPt: UN experts appalled by reported human rights violations against Palestinian women and girls |url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2024/02/israelopt-un-experts-appalled-reported-human-rights-violations-against |location=Geneva |publisher=[[Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights]] |access-date=20 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240410182953/https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2024/02/israelopt-un-experts-appalled-reported-human-rights-violations-against |archive-date=10 April 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/global-health/terror-and-security/sexual-violence-against-palestinian-women-un-report/ |title=Sexual violence against Palestinian women 'may be higher than first thought', says UN expert |first=Maeve |last=Cullinan |date=21 February 2024 |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240410135606/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/global-health/terror-and-security/sexual-violence-against-palestinian-women-un-report/ |archive-date=10 April 2024}}</ref> The [[Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights|UN High Commissioner for Human Rights]] issued a press release on the same day, stating that Israeli troops had photographed female detainees in “degrading circumstances” and that the photos had been uploaded online.<ref name="ohchr.org"/><ref>{{cite news |last=Robertson |first=Nick |date=19 February 2024 |title=UN experts condemn 'credible' reports of executions, sexual assault by Israeli soldiers |url=https://thehill.com/policy/international/4477340-un-experts-reports-executions-sexual-assault-israeli-soldiers/ |access-date=22 February 2024 |work=[[The Hill (newspaper)|The Hill]] |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240409122432/https://thehill.com/policy/international/4477340-un-experts-reports-executions-sexual-assault-israeli-soldiers/ |archive-date=9 April 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=UN experts demand investigation into claims Israeli forces killed, raped and sexually assaulted Palestinian women and girls|website=[[CNN]]|date=20 February 2024|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/02/20/middleeast/israel-hamas-un-investigation-sexual-abuse-intl/index.html|access-date=20 February 2024|archive-date=20 February 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240220122416/https://www.cnn.com/2024/02/20/middleeast/israel-hamas-un-investigation-sexual-abuse-intl/index.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Reem Alsalem, the [[United Nations Special Rapporteur on Violence Against Women|UN Special Rapporteur on Violence Against Women]], criticized that sexual violence against Palestinians is often not reported and investigated. She stated, "Rape and other forms of sexual violence can constitute war crimes, crimes against humanity or a constitutive act with respect to genocide! It must stop!"<ref>{{cite web |title=UN special rapporteurs decry underreporting of sexual violence against Palestinians |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/24/israels-war-on-gaza-live-19-killed-as-israel-again-fires-on-aid-seekers?update=2795432 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=26 March 2024}}</ref>

[[Physicians for Human Rights-Israel]] also described the [[sexual abuse|sexual humiliation]] of detainees, including sexual insults and urination on prisoners.<ref>{{cite web |title=Cruel and systematic violations of Palestinian rights in Israeli prisons: Report |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/19/israels-war-on-gaza-live-food-trucks-surrounded-as-hunger-spreads-in-gaza?update=2718554 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=21 February 2024}}</ref> The Palestinian Prisoner's Society stated men had been subjected to severe sexual assault, including attempted rape and violating strip searches.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Al Tahhan |first1=Zena |title=Palestinian groups share testimonies of sexual assault, rape of prisoners |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/20/israels-war-on-gaza-live-un-fears-explosion-in-child-deaths-in-gaza?update=2720319 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=21 February 2024}}</ref>

In June 2024, a detailed and legally mandated investigative report by the [[Independent International Commission of Inquiry on the Occupied Palestinian Territory]] concluded that "The frequency, prevalence and severity of sexual and gender-based crimes perpetrated against Palestinians since 7 October across the Occupied Palestinian Territories (OPT) indicate that specific forms of Sexual and gender-based violence (SGBV) are part of Israeli Security Forces (ISF) operating procedures."<ref>{{Cite web |date=12 June 2024 |title=Israeli authorities, Palestinian armed groups are responsible for war crimes, other grave violations of international law, UN Inquiry finds |url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2024/06/israeli-authorities-palestinian-armed-groups-are-responsible-war-crimes |website=UN Human Rights Office}}</ref>

A June 2024 investigation by ''The New York Times'' detailed reports that Israeli interrogators at the [[Sde Teiman detention camp]] inserted hot metal sticks into detainees' anuses. One detainee reportedly died from the resulting injuries.<ref name="nytimes-prisoner-abuse">{{cite web |last1=Kingsley |first1=Patrick |last2=Shbair |first2=Bilal |title=Inside the Base Where Israel Has Detained Thousands of Gazans |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/06/06/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-detention-base.html |website=[[The New York Times]] |date=6 June 2024 |access-date=8 June 2024}}</ref> An April 2024 ''Haaretz'' investigation found that prisoners in [[Ktzi'ot Prison]] were routinely stripped and humiliated, and they were also deliberately struck in the testicles while undergoing naked checks with a metal detector.<ref name="haaretz-prisoner-abuse">{{cite web |last1=Levy |first1=Gideon |last2=Levac |first2=Alex |title=Palestinian Released From Israeli Prison Describes Beatings, Sexual Abuse and Torture |url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/twilight-zone/2024-04-28/ty-article-magazine/.premium/palestinian-released-from-israeli-prison-describes-beatings-sexual-abuse-and-torture/0000018f-15e9-d2e1-a7df-15efb6590000# |website=haaretz.com |publisher=Haaretz |access-date=8 June 2024}}</ref> In August 2024, a video emerged from the same detention camp depicting the [[gang rape]] of a prisoner.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Cordall |first=Simon Speakman |title='Everything is legitimate': Israeli leaders defend soldiers accused of rape |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/8/9/everything-is-legitimate-israeli-leaders-defend-soldiers-accused-of-rape |access-date=2024-12-28 |website=Al Jazeera |language=en}}</ref> At the same time, Ibrahim Salem, who appeared in one of the first leaked photos from Sde Teiman, was released after being held there for 52 days without charge.<ref name="ibrahim-salem">{{cite web|url=https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/raped-female-soldiers-palestinian-leaked-sde-teiman-photo-speaks-out|title='Raped by female soldiers': Palestinian in leaked Sde Teiman photo speaks out|last1=al-Hajjar|first1=Mohammed|last2=Durgham|first2=Nader|date=8 August 2024|work=[[Middle East Eye]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240808182030/https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/raped-female-soldiers-palestinian-leaked-sde-teiman-photo-speaks-out|archive-date=8 August 2024|url-status=live|access-date=9 August 2024}}</ref> He reported widespread torture, including by medical staff, as well as electrocution during interrogations, sexual abuse, constant beatings, forced stripping, genital grabbing, and frequent occurrences of rape committed by both male and female soldiers. Children were also subjected to rape.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2WKeKZ6Csro|title=Palestinian in leaked Sde Teiman photo speaks out|date=10 August 2024|work=[[Middle East Eye]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240811152052/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2WKeKZ6Csro|archive-date=11 August 2024|url-status=live|access-date=11 August 2024}}</ref><ref name="They told me">{{Cite web |last=Ebrahim |first=Nadeen |date=2024-08-25 |title='They told me to strip.' Former Palestinian detainee says he was sexually abused in an Israeli prison |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2024/08/25/middleeast/former-palestinian-detainee-sexually-abused-in-israeli-prison-mime-intl/index.html |access-date=2024-08-25 |website=[[CNN]] |language=en}}</ref> In one instance, a prisoner in his 40s was handcuffed and forced to bend over a desk while a female soldier inserted her fingers and other objects into his rectum. If the prisoner moved, a male soldier positioned in front of him would beat him and compel him to remain in that position. According to Salem, "Most of the prisoners will come out with rectal injuries [caused by the sexual assault]."<ref name="ibrahim-salem" /> In an interview with [[CNN]], Salem stated that Palestinians were transported "like animals" to Israeli prisons on trucks, and described being hit in the genitals with metal detectors, as well as raped with a baton.<ref name="They told me"/>

[[Save the Children Fund|Save the Children]] reported receiving credible reports of sexual violence from children who had been detained by the IDF.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-07-22 |title=Physical abuse, infectious disease spreading as conditions for Palestinian children in Israeli military detention deteriorate |url=https://www.savethechildren.net/news/physical-abuse-infectious-disease-spreading-conditions-palestinian-children-israeli-military |access-date=2024-12-28 |website=Save the Children International |language=en}}</ref>

In March 2025, the [[UN Human Rights Commission]] published a report on sexual and gender-based abuses perpetrated by Israel against the Palestinian people, which concluded that sexual abuse of Palestinians is "committed either under explicit orders or with implicit encouragement by Israel's top civilian and military leadership."<ref>{{Cite news |last=Gritten|first=David|date=2025-03-13 |title=UN experts accuse Israel of sexual violence and 'genocidal acts' in Gaza |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/clyr154314vo|work=[[BBC]] |language=en-GB}}</ref>

==Destruction of religious, cultural and historic sites==
{{Main|Destruction of cultural heritage during the Israeli invasion of the Gaza Strip}}[[File:Holy Family Church in Gaza City (Catholic Church) - interior.jpg|thumb|The [[Holy Family Church, Gaza|Holy Family Church]], one of the buildings damaged by Israel.]]
A report in early November 2023 listed over 100 significant [[cultural heritage]] sites with religious, cultural and historical importance that Israel had partly or completely destroyed.<ref name=heritage>{{cite web |title=Report on the Impact of the Recent War in 2023 on the Cultural Heritage in Gaza Strip - Palestine |url=https://www.heritageforpeace.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/Report-of-the-effects-of-the-last-war-of-2023-on-the-cultural-heritage-in-Gaza-Strip-Palestine-english.pdf?fbclid=IwAR1adISTNx0oAWoqXuYDF0lCoxruPnP5dBylyFG7C0JmfATOiy0ciEK3Gyk |website=Heritage for Peace |access-date=28 January 2024 |archive-date=14 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240114065536/http://www.heritageforpeace.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/Report-of-the-effects-of-the-last-war-of-2023-on-the-cultural-heritage-in-Gaza-Strip-Palestine-english.pdf?fbclid=IwAR1adISTNx0oAWoqXuYDF0lCoxruPnP5dBylyFG7C0JmfATOiy0ciEK3Gyk |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=libraries>{{cite news |last1=Chamaa |first1=Mohamad El |title=Gazans mourn loss of their libraries: Cultural beacons and communal spaces |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/11/30/gaza-library-palestinian-culture/ |newspaper=Washington Post |access-date=28 January 2024 |date=4 December 2023 |archive-date=29 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231229210059/https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/11/30/gaza-library-palestinian-culture/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=theart:2>{{cite news |title=Bombing of Gaza has damaged or destroyed more than 100 heritage sites, NGO report reveals |url=https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2023/11/28/bombing-of-gaza-has-damaged-or-destroyed-more-than-100-heritage-sites-ngo-report-reveals |access-date=28 January 2024 |work=The Art Newspaper - International art news and events |date=28 November 2023 |archive-date=28 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240128215553/https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2023/11/28/bombing-of-gaza-has-damaged-or-destroyed-more-than-100-heritage-sites-ngo-report-reveals |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name = gilad1>{{cite news |last1=Gilad |first1=Moshe |title=Bombing Historical Sites in Gaza:'Israel Is Destroying Everything Beautiful': The 13th century Great Omari Mosque, the Church of Saint Porphyrius, the excavation site at the ancient port: Alongside thousands of dead and hundreds of thousands of displaced, dozens of heritage sites in the Gaza Strip have been destroyed by Israeli bombardment |url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2023-12-26/ty-article-magazine/.premium/bombing-historical-sites-in-gaza-israel-is-destroying-everything-beautiful/0000018c-a565-df1f-a7bf-b7e53e8e0000 |access-date=28 January 2024 |work=Haaretz |date=26 December 2023 |language=en |archive-date=30 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231230131242/https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2023-12-26/ty-article-magazine/.premium/bombing-historical-sites-in-gaza-israel-is-destroying-everything-beautiful/0000018c-a565-df1f-a7bf-b7e53e8e0000 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=New report details 104 Gaza cultural landmarks destoyed or damaged |url=https://www.npr.org/2023/12/03/1216200754/gaza-heritage-sites-destroyed-israel |access-date=28 January 2024 |work=NPR |date=3 December 2023 |archive-date=27 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240127172320/https://www.npr.org/2023/12/03/1216200754/gaza-heritage-sites-destroyed-israel |url-status=live }}</ref>

In January 2024, the ''BBC'' has verified 74 cases where religious sites were damaged or destroyed, of which 72 were mosques and two were churches.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Kansara |first1=Reha |last2=Nour |first2=Ahmed |date=30 January 2024 |title=Israel-Gaza war: Counting the destruction of religious sites |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-67983018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240201054751/https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-67983018 |archive-date=1 February 2024 |access-date=1 February 2024 |website=BBC}}</ref> In October 2024, the Palestinian Authority's [[Ministry of Awqaf and Religious Affairs (Palestine)|Ministry of Awqaf and Religious Affairs]] in Gaza estimated that 814 mosques and three churches were destroyed since the war started and a further 148 mosques damaged with the repair costs of over 350 million dollars.<ref name="aje.io">{{Cite web |date=5 October 2024 |title=Israeli army destroys 814 mosques, 3 churches, 19 cemeteries |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/10/5/live-israel-resumes-beirut-bombing-as-lebanon-death-toll-passes-2000?update=3223479 |website=Al Jazeera}}</ref>

''[[The Nation]]'' wrote that the destruction of the [[Great Mosque of Gaza|Great Omari Mosque]] in particular, originally a fifth-century [[Christianity as the Roman state religion|Byzantine church]], was "a crime against cultural heritage. But more importantly... part of a campaign of total annihilation... a deliberate element of the Israeli campaign to erase all traces of Palestinian life.".<ref>{{cite news |last1=Wagner |first1=Kate |title=What Israel's Destruction of the Great Omari Mosque Means |url=https://www.thenation.com/article/world/great-omari-mosque-urbicide-gaza/ |access-date=28 January 2024 |date=24 January 2024 |archive-date=27 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240127063347/https://www.thenation.com/article/world/great-omari-mosque-urbicide-gaza/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

