Israel has damaged or destroyed at least 19 cemeteries across the Gaza Strip, in some cases, creating dirt roads across them or establishing military positions.<ref name="cnn1">{{cite web |last1=Diamond |first1=Jeremy |date=20 January 2024 |title=At least 16 cemeteries in Gaza have been desecrated by Israeli forces, satellite imagery and videos reveal |url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/01/20/middleeast/israel-gaza-cemeteries-desecrated-investigation-intl-cmd/index.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240120225627/https://www.cnn.com/2024/01/20/middleeast/israel-gaza-cemeteries-desecrated-investigation-intl-cmd/index.html |archive-date=20 January 2024 |access-date=21 January 2024 |website=CNN}}</ref><ref name="aje.io" />

The intentional destruction of religious sites without military necessity is a possible war crime.<ref>{{cite news |title=Satellite Imagery and Video Shows Some Gazan Cemeteries Razed by Israeli Forces |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/14/world/middleeast/gaza-cemeteries-damage-israel.html |access-date=16 December 2023 |work=The New York Times |date=14 December 2023 |archive-date=16 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231216001940/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/14/world/middleeast/gaza-cemeteries-damage-israel.html |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Destruction of Cemeteries |url=https://www.uscirf.gov/sites/default/files/2021-09/2021%20Factsheet%20-%20Destruction%20of%20Cemeteries.pdf |website=United States Commission on International Religious Freedom |access-date=22 December 2023 |archive-date=15 April 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220415164700/https://www.uscirf.gov/sites/default/files/2021-09/2021%20Factsheet%20-%20Destruction%20of%20Cemeteries.pdf |url-status=live}}</ref> The Ministry of Awqaf and Religious Affairs in Gaza stated that the Israeli military was guilty of [[Grave desecration|desecrating graves]], exhuming bodies and committing acts of violence against those who died, such as [[Body snatching|stealing their remains]] and mutilating them.<ref name="aje.io" />

On 21 December, bulldozers destroyed a cemetery in the Al-Saha neighborhood in eastern Gaza.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israeli forces bulldoze cemetery in eastern Gaza, crushing the dead |url=https://www.msn.com/en-in/news/world/israeli-forces-bulldoze-cemetery-in-eastern-gaza-crushing-the-dead/vi-AA1lQLMf#details |website=MSN |access-date=22 December 2023 |archive-date=22 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231222005956/https://www.msn.com/en-in/news/world/israeli-forces-bulldoze-cemetery-in-eastern-gaza-crushing-the-dead/vi-AA1lQLMf#details |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Allison |first1=Ismail |title=CAIR Calls Israel's New Ethnic Cleansing, Bulldozing of Bodies in Cemetery, Forced Starvation of Gaza Children the Latest 'Israeli War Crimes of the Day' |url=https://www.cair.com/press_releases/cair-calls-israels-new-ethnic-cleansing-bulldozing-of-bodies-in-cemetery-forced-starvation-of-gaza-children-the-latest-israeli-war-crimes-of-the-day/ |website=Council on American Islamic Relations |access-date=22 December 2023 |archive-date=22 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231222005956/https://www.cair.com/press_releases/cair-calls-israels-new-ethnic-cleansing-bulldozing-of-bodies-in-cemetery-forced-starvation-of-gaza-children-the-latest-israeli-war-crimes-of-the-day/ |url-status=live }}</ref>  On 6 January 2024, Palestinians in [[Tuffah]] reburied bodies after the Israeli army reportedly exhumed them and smashed their graves.<ref>{{cite web |title=Palestinians Rebury Bodies Exhumed From Gaza Cemetery |url=https://www.barrons.com/news/palestinians-rebury-bodies-exhumed-from-gaza-cemetery-78208338 |website=Barron's |publisher=Agence France Presse |access-date=7 January 2024 |archive-date=7 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240107002054/https://www.barrons.com/news/palestinians-rebury-bodies-exhumed-from-gaza-cemetery-78208338 |url-status=live }}</ref> Gazans in Khan Younis reported the Israeli army raided a cemetery and took corpses.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Talmazan |first1=Yuliya |title=Gazans in Khan Younis allege Israeli soldiers raided cemetery |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/news/world/live-blog/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-rcna134245/rcrd31194?canonicalCard=true |website=NBC News |date=18 January 2024 |access-date=18 January 2024 |archive-date=18 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240118035157/https://www.nbcnews.com/news/world/live-blog/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-rcna134245/rcrd31194?canonicalCard=true |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Hostilities in the Gaza Strip and Israel Flash Update #95 |url=https://www.ochaopt.org/content/hostilities-gaza-strip-and-israel-flash-update-95 |website=UNOCHA |date=17 January 2024 |publisher=United Nations |access-date=19 January 2024 |archive-date=19 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240119002114/https://www.ochaopt.org/content/hostilities-gaza-strip-and-israel-flash-update-95 |url-status=live }}</ref> The Khan Younis cemetery was reportedly bulldozed over, tombstones crushed, and the human remains were visible.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israeli military indicates it searched Gaza cemetery for bodies of hostages |url=https://news.sky.com/story/middle-east-crisis-us-uk-launch-strikes-houthi-targets-israel-gaza-hamas-12978800?postid=7088248#liveblog-body |website=Sky News |access-date=19 January 2024 |archive-date=19 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240119031436/https://news.sky.com/story/middle-east-crisis-us-uk-launch-strikes-houthi-targets-israel-gaza-hamas-12978800?postid=7088248#liveblog-body |url-status=live }}</ref> Muna Haddad, a human rights lawyer, stated, "What is happening is... considered a war crime of 'committing outrages upon personal dignity' under the [[Rome Statute]]."<ref name="cnn1" /> On 27 January 2024, Israeli forces escorted CNN into Gaza in an attempt to explain the destruction of [[Bani Suheila]] cemetery. According to the IDF a tunnel ran through the cemetery, but during the three hour visit, Israeli commanders failed to prove their claim.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/01/29/world/israel-cemetery-bani-suheila-intl/index.html|title=Israel claims a tunnel ran through this Gaza cemetery it destroyed. A visit to the site raised more questions than answers|first=Jeremy|last=Diamond|date=29 January 2024|publisher=CNN|access-date=11 February 2024|archive-date=1 February 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240201170334/https://www.cnn.com/2024/01/29/world/israel-cemetery-bani-suheila-intl/index.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Moreover, the IDF did not allow CNN to see any alleged entrance to the tunnel inside the cemetery, and later provided drone footage of two tunnel entrances, both located ''outside'' the cemetery. CNN broadcast footage of completely destroyed, and dug-up cemetery grounds.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Diamond |first1=Jeremy |title=IDF says they destroyed this Gaza graveyard because of Hamas activity. CNN can't find the evidence {{!}} CNN |url=https://www.cnn.com/videos/world/2024/01/29/idf-gaza-graveyard-destruction-diamond-pkg-lead-vpx.cnn |access-date=31 January 2024 |work=CNN |date=29 January 2024 |language=en |archive-date=31 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240131143452/https://www.cnn.com/videos/world/2024/01/29/idf-gaza-graveyard-destruction-diamond-pkg-lead-vpx.cnn |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 3 of October 2024, the Israeli air force bombed and destroyed a cemetery in Lebanon's Bashoura neighbourhood.<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 October 2024 |title=Bashoura cemetery damaged due to Israeli attack |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/10/3/live-beirut-bombed-as-hezbollah-battles-israeli-army-in-south-lebanon?update=3219058 |website=Al Jazeera}}</ref>

== Collective punishment ==
{{main|2023 Israeli blockade of the Gaza Strip}}
{{see also|Gaza humanitarian crisis (2023–present)|Structural abuse}}
{{Rquote|right|It is an entire nation out there that is responsible. It is not true this rhetoric about civilians not being aware, not involved. It's absolutely not true. They could have risen up. They could have fought against that evil regime which took over Gaza in a coup d'etat.|[[Isaac Herzog]]<ref>{{cite web|title='No Innocent Civilians in Gaza', Israel President Says as Northern Gaza Struggles to Flee Israeli Bombs|url=https://thewire.in/world/northern-gaza-israel-palestine-conflict|website=The Wire|access-date=19 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022011552/https://thewire.in/world/northern-gaza-israel-palestine-conflict|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
[[Collective punishment]] refers to punishing a whole group of people for an act committed by some of its members. Such punishment targets innocent people along with those who can be held responsible for the punished act.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Collective punishments |url=https://casebook.icrc.org/a_to_z/glossary/collective-punishments |access-date=2025-03-21 |website=ICRC Casebook}}</ref> In the Gaza war this refers to punishing all Palestinian civilians in Gaza for crimes committed by a number of Hamas militants.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Civilians in Gaza Must Not Be Collectively Punished for Atrocities Committed by Hamas, Speakers Tell Security Council, Urging Ceasefire |url=https://press.un.org/en/2023/sc15473.doc.htm |access-date=2025-03-21 |website=United Nations}}</ref> Collective punishment constitutes a war crime prohibited by [[treaty]] in both international and non-international armed conflicts.<ref name=":3" /><ref name=":4" /><ref>{{Cite web |title=Protocol Additional to the Geneva Conventions of 12 August 1949, and Relating to the Protection of Victims of Non-International Armed Conflicts (Protocol II) |url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/instruments-mechanisms/instruments/protocol-additional-geneva-conventions-12-august-1949-and-0 |access-date=2025-03-21 |website=OHCHR |language=en}}</ref>

Several actions taken by the Israeli army, including its [[October 2023 Israeli blockade of the Gaza Strip|blockade]] on electricity, food, fuel and water, were characterized as collective punishment, therefore a war crime.<ref name=":3">{{cite book |editor1-last=Garner |editor1-first=Bryan A. |editor1-link=Bryan A. Garner|title=Black's Law Dictionary|date=2007|publisher=Thomson West|location=St. Paul, MN|isbn=978-0314151995|page=280|edition=8th|quote=Collective punishment was outlawed in 1949 by the Geneva Convention.}}</ref><ref name=":4">{{cite book|last=Klocker|first=Cornelia|title=Collective Punishment and Human Rights Law: Addressing Gaps in International Law|publisher=[[Routledge]]}}</ref> Israel's president [[Isaac Herzog]] accused the residents of Gaza of [[collective responsibility]] for the war.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Reed|first1=John|last2=Srivastava|first2=Mehul|title=Israel tells 1.1mn people to leave northern Gaza|work=[[Financial Times]]|url=https://www.ft.com/content/8ea2374e-c21c-4232-bc69-615e36b26caa |access-date=13 October 2023 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20231013142041/https://www.ft.com/content/8ea2374e-c21c-4232-bc69-615e36b26caa |archive-date=13 October 2023}}</ref>{{efn|The ''Financial Times'' later silently deleted Herzog's quote from its article, cf. [https://archive.today/20231013224947/https://www.ft.com/content/8ea2374e-c21c-4232-bc69-615e36b26caa archive] copy of the article from the evening of 13 October.<ref>{{Cite news|last=El-Kurd|first=Mohammed|date=20 October 2023|title=Western Journalists Have Palestinian Blood on Their Hands|language=en-US|url=https://www.thenation.com/article/world/western-journalists-have-palestinian-blood-on-their-hands/|work=[[The Nation]]|access-date=21 October 2023|issn=0027-8378|archive-date=21 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231021072332/https://www.thenation.com/article/world/western-journalists-have-palestinian-blood-on-their-hands/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}<ref>{{cite web|last1=Blumenthal|first1=Paul|title=Israeli President Says There Are No Innocent Civilians In Gaza|url=https://news.yahoo.com/israeli-president-says-no-innocent-154330724.html|website=Y! News|publisher=[[HuffPost]]|access-date=13 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022011553/https://news.yahoo.com/israeli-president-says-no-innocent-154330724.html|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Doctors Without Borders]] international president [[Christos Christou (physician)|Christos Christou]] said millions of civilians in Gaza faced "collective punishment" due to Israel's blockade on fuel and medicine.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Regan|first1=Helen|title=Israel calls on 1.1 million Gazans to evacuate south in order UN warns is 'impossible'|url=https://www.cnn.com/2023/10/13/middleeast/israel-gaza-hamas-war-friday-intl-hnk/index.html|work=[[CNN]]|access-date=13 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022012054/https://www.cnn.com/2023/10/13/middleeast/israel-gaza-hamas-war-friday-intl-hnk/index.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Indiscriminate violence and the collective punishment of Gaza must cease|url=https://www.msf.org/indiscriminate-violence-and-collective-punishment-gaza-must-cease|website=[[Doctors Without Borders]]|access-date=13 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022012057/https://www.msf.org/indiscriminate-violence-and-collective-punishment-gaza-must-cease|url-status=live}}</ref>

In an interview with ''[[The New Yorker]]'', human rights expert Sari Bashi noted the historical uniqueness of Israeli officials openly admitting they are engaging in collective punishment.<ref>{{cite magazine|last1=Chotiner|first1=Isaac|title=The Humanitarian Catastrophe in Gaza|url=https://www.newyorker.com/news/q-and-a/the-humanitarian-catastrophe-in-gaza|magazine=[[The New Yorker]]|date=15 October 2023|access-date=16 October 2023|archive-date=16 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231016023052/https://www.newyorker.com/news/q-and-a/the-humanitarian-catastrophe-in-gaza|url-status=live}}</ref> On 18 October, UN Secretary-General António Guterres stated Hamas' attacks "cannot justify the collective punishment of the Palestinian people."<ref>{{cite web|title=UN's Guterres Says Hamas Attacks Do Not Justify 'Collective Punishment' Of Palestinians|url=https://www.barrons.com/news/un-s-guterres-says-hamas-attacks-do-not-justify-collective-punishment-of-palestinians-d56430f0|work=Barron's|agency=[[Agence France-Presse]]|access-date=18 October 2023|archive-date=18 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231018171445/https://www.barrons.com/news/un-s-guterres-says-hamas-attacks-do-not-justify-collective-punishment-of-palestinians-d56430f0|url-status=live}}</ref> On 24 October, Human Rights Watch criticized Israel's refusal to allow fuel or water into a Gaza, terming it a war crime.<ref>{{cite web |title=HRW slams Israel for committing war crimes against Palestinians |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/10/23/israel-hamas-war-live-hundreds-killed-israeli-strikes-gaza?update=2434221 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=24 October 2023 |archive-date=24 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231024213227/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/10/23/israel-hamas-war-live-hundreds-killed-israeli-strikes-gaza?update=2434221 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 29 October, Karim Ahmad Khan stated Israel's impeding aid to Gaza may constitute a crime under the [[International Criminal Court]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Impeding aid to Gaza may constitute crime under ICC jurisdiction |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/10/28/israel-hamas-war-live-invasion-under-way-as-gaza-cut-off-from-the-world?update=2447182 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=29 October 2023 |archive-date=29 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231029225458/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/10/28/israel-hamas-war-live-invasion-under-way-as-gaza-cut-off-from-the-world?update=2447182 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 7 December, Khan again stated "wilfully impeding relief supplies" may constitute a war crime under the Rome Statute.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Wintour |first1=Patrick |title=Washington faces UN showdown over fresh resolution for Gaza ceasefire |url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/07/washington-faces-showdown-over-fresh-un-resolution-for-gaza-ceasefire-us-israel |website=The Guardian |date=7 December 2023 |access-date=7 December 2023 |archive-date=7 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231207125502/https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/07/washington-faces-showdown-over-fresh-un-resolution-for-gaza-ceasefire-us-israel |url-status=live |ref=none}}</ref> On 20 January 2024, the IDF dropped leaflets with hostages' images on Rafah, stating, "Do you want to return home? Please make the call if you recognise one of them."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Al-Mughrabi |first1=Nidal |title=Fighting across Gaza as Israel drops leaflets seeking its hostages |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/fighting-across-gaza-israel-drops-leaflets-seeking-its-hostages-2024-01-20/ |website=Reuters |access-date=21 January 2024}}</ref> On 25 January 2024, the Gaza Health Ministry reported that Israeli troops had fired upon and killed twenty civilians seeking humanitarian aid in Gaza City.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Jobain |first1=Najib |title=Gaza's Health Ministry blames Israeli troops for deadly shooting as crowd waited for aid |url=https://apnews.com/article/israel-hamas-war-news-01-25-2024-e5592d58f88fd04a87363b0137025926 |website=Associated Press |date=25 January 2024 |access-date=26 January 2024 |archive-date=25 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240125211606/https://apnews.com/article/israel-hamas-war-news-01-25-2024-e5592d58f88fd04a87363b0137025926 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=U.N. slams Israel for deadly strike on Gaza shelter as war with Hamas leaves hospitals under siege |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/israel-hamas-war-gaza-idf-unrwa-shelter-khan-younis-hospitals-under-siege/ |website=CBS News |date=25 January 2024 |access-date=26 January 2024 |archive-date=26 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240126024701/https://www.cbsnews.com/news/israel-hamas-war-gaza-idf-unrwa-shelter-khan-younis-hospitals-under-siege/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 31 January 2024, ''Haaretz'' reported that Israeli army commanders were ordering troops to burn down and destroy unoccupied buildings in Gaza.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Kubovich |first1=Yaniv |title=Israeli Army Occupies Gaza Homes – Then Burns Them Down |url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2024-01-31/ty-article/.premium/israeli-army-occupies-gaza-homes-then-burns-them-down/0000018d-6021-d16e-a39f-7f3f01e30000 |website=Haaretz |date=31 January 2024 |access-date=2 February 2024 |archive-date=1 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240201165613/https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2024-01-31/ty-article/.premium/israeli-army-occupies-gaza-homes-then-burns-them-down/0000018d-6021-d16e-a39f-7f3f01e30000 |url-status=live }}</ref> According to Human Rights Watch: "Unlawful and wanton excessive destruction of property that is not militarily justified, is also a war crime."<ref>{{cite web |title=Deadly Attacks Kill, Injure Civilians, Destroy Homes |url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/03/18/ukraine-deadly-attacks-kill-injure-civilians-destroy-homes |website=Human Rights Watch |date=18 March 2022 |access-date=2 February 2024 |archive-date=4 April 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220404131119/https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/03/18/ukraine-deadly-attacks-kill-injure-civilians-destroy-homes |url-status=live }}</ref> On 16 April 2024, a spokesperson for the UN Human Rights Office stated, "Israel continues to impose unlawful restrictions on the entry and distribution of humanitarian assistance, and to carry out widespread destruction of civilian infrastructure".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Farge |first1=Emma |title=Israel still imposing 'unlawful' restrictions on Gaza aid, UN rights office says |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israel-still-imposing-unlawful-restrictions-gaza-aid-un-rights-office-says-2024-04-16/#:~:text=%22Israel%20continues%20to%20impose%20unlawful,reiterating%20calls%20for%20unfettered%20access. |website=Reuters |access-date=19 April 2024}}</ref> The Irish foreign minister [[Micheál Martin]] called Israel's actions "fully disproportionate and... a breach of humanitarian law in terms of the destruction of Gaza".<ref>{{cite news |title=Ireland accuses Israel of war crime in Gaza |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2024/04/22/israel-hamas-gaza-war-iran-latest-news-jerusalem-car-terror/ |website=The Telegraph |date=22 April 2024 |access-date=25 April 2024 |last1=Henderson |first1=Cameron |archive-date=25 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240425004003/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2024/04/22/israel-hamas-gaza-war-iran-latest-news-jerusalem-car-terror/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Water access===
As part of Israel's blockade on Gaza, water supplies from Israel were cut off.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Shurafa|first1=Wafaa|last2=Krauss|first2=Joseph|title=Gaza residents struggle to follow Israeli evacuation order amid critical water shortage|url=https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/gaza-residents-struggle-to-follow-israeli-evacuation-order-amid-critical-water-shortage|work=[[PBS Newshour]]|access-date=15 October 2023|archive-date=15 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231015020157/https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/gaza-residents-struggle-to-follow-israeli-evacuation-order-amid-critical-water-shortage|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last1=Mehta|first1=Lyla|last2=Nicol|first2=Alan|title=Cutting off water to Gaza is a war crime|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/19/cutting-off-water-to-gaza-is-a-war|website=The Guardian|date=19 October 2023|access-date=19 October 2023|archive-date=19 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231019171300/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/19/cutting-off-water-to-gaza-is-a-war|url-status=live}}</ref> Article 51 of the [[Berlin Rules on Water Resources]] bars combatants from removing water or [[Water supply network|water infrastructure]] to cause death or force its movement.<ref>{{cite web|title=Water and Armed Conflicts|url=https://casebook.icrc.org/case-study/water-and-armed-conflicts|website=Casebook|publisher=[[International Committee of the Red Cross]]|access-date=15 October 2023|archive-date=15 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231015200255/https://casebook.icrc.org/case-study/water-and-armed-conflicts|url-status=live}}</ref> The EU's chief diplomat [[Josep Borrell]] called Israel's cutting off water, electricity and food as "not in accordance with international law".<ref>{{cite news|last1=O'Leary|first1=Naomi|title=Israel's move to cut Gaza off from food and water is against international law, says EU|url=https://www.irishtimes.com/world/middle-east/2023/10/10/cutting-gaza-off-from-food-and-water-against-international-law-says-eu/|work=[[Irish Times]]|access-date=15 October 2023|archive-date=15 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231015185207/https://www.irishtimes.com/world/middle-east/2023/10/10/cutting-gaza-off-from-food-and-water-against-international-law-says-eu/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 14 October, the UNRWA announced Gaza no longer had clean drinking water, and two million people were at risk of death from dehydration.<ref>{{cite news|title=Water a 'matter of life and death' for Gaza after Israeli siege, says UN|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/10/14/water-a-matter-of-life-and-death-for-gaza-strip-says-un-agency|work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]]|access-date=15 October 2023|archive-date=14 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231014215043/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/10/14/water-a-matter-of-life-and-death-for-gaza-strip-says-un-agency|url-status=live}}</ref> On 15 October, Israel announced it had resumed supplying water to a single location in southern Gaza to "encourage" movement.<ref>{{Cite news|last1=Spiro|first1=Amy|last2=Magid|first2=Jacob|date=15 October 2023|title=Israel says it is restarting water supply to southern Gaza Strip|language=en-US|work=[[Times of Israel]]|url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/israel-says-it-is-restarting-water-supply-to-southern-gaza-strip/ |access-date=15 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231016002435/https://www.timesofisrael.com/israel-says-it-is-restarting-water-supply-to-southern-gaza-strip/ |archive-date=16 October 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Oliphant |first1=Roland |title=Israel resumes water supply to south of Gaza to encourage evacuation |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2023/10/15/israel-gaza-hamas-evacuation-water-supply-south-encourage/ |website=The Telegraph |date=15 October 2023 |access-date=21 February 2024 |archive-date=24 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324115256/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2023/10/15/israel-gaza-hamas-evacuation-water-supply-south-encourage/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Aid workers in Gaza refuted water was available.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Jobain|first1=Najib|last2=Kullab|first2=Samya|title=Water runs out at UN shelters in Gaza|url=https://abcnews.go.com/International/wireStory/water-runs-shelters-gaza-medics-fear-patients-israeli-103991022|work=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]]|access-date=16 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022012056/https://abcnews.go.com/International/wireStory/water-runs-shelters-gaza-medics-fear-patients-israeli-103991022|url-status=live}}</ref> By 16 October, civilians drank seawater and water contaminated with sewage to survive.<ref name="drinking salty water">{{cite news|last1=Al-Mughrabi|first1=Nidal|title=In Gaza, people resort to drinking salty water, garbage piles up|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/gaza-people-resort-drinking-salty-water-garbage-piles-up-2023-10-16/|work=[[Reuters]]|date=16 October 2023|access-date=16 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022012057/https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/gaza-people-resort-drinking-salty-water-garbage-piles-up-2023-10-16/|url-status=live}}</ref> In July 2024, [[Oxfam]] published a report titled ''Water War Crimes'' in which it started that Israel was "systematically weaponizing water against Palestinians" in violation of international law.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel Using Water As Weapon Of War As Gaza Supply Plummets By 94%, Creating Deadly Health Catastrophe |url=https://www.oxfam.org.uk/media/press-releases/israel-using-water-as-weapon-of-war-as-gaza-supply-plummets-by-94-creating-deadly-health-catastrophe-oxfam/ |website=Oxfam |date=18 July 2024 |access-date=28 July 2024}}</ref>

===Starvation===
{{main|Gaza Strip famine}}
Israel imposed a "complete siege" on Gaza in the first ten days of the war, due to alleged security concerns that weapons, fuel, and armaments would be transferred to Hamas in the guise of humanitarian aid.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|date=22 October 2023 |title=Israel denies humanitarian aid wasn't checked for weapons before entering Gaza |work=[[Times of Israel]] |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/israel-denies-humanitarian-aid-not-checked-for-weapons-before-entering-gaza/}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last1=Baruch |first1=Pnina Sharvit |last2=Caner |first2=Tammy |date=26 October 2023 |title=What are Israel's humanitarian obligations toward the civilians in Gaza? |url=https://www.inss.org.il/publication/israel-duties/ |access-date=14 November 2023 |website=[[The Institute for National Security Studies]]}}</ref> Israel later allowed the delivery of limited humanitarian aid following security checks.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|title=Live Updates: Current US assessment is Israel 'not responsible' for Gaza hospital blast, White House says |url=https://apnews.com/live/israel-hamas-war-live-updates |access-date=14 November 2023 |work=[[AP News]]}}</ref> Israel's restriction of the flow of food, fuel, water, and other humanitarian aid was criticized as a war crime by human rights organizations and termed a "targeted starvation campaign" by United Nations rights experts.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|title=Human Rights Watch: Gaza siege is a 'clear-cut war crime' |newspaper=[[The Irish Times]] |date=15 October 2023 |url=https://www.irishtimes.com/video/video/2023/10/15/human-rights-watch-gaza-siege-is-a-clear-cut-war-crime/ |ref={{sfnref|The Irish Times|2023}} |access-date=22 October 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=U.N. experts say Gaza children dying in Israeli "targeted starvation campaign" |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/u-n-experts-say-gaza-children-dying-in-israeli-targeted-starvation-campaign/ |website=CBS News |date=9 July 2024 |access-date=20 July 2024}}</ref>

[[Tom Dannenbaum]], co-director of the Center for International Law & Governance at the [[Fletcher School at Tufts University]], wrote that the order "commands the starvation of civilians as a method of warfare, which is a violation of international humanitarian law and a war crime".<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Dannenbaum |first=Tom |date=11 October 2023 |title=The Siege of Gaza and the Starvation War Crime |url=https://www.justsecurity.org/89403/the-siege-of-gaza-and-the-starvation-war-crime/ |access-date=22 October 2023 |work=Just Security}}</ref> [[Oxfam]] issued a statement that accused Israel of using starvation as a weapon of war, saying "[[International humanitarian law|International Humanitarian Law]] (IHL) strictly prohibits the use of starvation as a method of warfare and as the occupying power in Gaza, Israel is bound by IHL obligations to provide for the needs and protection of the population of Gaza".<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|date=25 October 2023 |title=Starvation used as a 'weapon of war' in Gaza amid Israeli siege: Oxfam |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/10/25/starvation-used-as-a-weapon-of-war-on-civilians-in-gaza-oxfam |access-date=27 October 2023 |publisher=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]] |ref={{sfnref |Al Jazeera |2023}}}}</ref> Oxfam further stated that [[Israeli airstrikes on municipal services in the Gaza Strip|attacks on civilian infrastructure]] were part of the crime of using starvation as a weapon of war.<ref>{{cite web |title=Oxfam condemns killing of water engineers in Gaza |url=https://www.oxfam.org/en/press-releases/oxfam-condemns-killing-water-engineers-gaza |website=Oxfam International |date=21 October 2024 |access-date=22 October 2024}}</ref>

Geoffrey S. Corn, Chair of Criminal Law and Director of the Center for Military Law and Policy at [[Texas Tech University School of Law]], and Sean Watts, professor in the Department of Law at the [[United States Military Academy at West Point]], write that sieges are subject to the same laws of war as other military tactics such as [[Distinction (law)|distinction]] and proportionality.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last1=Corn |first1=Geoff |last2=Watts |first2=Sean |title=Israel – Hamas 2023 Symposium – Siege Law and Military Necessity |publisher=[[United States Military Academy at West Point]] |url=https://lieber.westpoint.edu/siege-law-military-necessity/ |website=Articles of War |access-date=7 November 2023 |date=13 October 2023}}</ref> Watts previously wrote that Article 23 of the [[Fourth Geneva Convention]] "requires that parties to a conflict allow passage of a limited class of relief supplies for civilians...only if the parties are satisfied no advantage will result 'to the military efforts or economy of the enemy'", but that if the law is interpreted to allow "incidental" starvation of civilians proportionate to anticipated military advantage, it "reduces the rule's humanitarian effect, perhaps to the vanishing point".<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last1=Watts |first1=Sean |title=Siege Law |url=https://lieber.westpoint.edu/siege-law |website=Articles of War |publisher=[[United States Military Academy at West Point]] |access-date=5 January 2024 |date=4 March 2022}}</ref>

In March 2024, the [[European Union]]'s top diplomat, Josep Borrell, stated Israel was using starvation as a weapon of war.<ref>{{cite news |last1=James |first1=Gregory |title=Israel Gaza war: EU says starvation being used as a weapon |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-68550937 |website=BBC |date=13 March 2024 |access-date=16 March 2024 |archive-date=16 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240316071418/https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-68550937 |url-status=live }}</ref> Similarly, the U.N. High Commissioner for Human Rights, [[Volker Türk]], stated, "The extent of Israel’s continued restrictions on entry of aid into Gaza, together with the manner in which it continues to conduct hostilities, may amount to the use of starvation as a method of war, which is a war crime".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Tétrault-Farber |first1=Gabrielle |title=Israel's restrictions to Gaza aid may be war crime, says UN rights office |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israels-restrictions-gaza-aid-may-amount-war-crime-says-un-rights-office-2024-03-19/#:~:text=%22The%20extent%20of%20Israel's%20continued,for%20Human%20Rights%2C%20Volker%20Turk. |website=Reuters |access-date=22 March 2024}}</ref>

Human Rights Watch stated Israel was committing a war crime by using starvation as a method of warfare.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel: Starvation Used as Weapon of War in Gaza |url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/12/18/israel-starvation-used-weapon-war-gaza |website=Human Rights Watch |date=18 December 2023 |access-date=18 December 2023 |archive-date=10 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240110222554/https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/12/18/israel-starvation-used-weapon-war-gaza |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Alex de Waal]] stated it was the worst man-made [[Gaza Strip famine|famine]] in 75 years.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Nolen |first1=Stephanie |title=Looming Starvation in Gaza Shows Resurgence of Civilian Sieges in Warfare |work=The New York Times |date=11 January 2024 |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/11/health/gaza-israel-hunger-starvation.html |access-date=14 January 2024 |archive-date=13 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240113173728/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/11/health/gaza-israel-hunger-starvation.html |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Luis Moreno Ocampo]], the former chief prosecutor for the ICC, stated, "Stopping aid in particular to destroy civilian life – with intention to destroy a historical community – is genocide."<ref>{{cite web |title=Israeli incitement and aid blocking should be investigated: Former ICC prosecutor |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/6/israels-war-on-gaza-live-staggering-destruction-in-north-gaza-unrwa?update=2684111 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=7 February 2024 |archive-date=7 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240207044423/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/6/israels-war-on-gaza-live-staggering-destruction-in-north-gaza-unrwa?update=2684111 |url-status=live }}</ref> In April 2024, the United Nations human rights office stated Israel was placing "unlawful restrictions" on humanitarian aid.<ref>{{cite web |title=UN says Israel unlawfully restricting Gaza aid |url=https://www.voanews.com/a/un-says-israel-unlawfully-restricting-gaza-aid/7572020.html |website=VOA |date=16 April 2024 |access-date=27 April 2024 |archive-date=28 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240428000136/https://www.voanews.com/a/un-says-israel-unlawfully-restricting-gaza-aid/7572020.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

[[Euro-Mediterranean Human Rights Monitor|EuroMed Monitor]] described the situation as a war of starvation against civilians in the Gaza Strip. EuroMed noted living conditions had reached catastrophic levels by Israel cutting off all food supplies to the Northern half, and bombing and destroying factories, bakeries, food stores, water stations, and tanks throughout the entire enclave. EuroMed additionally noted Israel deliberately focused its attacks on targeting electrical generators and solar energy units, on which commercial facilities and restaurants depend, to maintain the minimum possible level of their work. Israel also targeted the agricultural areas east of Gaza, flour stores, and fishermen's boats, as well as relief organizations' centers, including those belonging to the UNRWA. As a result, over 90% of the children in Gaza suffered from varying health issues, including malnutrition, anemia, and weakened immunity.<ref>{{Cite web |date=5 November 2023 |title=Israel is Waging an Extensive War of Starvation against Gaza's Civilian Population [EN/AR] - occupied Palestinian territory {{!}} ReliefWeb |url=https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/israel-waging-extensive-war-starvation-against-gazas-civilian-population-enar |access-date=6 November 2023 |website=reliefweb.int |language=en |archive-date=10 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231110042658/https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/israel-waging-extensive-war-starvation-against-gazas-civilian-population-enar |url-status=live }}</ref> Israeli snipers reportedly targeted people waiting for humanitarian aid.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Abu Azzoum |first1=Tareq |title=Israel using starvation as 'weapon of war' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/18/israels-war-on-gaza-live-palestinians-fleeing-rafah-face-israeli-strikes?update=2716291 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=19 February 2024 |archive-date=18 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240218202937/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/18/israels-war-on-gaza-live-palestinians-fleeing-rafah-face-israeli-strikes?update=2716291 |url-status=live }}</ref>

The ICJ ruled as part of the interim measures that Israel facilitate the flow of aid and lessen humanitarian suffering in Gaza.<ref name="7V4Vi">{{Cite web|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/3/7/israels-blocking-of-aid-creating-apocalyptic-conditions-in-gaza|title=Israel's blocking of aid creating 'apocalyptic' conditions in Gaza|author=Al Jazeera Staff|website=Al Jazeera|access-date=1 May 2024|archive-date=16 March 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240316103101/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/3/7/israels-blocking-of-aid-creating-apocalyptic-conditions-in-gaza|url-status=live}}</ref> In its March 2024 interim ruling, the ICJ stated, "The court observes that Palestinians in Gaza are no longer facing only a risk of famine ... but that famine is setting in."<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/world-court-orders-israel-take-measures-ensure-food-gets-into-gaza-2024-03-28/|title=World court orders Israel to take action to address Gaza famine &#124; Reuters|website=[[Reuters]] }}</ref>

Aid groups complain about the level of aid, blaming harsh war conditions, strict inspections and limits on the number of crossing points while Israel says that the restrictions are necessary to ensure that weapons and supplies do not fall into the hands of Hamas.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/27/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-war-humanitarian-aid.html|title=Aid Flows to Gaza Are Rising, U.N. Says, but More Is Needed|first1=Isabel|last1=Kershner|first2=Raja|last2=Abdulrahim|first3=Adam|last3=Rasgon|first4=Troy|last4=Closson|work=The New York Times|date=27 April 2024|via=NYTimes.com|access-date=1 May 2024|archive-date=1 May 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240501141150/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/27/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-war-humanitarian-aid.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Three reports, a leaked internal State Department memorandum, an internal assessment by the U.S. Agency for International Development (USAID), and the report of the Independent Task Force on the Application of National Security Memorandum-20 to Israel, confirm that Israel's blocking of humanitarian aid has triggered the legal requirement to halt military aid.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://dawnmena.org/u-s-state-department-suspend-military-aid-to-israel-under-section-620i-of-the-foreign-assistance-act/|title=U.S. State Department: Suspend Military Aid to Israel Under Section 620I of the Foreign Assistance Act|date=27 April 2024|access-date=1 May 2024|archive-date=29 April 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240429172923/https://dawnmena.org/u-s-state-department-suspend-military-aid-to-israel-under-section-620i-of-the-foreign-assistance-act/|url-status=live}}</ref> A report from Refugees International revealed that Israeli authorities have "erected unnecessary hurdles, complicated logistical processes, and an unpredictable vetting system, rendering the inspection regime overwhelmingly burdensome with layers of bureaucracy and inspection and limited working hours".<ref name="7V4Vi" /> Israeli professor [[Neve Gordon]] wrote of Israel’s history of restricting food access in the Gaza Strip "controlling and managing the population through food insecurity."<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.democracynow.org/2024/4/4/neve_gordon_israel_palestine_hunger_gaza|title=The Road to Famine: Israel's History of Using Food Access as Weapon in Gaza|website=Democracy Now!|access-date=1 May 2024|archive-date=24 April 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240424230739/https://www.democracynow.org/2024/4/4/neve_gordon_israel_palestine_hunger_gaza|url-status=live}}</ref> The UN and Human Rights Watch said the Israeli government is using starvation of civilians as a method of warfare in the Gaza Strip, a war crime.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/12/18/israel-starvation-used-weapon-war-gaza|title=Israel: Starvation Used as Weapon of War in Gaza &#124; Human Rights Watch|date=18 December 2023|access-date=18 December 2023|archive-date=1 March 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240301021244/https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/12/18/israel-starvation-used-weapon-war-gaza|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/19/un-israeli-restrictions-gaza-food-aid-war-crime-hunger|title=UN says Israeli restrictions on Gaza food aid may constitute a war crime|first=Peter|last=Beaumont|date=19 March 2024|newspaper=The Guardian|access-date=1 May 2024|archive-date=10 May 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240510150211/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/19/un-israeli-restrictions-gaza-food-aid-war-crime-hunger|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Crop destruction ===
As of summer 2024, over 60% of Gaza's farmland had been damaged or destroyed.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Tabrizy |first1=Nilo |last2=Piper |first2=Imogen |last3=Berger |first3=Miriam |date=2024-05-03 |title=Israel's offensive is destroying Gaza's ability to grow its own food|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/interactive/2024/gaza-israel-agriculture-food-fisheries/ |access-date=2024-12-01 |newspaper=[[The Washington Post]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Haddad |first=Mohammed |title=How Israel destroyed Gaza's ability to feed itself |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/longform/2024/7/2/how-israel-destroyed-gazas-ability-to-feed-itself |access-date=2024-12-01 |website=Al Jazeera |language=en}}</ref> [[Crop destruction]] is considered a war crime under the [[Protocol I|Geneva conventions article 54]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://ihl-databases.icrc.org/en/ihl-treaties/api-1977/article-54/commentary/1987 |access-date=2024-12-01 |website=ihl-databases.icrc.org| title=Protocol Additional to the Geneva Conventions of 12 August 1949, and relating to the Protection of Victims of International Armed Conflicts (Protocol I), 8 June 1977.}}</ref> By November 2024 over 70% of farmland had been hit and over 90% of cattle, killed.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Burke |first1=Jason |last2=Tantesh |first2=Malak A. |date=2024-11-21 |title=Gaza food production 'decimated' with 70% of farmland hit, UN finds |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/21/gaza-food-production-decimated-70-per-cent-farmland-hit |access-date=2024-12-01 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref> 52.5% of agricultural wells and 44.3% of greenhouses have also been damaged.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Gaza: Geospatial data shows intensifying damage to cropland |url=https://www.fao.org/newsroom/detail/gaza-geospatial-data-shows-intensifying-damage-to-cropland/en |access-date=2024-12-01 |website=Newsroom |language=en}}</ref>

=== Violations of medical neutrality ===
{{see also|Attacks on health facilities during the Gaza war|Killing of health workers in the Gaza war}}
[[File:Palestine ambulance strike.png|thumb|right|upright=1|[[Palestine Red Crescent]] ambulance destroyed by an Israeli airstrike]]
Israel is alleged to have broken [[medical neutrality]], a war crime under the Geneva Conventions as hospitals are given special protection under international humanitarian law.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Le Poidevin|first1=Olivia|last2=Fleming-Farrell|first2=Niamh|last3=Jadah|first3=Malek|last4=Hamadi|first4=Ghadir|title=Hundreds of Palestinians killed in Israeli airstrike on Gaza hospital: Day 11 of the Hamas-Israel war|url=https://today.lorientlejour.com/article/1353474/biden-to-visit-israel-wednesday-iran-threatens-possible-pre-emptive-action-day-11-of-the-israel-hamas-war.html|website=L'Orient Today |date=17 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231019201203/https://today.lorientlejour.com/article/1353474/biden-to-visit-israel-wednesday-iran-threatens-possible-pre-emptive-action-day-11-of-the-israel-hamas-war.html |access-date=19 October 2023|archive-date=19 October 2023 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Doctors observe black day against Israeli atrocities in Gaza|url=https://tribune.com.pk/story/2441900/doctors-observe-black-day-against-israeli-atrocities-in-gaza|website=The Express Tribune |date=19 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231019201447/https://tribune.com.pk/story/2441900/doctors-observe-black-day-against-israeli-atrocities-in-gaza |access-date=19 October 2023|archive-date=19 October 2023 }}</ref> These attacks have been carried out in a manner that aid groups and international bodies are increasingly referring to as systematic.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/26/world/middleeast/gaza-israel-hospitals-medical-system.html|title=Israel's Military Campaign Has Left Gaza's Medical System Near Collapse|first1=Vivian|last1=Nereim|first2=Abu Bakr|last2=Bashir|work=The New York Times|date=26 April 2024|via=NYTimes.com|access-date=27 April 2024|archive-date=27 April 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240427122433/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/26/world/middleeast/gaza-israel-hospitals-medical-system.html|url-status=live}}</ref> According to Gaza officials, the IDF deliberately targeted ambulances and health facilities with airstrikes.<ref name="CBC HEALTH">{{cite news|last1=Basu|first1=Brishti|title=Health-care and relief workers killed in Gaza as humanitarian groups navigate full blockade|url=https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/health-workers-gaza-killed-1.6992828|work=[[Canadian Broadcasting Corporation|CBC]]|access-date=14 October 2023|archive-date=13 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231013221713/http://www.cbc.ca/news/world/health-workers-gaza-killed-1.6992828|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|title=Ambulances hit during Israeli air attack in Gaza|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/program/newsfeed/2023/10/14/ambulances-hit-during-israeli-air-attack-in-gazavideo-shows-the-moment-a-co|work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]]|access-date=14 October 2023|archive-date=14 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231014184414/https://www.aljazeera.com/program/newsfeed/2023/10/14/ambulances-hit-during-israeli-air-attack-in-gazavideo-shows-the-moment-a-co|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="AJ121023">{{cite web |last1=Abu Riash|first1=Abed|last2=Marsi|first2=Federica|title=Gaza medics say Israel targeting ambulances, health facilities |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/10/12/war-crime-gaza-medics-say-israel-targeting-ambulances-health-facilities |website=aljazeera |date=12 October 2023 |access-date=21 October 2023 |archive-date=22 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022010523/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/10/12/war-crime-gaza-medics-say-israel-targeting-ambulances-health-facilities |url-status=live }}</ref> In a statement, the Palestine Red Crescent demanded "accountability for this war crime".<ref name="AJ121023"/> The [[International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies]], UNRWA, and [[Medecins Sans Frontieres]] reported the deaths of their medical personnel.<ref name="ifrc-gaza">{{cite news|title=Eleven workers with UN refugee agency, five IFRC members killed in Gaza|website=[[Reuters]]|date=11 October 2023|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/nine-staffers-working-with-un-palestinian-refugee-agency-killed-air-strikes-gaza-2023-10-11/|access-date=11 October 2023|archive-date=11 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231011182301/https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/nine-staffers-working-with-un-palestinian-refugee-agency-killed-air-strikes-gaza-2023-10-11/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="AJ121023"/> On 14 October, the [[World Health Organization]] said the killing of health care workers and the destruction of health facilities "denies civilians the basic human right of life-saving health" and is prohibited by International Humanitarian Law.<ref name="Evacuation orders by Israel">{{cite web|title=Evacuation orders by Israel to hospitals in northern Gaza are a death sentence for the sick and injured|url=https://www.emro.who.int/media/news/evacuation-orders-by-israel-to-hospitals-in-northern-gaza-are-a-death-sentence-for-the-sick-and-injured.html|website=[[World Health Organization]]|access-date=14 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022011030/https://www.emro.who.int/media/news/evacuation-orders-by-israel-to-hospitals-in-northern-gaza-are-a-death-sentence-for-the-sick-and-injured.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Gaza: Forcing patients to flee hospitals a 'death sentence' warns WHO|url=https://news.un.org/en/story/2023/10/1142347|website=[[United Nations]]|date=14 October 2023|access-date=14 October 2023|archive-date=17 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231017075513/https://news.un.org/en/story/2023/10/1142347|url-status=live}}</ref> On 17 October, WHO stated 51 health facilities had been attacked by Israel.<ref>{{cite news|title=In Gaza's deadliest day, hospital strike kills about 500|url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/international/world-news/in-gazas-deadliest-day-hospital-strike-kills-about-500/articleshow/104506456.cms|website=[[The Economic Times]]|date=18 October 2023|access-date=18 October 2023|archive-date=18 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231018133423/https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/international/world-news/in-gazas-deadliest-day-hospital-strike-kills-about-500/articleshow/104506456.cms|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last1=Ortiz|first1=Jorge L.|last2=Bacon|first2=John|title=After Gaza hospital bombing kills hundreds, Israel and Hamas blame each other: Updates|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/world/2023/10/17/israel-hamas-war-live-updates/71212615007/|work=[[USA Today]]|access-date=18 October 2023|archive-date=18 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231018133436/https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/world/2023/10/17/israel-hamas-war-live-updates/71212615007/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 4 November, the Gaza Health Ministry stated 105 medical facilities had been deliberately targeted.<ref>{{cite web |title=105 medical facilities 'deliberately targeted' by Israeli forces: Health ministry |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/4/israel-hamas-war-live-20-dead-in-israeli-attack-on-school-ministry?update=2461707 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=4 November 2023 |archive-date=24 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324115326/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/4/israel-hamas-war-live-20-dead-in-israeli-attack-on-school-ministry?update=2461707 |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 21 October, the Ministry of Health noted Israel had attacked 69 health facilities, 24 ambulances, put 7 hospitals out of commission, and killed 37 medical staff.<ref>{{cite web|title=250 attacks on medical staff and health facilities: Health ministry|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/10/20/israel-gaza-war-live-hamas-releases-two-american-captives-from-gaza|website=Al Jazeera|access-date=21 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022180346/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/10/20/israel-gaza-war-live-hamas-releases-two-american-captives-from-gaza|url-status=live}}</ref> Health workers and aid groups said several hospitals in Gaza were hit by airstrikes and shelling. The [[Palestine Red Crescent Society]] accused Israel of "deliberately" carrying out airstrikes "directly around" Gaza's second-largest hospital, [[al-Quds Hospital]], in north Gaza, to force them to evacuate the facility. The World Health Organization (WHO) found it impossible to evacuate the hospital. According to CNN, even those who evacuated south have not been safe.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Paddison|first1=Laura|last2=Michaelis|first2=Tamar|last3=Dahman|first3=Ibrahim|last4=Tal|first4=Amir|last5=McCarthy|first5=Simone|title=Israeli troops advance in Gaza, hostage freed and 'impossible' hospital evacuation: What to know Monday |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2023/10/29/middleeast/israel-second-stage-war-ground-forces-gaza-sunday-hnk-intl/index.html |website=CNN |date=31 October 2023 |access-date=31 October 2023 |archive-date=6 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231106034840/https://edition.cnn.com/2023/10/29/middleeast/israel-second-stage-war-ground-forces-gaza-sunday-hnk-intl/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref> On 30 October 2023, a [[Turkish-Palestinian Friendship Hospital]], located in the south of Gaza, was struck by a "direct hit", causing damage and injuries.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel-Hamas war live: Israeli attacks near Gaza City |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/10/31/israel-hamas-war-live-israeli-air-attacks-continue-across-gaza |website=Al Jazeera |date=31 October 2023 |access-date=31 October 2023 |archive-date=29 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240129052657/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/10/31/israel-hamas-war-live-israeli-air-attacks-continue-across-gaza |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 3 November, an Israeli [[Al-Shifa ambulance airstrike|airstrike hit an ambulance convoy]] departing from [[al-Shifa Hospital]] carrying, according to a [[Palestinian Health Ministry]] spokesman, 15-20 critically injured patients.<ref name="niaha">{{cite news |url=https://www.newarab.com/news/israeli-strikes-hit-gazas-al-shifa-hospital-al-rashid-road |title=New Israeli airstrikes hit Al-Shifa hospital, al-Rashid road as Israel's bombardment of the Gaza Strip continues |publisher=The New Arab |access-date=4 November 2023 |archive-date=7 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231107192212/https://www.newarab.com/news/israeli-strikes-hit-gazas-al-shifa-hospital-al-rashid-road |url-status=live }}</ref> The Israeli military confirmed the strike, saying one of the ambulances was being used by a "Hamas terrorist cell", and was close to their position.<ref name="imcit">{{cite news |date=3 November 2023 |title=Israel strikes ambulance near Gaza hospital, 15 reported killed |work=[[Reuters]] |publisher= |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/health-ministry-gaza-says-israel-targeted-convoy-ambulances-leaving-al-shifa-2023-11-03/#:~:text=GAZA%2C%20Nov%203%20(Reuters),the%20south%20of%20the%20territory. |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231103235417/https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/health-ministry-gaza-says-israel-targeted-convoy-ambulances-leaving-al-shifa-2023-11-03/ |archive-date=3 November 2023}}</ref> In response, [[Yanis Varoufakis]] noted, "Even if the ambulance was carrying a Hamas overlord, bombing it violates the Geneva Convention."<ref>{{cite web |title=Even if the ambulance was carrying a Hamas overlord, bombing it violates the Geneva Convention. |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/4/israel-hamas-war-live-20-dead-in-israeli-attack-on-school-ministry?update=2460653 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=4 November 2023 |archive-date=24 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324115319/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/4/israel-hamas-war-live-20-dead-in-israeli-attack-on-school-ministry?update=2460653 |url-status=live }}</ref> UN chief António Guterres stated he was "horrified" by the attack.<ref>{{cite web |title=UN secretary-general 'horrified' by Israel's attack on ambulances |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/4/israel-hamas-war-live-20-dead-in-israeli-attack-on-school-ministry?update=2460796 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=4 November 2023 |archive-date=24 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324115126/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/4/israel-hamas-war-live-20-dead-in-israeli-attack-on-school-ministry?update=2460796 |url-status=live }}</ref>  In prior weeks, Israel had released an animated video stating Al-Shifa hospital contained a hidden, top-secret underground military center.<ref>{{Unbulleted list citebundle |{{cite news|last1=Carey|first1=Andrew|last2=John|first2=Tara|last3=Flower|first3=Kevin |title=Israel admits airstrike on ambulance near hospital that witnesses say killed and wounded dozens |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2023/11/03/middleeast/casualties-gazas-shifa-hospital-idf/index.html |access-date=4 November 2023 |work=CNN |date=3 November 2023 |language=en |archive-date=4 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231104002513/https://edition.cnn.com/2023/11/03/middleeast/casualties-gazas-shifa-hospital-idf/index.html |url-status=live }}|{{cite news |title=How Hamas uses hospitals as shields during war |url=https://nationalpost.com/news/hamas-hospitals-israel |access-date=4 November 2023 |archive-date=24 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324115321/https://nationalpost.com/news/hamas-hospitals-israel |url-status=live }}|{{cite news |last1=Bettini |first1=Daniel |title=Foreign journalists reveal Hamas' false front |url=https://www.ynetnews.com/articles/0,7340,L-4556016,00.html |access-date=4 November 2023 |work=Ynetnews |date=7 August 2014 |language=en |archive-date=4 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231104081743/https://www.ynetnews.com/articles/0,7340,L-4556016,00.html |url-status=live }}|{{cite news |last1=Beaumont |first1=Peter |title=What is a human shield and how has Hamas been accused of using them? |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/30/human-shield-israel-claim-hamas-command-centre-under-hospital-palestinian-civilian-gaza-city |access-date=4 November 2023 |work=The Guardian |date=30 October 2023 |archive-date=7 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231107212606/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/30/human-shield-israel-claim-hamas-command-centre-under-hospital-palestinian-civilian-gaza-city |url-status=live }}}}</ref> This was flatly denied, with Hamas stating Israel was using "prefabricated" evidence to pre-empt a military strike on a hospital.<ref>{{cite web |title=Hamas rejects Israeli claim over installations under al-Shifa hospital |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/10/27/hamas-rejects-israeli-claim-over-installations-under-al-shifa-hospital |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=4 November 2023 |archive-date=15 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231115182224/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/10/27/hamas-rejects-israeli-claim-over-installations-under-al-shifa-hospital |url-status=live }}</ref> Laws of war provide limited protections to medical facilities used in such capacities.<ref>{{cite web |title=Practice relating to Rule 28. Medical Units I. Treaties |url=https://ihl-databases.icrc.org/en/customary-ihl/v2/rule28 |website=International Order of the Red Cross |access-date=4 November 2023 |archive-date=4 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231104135422/https://ihl-databases.icrc.org/en/customary-ihl/v2/rule28 |url-status=live }}</ref> HRW stated the strikes were apparently unlawful and should be investigated as a possible war crime.<ref>{{cite web |title=Gaza: Israeli Ambulance Strike Apparently Unlawful |url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/11/07/gaza-israeli-ambulance-strike-apparently-unlawful |website=Human Rights Watch |date=7 November 2023 |access-date=14 November 2023 |archive-date=15 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231115152357/https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/11/07/gaza-israeli-ambulance-strike-apparently-unlawful |url-status=live }}</ref>

During the [[Siege of Gaza City]], Israeli snipers reportedly fired on the intensive care unit in Al-Quds Hospital, killing one person and wounding 28.<ref>{{cite web |url= https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/10/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-benjamin-netanyahu-gaza-fighting-pauses-un-palestine?CMP=share_btn_tw&page=with%3Ablock-654e637a8f08a95ef07ec2be#block-654e637a8f08a95ef07ec2be |title= One person killed, many children wounded after Israeli snipers target al-Quds hospital, according to Palestinian Red Crescent |work= The Guardian |access-date= 12 November 2023 |archive-date= 16 November 2023 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20231116152921/https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/10/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-benjamin-netanyahu-gaza-fighting-pauses-un-palestine?CMP=share_btn_tw&page=with%3Ablock-654e637a8f08a95ef07ec2be#block-654e637a8f08a95ef07ec2be |url-status= live }}</ref> Doctors in Al-Shifa Hospital reported snipers at the outskirts of the complex were firing at "any moving person".<ref>{{cite web | url= https://www.tbsnews.net/hamas-israel-war/who-loses-contact-gazas-al-shifa-hospital-737686 | title= WHO loses contact with Gaza's al-Shifa Hospital | work= Business Standard | date= 12 November 2023 | access-date= 12 November 2023 | archive-date= 12 November 2023 | archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20231112080718/https://www.tbsnews.net/hamas-israel-war/who-loses-contact-gazas-al-shifa-hospital-737686 | url-status= live }}</ref> [[Fabrizio Carbone]], the Middle East regional head of the International Committee of the Red Cross, stated Israel's attacks on al-Shifa Hospital could not continue, stressing patients and hospital staff should be "protected in line with the laws of war".<ref>{{cite web |title='Distressing' information coming from al-Shifa Hospital: ICRC |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/11/israel-hamas-war-live-pleas-for-help-as-israel-bombards-gaza-hospitals?update=2478828 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=11 November 2023 |archive-date=24 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324115330/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/11/israel-hamas-war-live-pleas-for-help-as-israel-bombards-gaza-hospitals?update=2478828 |url-status=live }}</ref> In response to the [[Al-Shifa Hospital siege]], Human Rights Watch stated Israel's actions against hospitals need to be investigated as war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Moran |first1=Mark |last2=Godfrey |first2=Paul |title=HRW: Israeli attacks on Gaza hospitals should be investigated as war crimes |url=https://www.upi.com/Top_News/World-News/2023/11/14/Israel-claims-evidence-of-Hamas-headquarters-in-Gaza-childrens-hospital/9471699948488/ |website=UPI |access-date=14 November 2023 |archive-date=14 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231114081653/https://www.upi.com/Top_News/World-News/2023/11/14/Israel-claims-evidence-of-Hamas-headquarters-in-Gaza-childrens-hospital/9471699948488/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Jennifer Cassidy, a legal expert at University of Oxford, stated Israel's siege on al-Shifa was a war crime "plain and simple".<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel's hospital raid 'a war crime plain and simple' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/15/israel-hamas-war-live-israel-says-it-plans-to-raid-al-shifa-ministry?update=2489446 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=15 November 2023 |archive-date=24 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324115621/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/15/israel-hamas-war-live-israel-says-it-plans-to-raid-al-shifa-ministry?update=2489446 |url-status=live }}</ref> Following an Israeli attack on [[Indonesia Hospital]], the Indonesian Foreign Minister called it a clear violation of international humanitarian law.<ref>{{cite web |title=Indonesia condemns Israeli 'attack' on Gaza hospital |url=https://www.jpost.com/breaking-news/article-774171 |website=The Jerusalem Post |date=20 November 2023 |access-date=20 November 2023 |archive-date=20 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231120142351/https://www.jpost.com/breaking-news/article-774171 |url-status=live }}</ref>
[[File:Cardiff Solidarity for Palestine protest, 25 November 2023 142309 (redacted).jpg|thumb|Photos of Palestinian healthcare workers killed during fighting in Gaza, 25 November 2023]]
On 18 November 2023, two people were killed while traveling in a clearly identified Doctors Without Borders evacuation convoy in Gaza City.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Robertson |first1=Nick |title=Doctors Without Borders: Attack on organization's convoy 'deliberate,' calling for investigation |url=https://thehill.com/policy/international/4338868-msf-attack-convoy-deliberate-demanding-investigation/#:~:text=On%20Nov.%2018%2C%20a%20convoy,the%20clinic%2C%20the%20organization%20said. |website=The Hill |date=2 December 2023 |access-date=3 December 2023 |archive-date=3 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231203012656/https://thehill.com/policy/international/4338868-msf-attack-convoy-deliberate-demanding-investigation/#:~:text=On%20Nov.%2018%2C%20a%20convoy,the%20clinic%2C%20the%20organization%20said. |url-status=live }}</ref> Doctors Without Borders termed it a "deliberate attack."<ref>{{cite web |title=MSF convoy attacked in Gaza: all elements point to Israeli army responsibility |url=https://www.msf.org/msf-convoy-attacked-gaza-all-elements-point-israeli-army-responsibility |website=Doctors Without Borders |access-date=3 December 2023 |archive-date=2 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231202223835/https://www.msf.org/msf-convoy-attacked-gaza-all-elements-point-israeli-army-responsibility |url-status=live }}</ref> On 16 December, the [[Euro-Mediterranean Human Rights Monitor]] called for an international investigation into Israeli war crimes at the Kamal Adwan Hospital.<ref>{{cite web |title=Urgent int'l investigation needed to probe Israeli war crimes after Palestinian civilians buried alive at Gaza's Kamal Adwan Hospital |url=https://euromedmonitor.org/en/article/6039/Urgent-int%E2%80%99l-investigation-needed-to-probe-Israeli-war-crimes-after-Palestinian-civilians-buried-alive-at-Gaza%E2%80%99s-Kamal-Adwan-Hospital |website=Euro-Med Human Rights Monitor |access-date=17 December 2023 |archive-date=16 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231216224752/https://euromedmonitor.org/en/article/6039/Urgent-int%E2%80%99l-investigation-needed-to-probe-Israeli-war-crimes-after-Palestinian-civilians-buried-alive-at-Gaza%E2%80%99s-Kamal-Adwan-Hospital |url-status=live }}</ref> On 17 January 2024, Israeli fire damaged the Jordanian field hospital, leading the Jordanian army to call it a "flagrant breach of international law".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Barbakh |first1=Arafat |title=Israel presses southern Gaza assault, Jordan decries damage to hospital |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/jordan-says-southern-gaza-hospital-badly-damaged-by-israeli-shelling-nearby-2024-01-17/#:~:text=The%20Jordanian%20army%20said%20it,cell%22%20next%20to%20the%20hospital. |website=Reuters |access-date=18 January 2024}}</ref> On 19 January, Jordan stated Israel had "deliberately" targeted the hospital.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Arraf |first1=Jane |title=Jordan accuses Israel of deliberately targeting its Gaza field hospital |url=https://www.npr.org/2024/01/19/1225623652/jordan-field-hospital-gaza-israel |website=NPR |date=19 January 2024 |access-date=20 January 2024 |archive-date=20 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240120025517/https://www.npr.org/2024/01/19/1225623652/jordan-field-hospital-gaza-israel |url-status=live }}</ref> The World Health Organization stated on 24 January it had recorded 660 Israel attacks on healthcare facilities, calling them "a flagrant violation of international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite news | title=Israel continues to target health institutions in Gaza, says WHO regional director | url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jan/24/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-us-military-strikes-houthi-rebels-yemen-red-sea-israel-gaza-war-hamas-hostages?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-65b11bf28f0898882cc4fbfe#block-65b11bf28f0898882cc4fbfe | website=The Guardian | date=24 January 2024 | access-date=25 January 2024 | last1=Chao-Fong | first1=Léonie | last2=Sedghi | first2=Amy | last3=Belam | first3=Martin | last4=Ahmad | first4=Reged | archive-date=25 January 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240125000009/https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jan/24/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-us-military-strikes-houthi-rebels-yemen-red-sea-israel-gaza-war-hamas-hostages?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-65b11bf28f0898882cc4fbfe#block-65b11bf28f0898882cc4fbfe | url-status=live }}</ref> On 31 January, Doctors Without Borders stated Israel had conducted "systematic attacks on health facilities" which they stated was unprecedented for their organization.<ref>{{cite web |title=Facing a 'massacre' in Gaza, MSF laments limited ability to help |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20240131-facing-a-massacre-in-gaza-msf-laments-limited-ability-to-help |website=France24 |date=31 January 2024 |access-date=31 January 2024 |archive-date=31 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240131205209/https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20240131-facing-a-massacre-in-gaza-msf-laments-limited-ability-to-help |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 8 February 2024, the Palestinian Red Crescent accused the IDF of deliberately killing one of their paramedics.<ref>{{cite web |title=PRCS: Killing of paramedic was 'deliberate' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/8/israels-war-on-gaza-live-us-says-space-for-truce-deal-israel-vows-war?update=2691193 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=9 February 2024 |archive-date=8 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240208114341/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/8/israels-war-on-gaza-live-us-says-space-for-truce-deal-israel-vows-war?update=2691193 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 11 February, the Red Crescent accused the IDF of deliberately targeting and killing two of their paramedics sent to rescue [[Killing of Hind Rajab|Hind Rajab]], calling the killing a war crime.<ref>{{cite web |title=Attacking paramedics a 'war crime': Red Crescent |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/11/israels-war-on-gaza-live-leaders-warn-of-catastrophe-if-rafah-invaded?update=2701166 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=11 February 2024 |archive-date=11 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240211215058/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/11/israels-war-on-gaza-live-leaders-warn-of-catastrophe-if-rafah-invaded?update=2701166 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=The Palestine Red Crescent Society renews its calls to the international community to ensure the protection of its personnel and facilities and to provide a safe humanitarian space |url=https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/palestine-red-crescent-society-renews-its-calls-international-community-ensure-protection-its-personnel-and-facilities-and-provide-safe-humanitarian-space-enar |website=ReliefWeb |date=12 February 2024 |publisher=Palestine Red Crescent Society |access-date=19 February 2024 |archive-date=24 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324115621/https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/palestine-red-crescent-society-renews-its-calls-international-community-ensure-protection-its-personnel-and-facilities-and-provide-safe-humanitarian-space-enar |url-status=live }}</ref> In response to an Israeli attack at the [[Al-Aqsa Hospital]] on 31 March 2024, WHO chief [[Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus]] stated, "The ongoing attacks and militarisation of hospitals must stop. International humanitarian law must be respected."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Abualouf |first1=Rushdi |last2=Wright |first2=George |title=Journalists injured in al-Aqsa hospital air strike |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-68704280 |website=BBC |date=31 March 2024 |access-date=7 April 2024}}</ref> In May 2024, the Palestinian Red Crescent stated an Israeli attack on their ambulances near Rafah was a war crime.<ref>{{cite web |title=PRCS says killing of medics in south Gaza 'war crime' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/5/30/israels-war-on-gaza-live-no-safe-shelter-as-dozens-killed-in-rafah?update=2936480 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=8 June 2024}}</ref> Following the attack, WHO stated, "Health workers are protected under international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite web |title=WHO mourns 2 Red Crescent paramedics slain in Rafah |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/5/31/israels-war-on-gaza-live-unrelenting-nightmare-for-weary-palestinians?update=2938462 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=9 June 2024}}</ref> In June 2024, the UN Human Rights Office discussed the [[Killing of health workers in the Gaza war|killing of health workers in Gaza]], stating, "These killings have occurred against the backdrop of systematic attacks on hospitals and other medical facilities in violation of the laws of war".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Ngendakumana |first1=Pierre Emmanuel |title=500 medical workers killed during Israel's military assault on Gaza, UN says |url=https://www.politico.eu/article/500-healthcare-workers-killed-during-israel-military-assault-on-gaza-hospital-un-charity-says/ |website=Politico |date=26 June 2024 |access-date=4 July 2024}}</ref> In July 2024, the government of Turkey stated that images showing Israel using the [[Turkish-Palestinian Friendship Hospital]] as a military base indicated violations of international humanitarian law and threatened to take Israel to court.<ref>{{cite web |title=Turkey 'threatens' Israel with legal action after army uses Gaza hospital as base |url=https://www.newarab.com/news/turkey-threatens-israel-after-army-uses-gaza-hospital-base |website=The New Arab |access-date=26 July 2024}}</ref>

In October 2024, a UN inquiry accused Israel of committing serious violations of international law during the conflict, including attacks on medical personnel and facilities.<ref>
*{{cite press release|url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2024/10/un-commission-finds-war-crimes-and-crimes-against-humanity-israeli-attacks|title=UN Commission finds war crimes and crimes against humanity in Israeli attacks on Gaza health facilities and treatment of detainees, hostages|date=10 October 2024|agency=[[Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights]]|archive-url=https://archive.today/20241012003905/https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2024/10/un-commission-finds-war-crimes-and-crimes-against-humanity-israeli-attacks|archive-date=12 October 2024|url-status=live|access-date=12 October 2024}}
*{{cite web|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/10/10/un-inquiry-accuses-israel-of-deliberately-hitting-gaza-health-facilities|title=UN inquiry accuses Israel of crime of 'extermination' in Gaza|date=10 October 2024|work=[[Al Jazeera]]|archive-url=https://archive.today/20241011095557/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/10/10/un-inquiry-accuses-israel-of-deliberately-hitting-gaza-health-facilities|archive-date=11 October 2024|url-status=live|access-date=12 October 2024}}
*{{cite web|url=https://edition.cnn.com/2024/10/11/middleeast/un-israel-war-crimes-gaza-health-system-intl/index.html|title=UN inquiry accuses Israel of 'crime of extermination' through deliberate destruction of Gaza's health care system|last1=Kennedy|first1=Niamh|last2=Darwish|first2=Muhammad|date=11 October 2024|work=[[CNN]]|archive-url=https://archive.today/20241012174219/https://edition.cnn.com/2024/10/11/middleeast/un-israel-war-crimes-gaza-health-system-intl/index.html|archive-date=12 October 2024|url-status=live|access-date=12 October 2024}}
*{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c2lnw2gvllxo|title=UN accuses Israel of war crimes over attacks on Gaza hospitals|last=Foulkes|first=Imogen|date=10 October 2024|work=[[BBC]]|archive-url=https://archive.today/20241011105921/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c2lnw2gvllxo|archive-date=11 October 2024|url-status=live|access-date=12 October 2024}}
*{{cite web|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/un-inquiry-accuses-israel-crime-extermination-destruction-gaza-health-system-2024-10-10/|title=UN inquiry accuses Israel of seeking to destroy Gaza healthcare system|last=Farge|first=Emma|date=10 October 2024|work=[[Reuters]]|archive-url=https://archive.today/20241010193354/https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/un-inquiry-accuses-israel-crime-extermination-destruction-gaza-health-system-2024-10-10/|archive-date=10 October 2024|url-status=live|access-date=12 October 2024}}</ref> The inquiry alleged that Israeli actions contributed to the collapse of Gaza's healthcare system, citing restrictions on medical evaluations and damage to healthcare infrastructure.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel has 'concerted policy to destroy Gaza healthcare system': Independent UN report |url=https://news.un.org/en/audio/2024/10/1156281 |website=UN News |date=30 October 2024 |access-date=3 November 2024}}</ref>

==== Rafah humanitarian convoy attacks ====
{{main|Rafah paramedic massacre}}
In March 2025, the United Nations said that Israeli troops killed 15 Palestinian aid workers in southern Gaza and buried them in a [[Gaza Strip mass graves|mass grave]]. On March 23, the PRCS said it lost contact with an ambulance sent to the scene of an Israeli airstrike. A convoy sent to retrieve the medics subsequently went missing as well.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Shurafa |first1=Wafaa |last2=Keath |first2=Lee |last3=Khaled |first3=Fatima |title=Israeli troops killed 15 Palestinian medics and buried them in a mass grave, UN says |url=https://apnews.com/article/gaza-medics-killed-israel-ambulances-f34b6ecc985d9127265a400bd52c72b7 |website=Associated Press |date=31 March 2025 |access-date=31 March 2025}}</ref><ref name="Tondo0331">{{cite web |last1=Tondo |first1=Lorenzo |last2=Tantesh |first2=Malak |last3=Borger |first3=Julian |title=Israel killed 15 Palestinian paramedics and rescue workers one by one, says UN |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/mar/31/israel-killed-15-palestinian-paramedics-and-rescue-workers-one-by-one-says-un |website=The Guardian |date=31 March 2025 |access-date=31 March 2025}}</ref> The IDF claimed that it fired on "suspicious vehicles" that were driving with their lights off. However, video taken by one of the men killed by Israel showed clearly marked ambulances driving with both headlights and flashing emergency lights.<ref>{{cite web |last1=McKernan |first1=Bethan |title=Phone footage appears to contradict Israeli account of killing of Gaza medics |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/apr/05/phone-footage-appears-to-contradict-israeli-account-of-killing-of-gaza-paramedics |website=The Guardian |access-date=5 April 2025}}</ref> The U.N. said that it was prevented from accessing the site where the medics went missing for several days. On March 29, one of the bodies was found and 14 more were recovered the next day, buried alongside their emergency vehicles.<ref name="Tondo0331"/> According to eyewitness accounts, some of the bodies were found with their hands or legs tied and appeard to have been shot in the head.<ref name="Tondo0401">{{cite web |last1=Tondo |first1=Lorenzo |last2=Tantesh |first2=Malak |last3=Borger |first3=Julian |title=Palestinian paramedics shot by Israeli forces had hands tied, eyewitnesses say |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/apr/01/palestinian-paramedics-shot-by-israeli-forces-had-hands-tied-eyewitnesses-say |website=The Guardian |access-date=1 April 2025}}</ref> According to an [[United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs|OCHA]] spokesperson, "The available information indicates that the first team was killed by Israeli forces on 23 March, and that other emergency and aid crews were struck one after another over several hours as they searched for their missing colleagues."<ref name="Tondo0331" /> The Gaza health ministry claimed, "They were executed, some of them handcuffed and had sustained head and chest injuries. They were buried in a deep hole to prevent their identities from being identified."<ref name="Tondo0401" />

===Protected status===
Israel alleges medical facilities are used to store weapons and have been used as a base of fire, and that hospitals' special protection is lost if that is the case.<ref name="CNNHospitalSchoolTunnel">{{cite news |title=Israel shows CNN an underground tunnel between a school and hospital in Gaza |url=https://edition.cnn.com/videos/world/2023/11/13/cnn-inside-gaza-hospital-israel-defense-forces-hamas-robertson-pkg-src-vpx.cnn |access-date=15 November 2023 |date=14 November 2023 |language=en |archive-date=24 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231124095513/https://edition.cnn.com/videos/world/2023/11/13/cnn-inside-gaza-hospital-israel-defense-forces-hamas-robertson-pkg-src-vpx.cnn |url-status=live }}</ref> However, the IDF has not presented hard evidence to support their claims.<ref name="Israeli military">{{cite web |title=Israeli military: Gaza hospitals risk losing protection |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/14/israel-hamas-war-live-israeli-attacks-displace-700000-children-in-gaza?update=2487009 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=15 November 2023 |archive-date=15 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231115025856/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/14/israel-hamas-war-live-israeli-attacks-displace-700000-children-in-gaza?update=2487009 |url-status=live }}</ref> Israel also does not have the power to unilaterally decide if a hospital has lost protected status.<ref name="Israeli military"/> According to International Criminal Court prosecutor Karim Khan, the [[Burden of proof (law)|bar for evidence]] that a hospital, school, or place of worship is being used for military purposes is very high.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Khan |first1=Karim |title=We are witnessing a pandemic of inhumanity: to halt the spread, we must cling to the law |url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/nov/10/law-israel-hamas-international-criminal-court-icc |website=The Guardian |date=10 November 2023 |access-date=15 November 2023 |archive-date=14 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231114230514/https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/nov/10/law-israel-hamas-international-criminal-court-icc |url-status=live }}</ref> The burden of proof also lays with the Israelis.<ref name="hospitals have special protection">{{cite web |last1=Debre |first1=Isabel |title=In wars, hospitals have special protection under international law. How does that apply in Gaza? |url=https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/in-wars-hospitals-have-special-protection-under-international-law-how-does-that-apply-in-gaza#:~:text=International%20humanitarian%20law%20lends%20hospitals,of%20the%20Red%20Cross%20said. |website=PBS |date=12 November 2023 |access-date=15 November 2023 |archive-date=15 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231115025853/https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/in-wars-hospitals-have-special-protection-under-international-law-how-does-that-apply-in-gaza#:~:text=International%20humanitarian%20law%20lends%20hospitals,of%20the%20Red%20Cross%20said. |url-status=live }}</ref> Jessica Wolfendale, an expert in military ethics at [[Case Western Reserve University]], stated that even if Israel had been able to prove Shifa concealed a military operation, international law remains in place, as, "Steps need to be taken to protect the innocent."<ref name="hospitals have special protection"/> A hospital attack is also still illegal under international law if it harms civilians disproportionately to the military objective.<ref name="hospitals have special protection"/>

Ardi Imseis, an international law expert at [[Queen's University at Kingston]], stated, "Until such time that the Israelis provide proof that it has been converted into a military object, the civilian nature of the object does not change."<ref>{{cite web |title=What does the Geneva Convention say about the protection of civilians inside hospitals? |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/15/israel-hamas-war-live-israel-says-it-plans-to-raid-al-shifa-ministry?update=2487375 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=15 November 2023 |archive-date=24 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324115623/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/15/israel-hamas-war-live-israel-says-it-plans-to-raid-al-shifa-ministry?update=2487375 |url-status=live }}</ref> Human Rights Watch stated, "The Israeli government has put forward no evidence that would justify stripping hospitals of their special protections."<ref>{{cite web |title=Gaza's hospitals under 'sustained, systematic assault': HRW |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/15/israel-hamas-war-live-israel-says-it-plans-to-raid-al-shifa-ministry?update=2487320 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=15 November 2023 |archive-date=24 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324115720/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/15/israel-hamas-war-live-israel-says-it-plans-to-raid-al-shifa-ministry?update=2487320 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Sullivan |first1=Helen |last2=Chao-Fong |first2=Léonie |last3=Banfield-Nwachi |first3=Mabel |last4=Livingstone |first4=Helen |date=17 November 2023 |title=Human Rights Watch (HRW) have said images released by Israel showing what it said were weapons found inside Gaza's al-Shifa hospital were not sufficient to justify the hospital's status as protected by the laws of war. |website=The Guardian |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/16/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-biden-ceasefire-israel-criticises-un-humanitarian-pauses?page=with:block-655641f58f08d1d922ef829e |access-date=18 November 2023 |archive-date=18 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231118095841/https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/16/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-biden-ceasefire-israel-criticises-un-humanitarian-pauses?page=with:block-655641f58f08d1d922ef829e |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Israel's attacks on hospitals 'should be investigated as war crimes': HRW |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/11/14/israels-attacks-on-hospitals-should-be-investigated-as-war-crimes-hrw |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=15 November 2023 |archive-date=14 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231114224711/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/11/14/israels-attacks-on-hospitals-should-be-investigated-as-war-crimes-hrw |url-status=live }}</ref> The [[OHCHR]] stated, "Even if Israel contends that a medical facility has lost its protection... it must nevertheless comply with the principles of precautions and proportionality."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Parvaz |first1=D. |title=Searching for the remains of hostages, Israeli forces raid another Gaza hospital |url=https://www.npr.org/2024/02/16/1231942329/israel-hamas-war-gaza-nasser-hospital-khan-younis#:~:text=%22Even%20if%20Israel%20contends%20that,said%20in%20a%20statement%20Thursday. |website=NPR |date=16 February 2024 |access-date=17 February 2024 |archive-date=17 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240217004117/https://www.npr.org/2024/02/16/1231942329/israel-hamas-war-gaza-nasser-hospital-khan-younis#:~:text=%22Even%20if%20Israel%20contends%20that,said%20in%20a%20statement%20Thursday. |url-status=live }}</ref>

==Targeting of journalists==
{{See also|Killing of journalists in the Gaza war|List of journalists killed in the Gaza war}}
[[File:Hossam Shabat.jpg|thumb|210px|[[Al Jazeera]]'s Gaza correspondent [[Hossam Shabat]] was assassinated by Israel on 24 March 2025]]
On 1 November 2023, [[Reporters Without Borders]] (RSF) asked the [[International Criminal Court]] (ICC) to begin a priority war crimes investigation into the killing of nine journalists.<ref>{{cite web |title=Media watchdog files war crimes complaint with ICC |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/1/israel-hamas-war-live-anger-grows-over-israeli-attack-on-gaza-refugee-camp?update=2453874 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=1 November 2023}}</ref> RSF noted that of the 41 journalists killed in the first month of the conflict, 36 among them were Palestinian reporters killed by Israeli strikes in the Gaza Strip.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel/Palestine war: 41 journalists, more than one a day, killed in first month of Israel-Palestine war |url=https://rsf.org/en/israelpalestine-war-41-journalists-more-one-day-killed-first-month-israel-palestine-war |website=Reporters Without Borders |date=7 November 2023 |access-date=8 November 2023}}</ref>

[[Jodie Ginsberg]], the president of the [[Committee to Protect Journalists]], called for an ICC investigation into the killing of journalists in Gaza, stating the killings "appear to have been targeted".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Martin |first1=Michel |title=Number of journalists killed in Gaza since Oct. 7 attacks called unprecedented loss |url=https://www.npr.org/2023/12/19/1220210900/number-of-journalists-killed-in-gaza-since-oct-7-attacks-called-unprecedented-lo |website=NPR |access-date=20 December 2023}}</ref> On 27 January 2024, the [[International Federation of Journalists]] wrote an open-letter to Benjamin Netanyahu and Yoav Gallant stating they would take Israel to court if it did not comply with the [[International Court of Justice]] (ICJ) order to avoid targeting journalists.<ref>{{cite web |title=IFJ will take Israel to court if journalists are targeted |url=https://www.ifj.org/media-centre/news/detail/article/ifj-will-take-israel-to-court-if-journalists-are-targeted |website=International Federation of Journalists |date=27 January 2024 |access-date=28 January 2024}}</ref> In February 2024, the deputy director of the International Federation of Journalists stated, "There appears to have been a systematic campaign to kill and terrify and maim journalists in Gaza".<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel carrying out campaign to 'terrify' journalists in Gaza: Advocate |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/13/israels-war-on-gaza-live-jordans-king-urges-ceasefire-in-biden-meeting?update=2705425 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=15 February 2024}}</ref>

On 13 February 2024, [[Al Jazeera Media Network|Al Jazeera]] stated Israel had attacked two of its journalists in Gaza. They called it "a full-fledged crime added to Israel's crimes against journalists, and a new part in the series of the deliberate targeting of Al Jazeera's journalists".<ref>{{cite web |title=Statement: Al Jazeera condemns Israeli army's 'deliberate targeting' of its correspondent in Rafah, Ismail Abu Omar |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/13/israels-war-on-gaza-live-jordans-king-urges-ceasefire-in-biden-meeting?update=2705289 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=15 February 2024}}</ref> A representative from [[Media Defence]] stated, "Journalists are civilians so they are entitled to all the protections that civilians should have in times of conflict".<ref>{{cite web |title=Journalists entitled to protections as civilians in times of conflict: Legal network |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/13/israels-war-on-gaza-live-jordans-king-urges-ceasefire-in-biden-meeting?update=2705296 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=15 February 2024}}</ref> The director of the [[International Press Institute]] stated, "We see journalists clearly targeted… Our organisation has been monitoring press freedom for almost 75 years and this is the worst attack we have seen on journalists in any conflict".<ref>{{cite web |title=Journalists 'clearly targeted' in Israel's war on Gaza: IPI |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/13/israels-war-on-gaza-live-jordans-king-urges-ceasefire-in-biden-meeting?update=2705188 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=15 February 2024}}</ref>

Following the Israeli killing of [[Samer Abu Daqqa]], ''[[Al Jazeera Media Network|Al Jazeera]]'' stated it was referring the incident to the ICC.<ref>{{cite web |title=Al Jazeera to refer journalist Samer Abudaqa's killing to ICC |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/12/16/al-jazeera-to-refer-journalist-samer-abudaqas-killing-to-icc |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=17 December 2023}}</ref> In June 2024, a [[Forbidden Stories]] investigation into Israel's killing of journalists suggested that some of the killings were deliberate.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Zerrouky |first1=Madjid |last2=Abreu |first2=Mariana |last3=Layan |first3=Eloïse |last4=Delpuech |first4=Aïda |title=How Israel targets journalists in Gaza: 'The press vest now puts us in danger' |url=https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2024/06/25/how-israel-targets-journalists-in-gaza-the-press-vest-now-puts-us-in-danger_6675653_4.html |website=Le Monde |date=25 June 2024 |access-date=4 July 2024}}</ref> The investigation further found that Israeli tanks were likely responsible for an attack on the [[Agence France Press]] building in Gaza, described by investigators as "likely targeted".<ref>{{cite web |title=Media probe finds Israeli tank fire likely hit AFP Gaza office |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20240625-media-probe-finds-israeli-tank-fire-likely-hit-afp-gaza-office |website=France24 |date=25 June 2024 |access-date=4 July 2024}}</ref> In September 2024, RSF stated there were 31 credible cases where journalists were directly targeted by the Israeli army.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Salhani |first1=Justin |title=Israel is deliberately targeting journalists in Gaza: Experts |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/9/23/israel-is-deliberately-targeting-journalists-in-gaza-experts |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=6 October 2024}}</ref>

===Killing of Issam Abdallah===
{{see also|Issam Abdallah#Death}}
[[File:Reuters Journalist Issam Abdullah killed by a targeted IDF missile strike (53335018159).jpg|thumb|200px|A protestor holding up a sign of [[Issam Abdallah]] during mass demonstrations in London, 29 October 2023]]
RSF conducted a preliminary investigation into the killing of [[Issam Abdallah]], a [[Reuters]] photojournalist killed in Lebanon. They found that the strike on a clearly marked vehicle marked "Press" was purposely targeted and that the fire had come from Israel.<ref>{{cite web | title=RSF video investigation into the death of Reuters reporter Issam Abdallah in Lebanon: the journalists' vehicle was explicitly targeted | website=RSF | date=29 October 2023 | url=https://rsf.org/en/rsf-video-investigation-death-reuters-reporter-issam-abdallah-lebanon-journalists-vehicle-was | access-date=9 November 2023}}</ref> An investigation by the [[Agence France Press]] found Abdallah's killing was used with tank shells of Israeli origin and were deliberate and targeted.<ref>{{cite web |title=Journalists killed and injured in Lebanon: AFP investigation points to Israeli army strike |url=https://www.afp.com/en/agency/press-releases-newsletter/journalists-killed-and-injured-lebanon-afp-investigation-points-israeli-army-strike |website=Agence France Press |date=7 December 2023 |access-date=7 December 2023}}</ref> Amnesty International stated the attack was a likely war crime and that "Israel must not be allowed to kill and attack journalists with impunity."<ref>{{cite web |title=Lebanon: Israel's attack on seven journalists was a likely war crime - new investigation |url=https://www.amnesty.org.uk/press-releases/lebanon-israels-attack-seven-journalists-was-likely-war-crime-new-investigation |website=Amnesty International |access-date=7 December 2023}}</ref> Human Rights Watch stated the attack was apparently deliberate and constitutes a war crime.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel: Strikes on Journalists in Lebanon Apparently Deliberate |url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/12/07/israel-strikes-journalists-lebanon-apparently-deliberate#:~:text=Two%20Israeli%20strikes%20on%20a,were%20firing%20on%20were%20civilians. |website=Human Rights Watch | date=7 December 2023 |access-date=7 December 2023}}</ref> A study by the [[Netherlands Organisation for Applied Scientific Research]] found it likely "that a Merkava tank, after firing two tank rounds, also used its machine gun against the location of the journalists".<ref>{{cite web |title=Israeli tank in 'likely scenario' fired machine gun at reporters after deadly shelling, report finds |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2024/03/08/israeli-tank-in-likely-scenario-fired-machine-gun-at-reporters-after-deadly-shelling-report-finds.html#:~:text=“It%20is%20considered%20a%20likely,fire%20could%20not%20be%20established.” |website=CNBC | date=8 March 2024 |publisher=Reuters |access-date=9 March 2024}}</ref>

A February 2024 report by the [[United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon]] concluded that an Israeli tank killed Abadallah when it fired at "clearly identifiable journalists", and that this broke international law.<ref name=Bassam>{{cite news |last1=Gauthier-Villars |first1=David |last2=Bassam |first2=Laila |last3=Perry |first3=Tom |title=Israeli tank strike killed 'clearly identifiable' Reuters reporter - UN report |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israeli-tank-strike-killed-clearly-identifiable-reuters-reporter-un-report-2024-03-13/ |access-date=14 March 2024 |work=[[Reuters]] |date=14 March 2024}}</ref> The report "assessed that there was no exchange of fire across the [[Blue Line (withdrawal line)|Blue Line]] at the time of the incident", with no records of any exchange of fire across the border for the 40 minutes before the tank firing.<ref name=Bassam/> The Israel Defense Forces responded to the United Nations report by claiming that Hezbollah attacked them, so tank fire was used to retaliate.<ref name=Bassam/> The report concluded that the attack was a violation of [[UNSCR 1701]] and international law.<ref>{{cite news |title=Israel broke international law with tank shelling that killed journalist, UN finds |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/13/israel-broke-international-law-journalist-killed?CMP=twt_b-gdnnews |website=The Guardian | date=13 March 2024 |access-date=18 March 2024}}</ref>

== Forced evacuation ==
{{main|Gaza Strip evacuations}}
[[File:The return of displaced Palestinians from the south to the northern Gaza Strip.jpg|thumb|Return of displaced Palestinians from the south to the northern Gaza Strip during the [[January 2025 Gaza war ceasefire|ceasefire]] in January 2025]]
On 13 October, the Israeli army ordered the [[2023 Gaza Strip evacuations|evacuation]] of 1.1&nbsp;million people from north Gaza, saying that they needed to separate the civilian population from the militants embedded among them, and that the population would be allowed to return after the war.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Debre|first1=Isabel|title=Israel orders evacuation of 1 million in northern Gaza in 24 hours|url=https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/israel-orders-evacuation-of-1-million-in-northern-gaza-in-24-hours|work=[[PBS News]]|access-date=13 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022011029/https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/israel-orders-evacuation-of-1-million-in-northern-gaza-in-24-hours|url-status=live}}</ref> Gazan officials initially asked residents to ignore the order, with the [[Interior Minister of the Gaza Strip|Interior Ministry]] stating Israel sought to "displace us once again from our land".<ref>{{Unbulleted list citebundle |{{cite web |last1=Batrawy |first1=Aya |last2=Sullivan |first2=Becky |title=Gazans flee their homes after an Israeli evacuation order but have few places to go |url=https://www.npr.org/2023/10/13/1205672587/israel-warns-evacuate-northern-gaza |website=NPR |date=13 October 2023 |access-date=26 October 2023 |archive-date=26 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231026012822/https://www.npr.org/2023/10/13/1205672587/israel-warns-evacuate-northern-gaza |url-status=live }}|{{Cite news |date=13 October 2023 |title=Hamas tells Gaza residents to stay put as Israel ground offensive looms |language=en |work=Reuters |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/hamas-tells-gaza-residents-stay-home-israel-ground-offensive-looms-2023-10-13/ |access-date=26 October 2023 |archive-date=13 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231013165455/https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/hamas-tells-gaza-residents-stay-home-israel-ground-offensive-looms-2023-10-13/ |url-status=live }}|{{Cite web |last=Sharon |first=Itamar |date=14 October 2023 |title=IDF says it's completing preparations to strike Gaza 'from air, sea and land' |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/idf-says-its-completing-preparations-to-attack-gaza-from-air-sea-and-land/ |access-date=26 October 2023 |website=The Times of Israel |language=en-US |archive-date=14 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231014232648/https://www.timesofisrael.com/idf-says-its-completing-preparations-to-attack-gaza-from-air-sea-and-land/ |url-status=live }}}}</ref> The evacuation was characterized as a [[population transfer|forcible transfer]] by [[Jan Egeland]], a Norwegian diplomat involved with the [[Oslo Accord]].<ref name="Gazans stream south">{{cite news|last1=Srivastava|first1=Mehul|title=Gazans stream south to seek shelter from Israeli bombardment|url=https://www.ft.com/content/eb4717fc-432e-4251-b778-7a365f8de825?accessToken=zwAGB63wDZbYkdPrRxf8Qy5CUdO3eHo2X43oJQ.MEQCIQDcwGudDMv5bHMEEl000xy4DPGx7c0vFLiArY6aUdpF2AIfL1wVgRM8vtVUAlUm6FxWr3LlBBJD1XlhZAq_ln33rw&sharetype=gift&token=37a455ea-c676-4b2f-9449-fbbae0077868|work=[[Financial Times]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231014132458/https://www.ft.com/content/eb4717fc-432e-4251-b778-7a365f8de825?accessToken=zwAGB63wDZbYkdPrRxf8Qy5CUdO3eHo2X43oJQ.MEQCIQDcwGudDMv5bHMEEl000xy4DPGx7c0vFLiArY6aUdpF2AIfL1wVgRM8vtVUAlUm6FxWr3LlBBJD1XlhZAq_ln33rw&sharetype=gift&token=37a455ea-c676-4b2f-9449-fbbae0077868 |access-date=14 October 2023 |archive-date=14 October 2023}}</ref> Egeland stated, "There are hundreds of thousands of people fleeing for their life — [that is] not something that should be called an evacuation. It is a forcible transfer of people from all of northern Gaza, which according to the Geneva Convention is a war crime."<ref name="Gazans stream south"/> UN Special rapporteur [[Francesca Albanese]] warned of a mass [[ethnic cleansing]] in Gaza.<ref name="OHCHR102023">{{cite web|title=UN expert warns of new instance of mass ethnic cleansing of Palestinians, calls for immediate ceasefire|url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2023/10/un-expert-warns-new-instance-mass-ethnic-cleansing-palestinians-calls|website=UN Human Rights Office of the High Commissioner|access-date=14 October 2023|archive-date=14 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231014150546/https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2023/10/un-expert-warns-new-instance-mass-ethnic-cleansing-palestinians-calls|url-status=live}}</ref> Israeli historian [[Raz Segal]] termed it a "textbook case of [[genocide]]."<ref>{{cite web|last1=Segal|first1=Raz|title=A Textbook Case of Genocide|url=https://jewishcurrents.org/a-textbook-case-of-genocide|website=[[Jewish Currents]]|access-date=14 October 2023|archive-date=14 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231014034453/https://jewishcurrents.org/a-textbook-case-of-genocide|url-status=live}}</ref> The action was condemned by the UN, Doctors Without Borders, [[UNICEF]], and the [[International Rescue Committee|IRC]].<ref>{{Unbulleted list citebundle|{{Cite web|title=WHO pleads for immediate reversal of Gaza evacuation order to protect health and reduce suffering|url=https://www.who.int/news/item/13-10-2023-who-pleads-for-immediate-reversal-of-gaza-evacuation-order-to-protect-health-and-reduce-suffering|access-date=14 October 2023|website=www.who.int|language=en|archive-date=13 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231013232108/https://www.who.int/news/item/13-10-2023-who-pleads-for-immediate-reversal-of-gaza-evacuation-order-to-protect-health-and-reduce-suffering|url-status=live}}|{{cite web|title=MSF: Israeli order to evacuate northern Gaza 'outrageous'|website=[[Doctors Without Borders]]|date=13 October 2023|url=https://www.doctorswithoutborders.org/latest/msf-israeli-order-evacuate-northern-gaza-outrageous|ref={{sfnref |Doctors Without Borders - USA |2023}}|access-date=14 October 2023|archive-date=13 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231013220725/https://www.doctorswithoutborders.org/latest/msf-israeli-order-evacuate-northern-gaza-outrageous|url-status=live}}|{{Cite web|title=Time is running out for children in Gaza—UNICEF|url=https://www.unicef.org/press-releases/time-running-out-children-gazaunicef|access-date=14 October 2023|website=www.unicef.org|language=en|archive-date=14 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231014103535/https://www.unicef.org/press-releases/time-running-out-children-gazaunicef|url-status=live}}|{{Cite web|title=Occupied Palestinian Territory: The IRC calls for protection of civilians and upholding of International Humanitarian Law|url=https://www.rescue.org/press-release/occupied-palestinian-territory-irc-calls-protection-civilians-and-upholding|archive-date=14 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231014042335/https://www.rescue.org/press-release/occupied-palestinian-territory-irc-calls-protection-civilians-and-upholding |date=14 October 2023 |access-date=14 October 2023|website=www.rescue.org|language=en}}}}n</ref>

On 14 October, the World Health Organization issued a statement condemning Israel's order to evacuate 22 hospitals in northern Gaza, calling it a "death sentence".<ref>{{cite news|last1=Thomas|first1=Steff Danielle|title=WHO condemns Israel's Gaza evacuation order as 'death sentence' for sick, injured|url=https://thehill.com/policy/international/4256422-who-condemns-israel-gaza-evacuation-order/|work=[[The Hill (newspaper)|The Hill]]|access-date=14 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022011035/https://thehill.com/policy/international/4256422-who-condemns-israel-gaza-evacuation-order/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Evacuation orders by Israel to hospitals in northern Gaza are a death sentence for the sick and injured |url=https://www-who-int.translate.goog/news/item/14-10-2023-evacuation-orders-by-israel-to-hospitals-in-northern-gaza-are-a-death-sentence-for-the-sick-and-injured?_x_tr_sl=fa&_x_tr_tl=en&_x_tr_hl=en&_x_tr_pto=wapp |website=World Health Organization |date=14 October 2023 |access-date=22 October 2023 |archive-date=22 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022174722/https://www-who-int.translate.goog/news/item/14-10-2023-evacuation-orders-by-israel-to-hospitals-in-northern-gaza-are-a-death-sentence-for-the-sick-and-injured?_x_tr_sl=fa&_x_tr_tl=en&_x_tr_hl=en&_x_tr_pto=wapp |url-status=live }}</ref> Doctors noted both the southern Gaza Strip's lack of hospital beds and the impossibility of transporting patients, such as [[2023 Gaza Strip preterm births|newborns in incubators]] and patients on [[ventilators]].<ref>{{Unbulleted list citebundle|{{Cite news |last=Tétrault-Farber |first=Gabrielle |date=17 October 2023 |title=Attack on Gaza hospital 'unprecedented' in scale, WHO says |language=en |work=Reuters |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/attack-gaza-hospital-unprecedented-scale-who-says-2023-10-17/ |url-status=live|access-date=18 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231017223550/https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/attack-gaza-hospital-unprecedented-scale-who-says-2023-10-17/ |archive-date=17 October 2023}}|{{Cite news|last=Abdulrahim |first=Raja |date=15 October 2023 |title=Gaza's Hospitals Face 'Impossible' Choices With Israel Evacuation Order |language=en-US |work=[[The New York Times]]|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/15/world/middleeast/israel-gaza.html |url-status=live |access-date=18 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231018020440/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/15/world/middleeast/israel-gaza.html#:~:text=Since%20last%20Saturday%2C%20at%20least,for%20the%20sick%20and%20wounded. |archive-date=18 October 2023 |issn=0362-4331}}|{{Cite web |date=17 October 2023 |title=UN chief 'horrified' by strike on Gaza hospital, as warring sides blame each other {{!}} UN News|url=https://news.un.org/en/story/2023/10/1142472|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231018041701/https://news.un.org/en/story/2023/10/1142472 |archive-date=18 October 2023 |access-date=18 October 2023 |website=news.un.org |language=en}}|{{cite news|last1=Abdel-Baqui |first1=Omar |last2=Jones |first2=Rory |last3=AbdulKarim |first3=Fatima |date=17 October 2023 |title=Blast at Gaza Hospital Kills More Than 500, Palestinian Officials Say |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]]|location=New York|url=https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/israel-attacks-200-targets-in-gaza-ahead-of-biden-visit-cd6889d6 |url-status=live |access-date=17 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231018024704/https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/israel-attacks-200-targets-in-gaza-ahead-of-biden-visit-cd6889d6 |archive-date=18 October 2023 |url-access=subscription}}}}</ref> Nevertheless, on 22 October, the IDF dropped leaflets in northern Gaza stating anyone who did not comply with the evacuation would be considered a "terrorist".<ref>{{cite news |last1=Morris |first1=Loveday |last2=Berger |first2=Miriam |title=IDF leaflets says civilians that don't evacuate Gaza can be seen as accomplices |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/10/22/israel-hamas-war-news-gaza-aid-updates/#link-HW6X3JZXDFGWLPYFA6667YB4G4 |newspaper=The Washington Post |access-date=22 October 2023 |archive-date=22 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022053342/https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/10/22/israel-hamas-war-news-gaza-aid-updates/#link-HW6X3JZXDFGWLPYFA6667YB4G4 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 20 December, Human Rights Watch stated the risk of [[forced displacement]] was growing.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Hardman |first1=Nadia |title=Most of Gaza's Population Remains Displaced and in Harm's Way |url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/12/20/most-gazas-population-remains-displaced-and-harms-way#:~:text=Repeated%20attacks%20by%20the%20Israeli,Gaza%27s%20hospitals%20have%20been%20damaged. |website=Human Rights Watch |date=20 December 2023 |access-date=21 December 2023 |archive-date=20 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231220222612/https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/12/20/most-gazas-population-remains-displaced-and-harms-way#:~:text=Repeated%20attacks%20by%20the%20Israeli,Gaza%27s%20hospitals%20have%20been%20damaged. |url-status=live }}</ref> On 12 January, the Assistant Secretary General for Human Rights stated that Israel's compelled evacuations had failed to ensure protections required under international law, thus constituting a potential war crime.<ref name="auto"/> In March 2024, [[Forensic Architecture]] stated that Israel's "humanitarian evacuations" might amount to the war crime of forced displacement.<ref>{{cite web |title=Gaza 'safe zones' led to displacement, Israeli attacks on civilians: Report |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/3/13/gaza-safe-zones-led-to-displacement-israeli-attacks-on-civilians-report |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=17 March 2024 |archive-date=17 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240317040054/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/3/13/gaza-safe-zones-led-to-displacement-israeli-attacks-on-civilians-report |url-status=live }}</ref>

In March 2024, Paula Gaviria Betancur, the [[United Nations special rapporteur|UN Special Rapporteur]] on the rights of internally displaced persons, stated ahead of Israel's planned [[Rafah offensive]]: "Any evacuation order imposed on Rafah under the current circumstances, with the rest of Gaza reduced to rubble, would be a flagrant violation of international humanitarian and human rights law."<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel's evacuation orders in Gaza illegal: UN special rapporteur |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/7/israels-war-on-gaza-live-20-starve-to-death-in-gaza-more-feared-dead?update=2755187 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=9 March 2024 |archive-date=9 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240309190842/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/7/israels-war-on-gaza-live-20-starve-to-death-in-gaza-more-feared-dead?update=2755187 |url-status=live }}</ref> French president [[Emmanuel Macron]] told Netanyahu that a forced transfer of the population from Rafah would be a war crime.<ref>{{cite news |title=Macron tells Israel forced displacement of people from Rafah would be 'war crime' |url=https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2024/03/25/macron-tells-israel-forced-transfer-of-people-would-be-war-crime_6650612_4.html#:~:text=French%20President%20Emmanuel%20Macron%20on,constitute%20%22a%20war%20crime.%22 |newspaper=Le Monde.fr | date=25 March 2024 |publisher=AFP |access-date=26 March 2024}}</ref> In May 2024, [[Volker Türk]] condemned Israel's evacuation orders in Rafah, stating, "This is inhumane. It runs contrary to the basic principles of international humanitarian and human rights laws".<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel's Rafah Evacuation Order 'Inhumane': UN |url=https://www.barrons.com/news/rafah-evacuation-order-inhumane-un-f61df640 |website=Barron's |publisher=Agence France Presse |access-date=10 May 2024}}</ref> A UNOCHA spokesperson said of the Rafah evacuation: "There are strong indications that this is being conducted in violation of international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite web |title=UN agencies slam Israeli offensive in Rafah as 'darkest' day |url=https://www.yahoo.com/news/un-agencies-slam-israeli-offensive-124845028.html |website=Yahoo! News |date=7 May 2024 |publisher=DPA |access-date=12 May 2024}}</ref>

==Buffer zone==
Israel sought to create an expanded [[buffer zone]] in Gaza. Satellite analysis by researchers at [[Hebrew University]] found the buffer zone was already in advanced stages.<ref>{{cite web |title=Almost 40% of buildings within planned Gaza buffer zone said demolished |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/almost-40-of-buildings-within-planned-gaza-buffer-zone-said-demolished/ |website=The Times of Israel |access-date=26 January 2024 |archive-date=25 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240125125317/https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/almost-40-of-buildings-within-planned-gaza-buffer-zone-said-demolished/ |url-status=live }}</ref> By January 2024, Israel had destroyed more than 1,000 buildings for the planned zone.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Shotter |first1=James |title=Israel demolishes buildings to create buffer zone within Gaza |url=https://www.ft.com/content/0694ab13-a291-4b4a-81c2-53ec91ae1cad |website=Financial Times |date=24 January 2024 |access-date=26 January 2024 |archive-date=26 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240126042136/https://www.ft.com/content/0694ab13-a291-4b4a-81c2-53ec91ae1cad |url-status=live }}</ref> In April 2024, [[UNOSAT]] found that around 90 percent of the 4,000 buildings on Gaza's eastern border had been damaged or destroyed.<ref>{{cite web |title=Hostilities in the Gaza Strip and Israel Flash Update #153 |url=https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/hostilities-gaza-strip-and-israel-flash-update-153-enarhe |website=ReliefWeb |date=15 April 2024 |publisher=UNOCHA |access-date=19 April 2024}}</ref> The [[Palestinian Center for Human Rights]] stated such civilian properties were protected under international humanitarian law.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Morris |first1=Loveday |title=What to know about Israel's controversial 'buffer zone' in Gaza |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2024/01/24/israel-buffer-zone-gaza-war/ |newspaper=The Washington Post |access-date=26 January 2024 |archive-date=25 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240125060625/https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2024/01/24/israel-buffer-zone-gaza-war/ |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Shaul Arieli]], a former IDF colonel and expert on Israeli borders, stated that the creation of a permanent buffer zone was illegal, since Israel is prohibited from altering the boundaries of Gaza as an occupying power.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Lieber |first1=Dov |title=Israel Builds Buffer Zone Along Gaza Border, Risking New Rift With U.S. |url=https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/israel-border-gaza-buffer-zone-4131020d |newspaper=WSJ |access-date=26 January 2024 |archive-date=25 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240125211342/https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/israel-border-gaza-buffer-zone-4131020d |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Geoffrey Nice]], a war crimes prosecutor, stated, "It is unjustified, by any view, under international law."<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel's Gaza landgrab 'unjustified, by any view, under international law' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/1/25/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israel-kills-9-in-un-shelter-sparking-outrage?update=2648250 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=26 January 2024 |archive-date=26 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240126042136/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/1/25/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israel-kills-9-in-un-shelter-sparking-outrage?update=2648250 |url-status=live }}</ref> Volker Türk, the UN human rights chief, stated, "Extensive destruction of property, not justified by military necessity and carried out unlawfully and wantonly, amounts to a grave breach of the Fourth Geneva Convention, and a war crime."<ref>{{cite web |title=Gaza 'buffer zone' possible war crime: UN human rights chief |url=https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/02/1146352 |website=UN News |date=8 February 2024 |publisher=United Nations |access-date=9 February 2024 |archive-date=8 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240208164744/https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/02/1146352 |url-status=live }}</ref> An analysis by ''Haaretz'' found the buffer zone could occupy as much as 16 percent of Gaza's overall territory.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Michaeli |first1=Yarden |last2=Avi |first2=Scharf |title=Buffer Zone and Control Corridor: What the Israeli Army's Entrenchment in Gaza Looks Like |url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/security-aviation/2024-03-28/ty-article-magazine/.premium/buffer-zone-and-control-corridor-what-israeli-armys-entrenchment-in-gaza-looks-like/0000018e-8556-df92-a5ff-e77e0d6a0000 |website=Haaretz |date=28 March 2024 |access-date=5 April 2024}}</ref> A May 2024 ''Al Jazeera'' investigation found the buffer zone had taken 32 percent of Gaza's territory.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Salhani |first1=Justin |title=Israel has encroached on 32% of Gaza, Al Jazeera investigation shows |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/5/31/israel-has-encroached-on-32-of-gaza-al-jazeera-investigation-shows |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=8 June 2024}}</ref>

==Looting==
During the war, soldiers [[looting|looted]] Palestinian homes in Gaza, reportedly taking "whatever is easy and accessible".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Ziv |first1=Oren |title=Rugs, cosmetics, motorbikes: Israeli soldiers are looting Gaza homes en masse |url=https://www.972mag.com/israeli-soldiers-looting-gaza/ |website=+972 Magazine |date=20 February 2024 |access-date=23 February 2024 |archive-date=22 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240222112333/https://www.972mag.com/israeli-soldiers-looting-gaza/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On 21 February 2024, [[Yifat Tomer-Yerushalmi]], the IDF's [[Military Advocate General]], stated that some soldiers' actions — including looting and the removal of private property — had "crossed the criminal threshold".<ref>{{cite news |last1=Kubovich |first1=Yaniv |title=Top IDF Lawyer: Some Soldiers' Behavior in Gaza Has 'Crossed the Criminal Threshold' |url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2024-02-21/ty-article/.premium/top-idf-lawyer-some-israeli-soldiers-have-engaged-in-criminal-behavior-during-war/0000018d-cbb5-d6e9-a38d-fbbdc0610000 |website=Haaretz |date=21 February 2024 |access-date=23 February 2024 |archive-date=21 February 2024 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20240221152828/https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2024-02-21/ty-article/.premium/top-idf-lawyer-some-israeli-soldiers-have-engaged-in-criminal-behavior-during-war/0000018d-cbb5-d6e9-a38d-fbbdc0610000 |url-status=live }}</ref> Tomer-Yerushalmi stated such cases were under investigation.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Fabian |first1=Emanuel |title=IDF's top lawyer warns against 'cases of unacceptable conduct' by troops in Gaza |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/idfs-top-lawyer-warns-against-unacceptable-cases-of-conduct-by-troops-in-gaza/ |website=The Times of Israel |access-date=23 February 2024 |archive-date=23 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240223041151/https://www.timesofisrael.com/idfs-top-lawyer-warns-against-unacceptable-cases-of-conduct-by-troops-in-gaza/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The [[Council on American-Islamic Relations]] called the looting a war crime and demanded the Biden administration to condemn them.<ref>{{cite web |title=US Muslim group condemns Israeli soldiers looting Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/21/israels-war-on-gaza-live-us-ceasefire-veto-a-new-low-as-hunger-spreads?update=2721700 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=23 February 2024 |archive-date=23 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240223023611/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/21/israels-war-on-gaza-live-us-ceasefire-veto-a-new-low-as-hunger-spreads?update=2721700 |url-status=live }}</ref> The [[Fourth Geneva Convention]] of 1949 explicitly prohibits the looting of civilian property during wartime.<ref name="ICRC">[https://ihl-databases.icrc.org/customary-ihl/eng/docs/v1_rul_rule52 Rule 52. Pillage is prohibited.] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210308140301/https://ihl-databases.icrc.org/customary-ihl/eng/docs/v1_rul_rule52// |date=8 March 2021 }}, ''Customary IHL Database'', [[International Committee of the Red Cross]] (ICRC)/[[Cambridge University Press]].</ref><ref>[[Hague Conventions of 1899 and 1907#Hague Convention of 1899|Hague Convention on the Law and Customs of War on Land]] (Hague II), [https://avalon.law.yale.edu/19th_century/hague02.asp article 28] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230804035218/https://avalon.law.yale.edu/19th_century/hague02.asp |date=4 August 2023 }}.</ref><ref name=gen>E. Lauterpacht, C. J. Greenwood, Marc Weller, [https://books.google.com/books?id=5xVSkGtcT5YC&pg=PA154 ''The Kuwait Crisis: Basic Documents''] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324115623/https://books.google.com/books?id=5xVSkGtcT5YC&pg=PA154#v=onepage&q&f=false |date=24 March 2024 }}, Cambridge University Press, 1991, p. 154. {{ISBN|0521463084}}</ref> In August 2024, Yuval Green, an IDF paratrooper returning from Gaza, stated he had witnessed widespread abuses against Palestinians in Gaza, including looting and the destruction of homes.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Kaufman |first1=Ami |title=Palestinian homes were destroyed 'for revenge,' says Israeli soldier who served in Gaza |url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/08/01/middleeast/israeli-soldier-alleges-serious-misconduct-gaza-intl/index.html#:~:text=Destroyed%20homes%2C%20looting%2C%20and%20a,in%20an%20interview%20with%20CNN. |website=CNN |date=August 2024 |access-date=18 August 2024}}</ref>

==Additional theaters of war==
===Yemen===
{{further|Red Sea crisis}}
In July 2024, Israel [[2024 Israeli strikes on Yemen|bombed]] the [[Al Hudaydah|Hodeidah port]] during its [[Red Sea crisis|conflict with the Houthis]]. [[Human Rights Watch]] termed the strikes a possible war crime, as they appeared to be an indiscriminate or disproportionate attack on civilians.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Tanios |first1=Clauda |title=Israel's July strikes on Yemen's Hodeidah port a 'possible war crime', HR Watch says |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israels-july-strikes-yemens-hodeidah-port-possible-war-crime-hr-watch-says-2024-08-19/ |website=Reuters |access-date=11 September 2024}}</ref>

===Lebanon===
{{Excerpt|Israel–Hezbollah conflict (2023–2024)|Killing of Lebanese civilians|paragraphs=1}}
According to the Syrian Observatory for Human rights, 232 Syrian refugees were killed by the IDF in Lebanon since the start of the Israel-Hamas war.<ref name="Hezbollah–Israel conflict (2023–present) syrianrefugees">{{cite web|url=https://www.syriahr.com/en/348470/|title=Israeli military escalation on Lebanon {{!}} 216 Syrian refugees killed in Israeli strikes on Lebanon in 50 days|date=5 November 2024|website=The Syrian Observatory For Human Rights}}</ref>

===West Bank===
{{further|Israeli incursions in the West Bank during the Gaza war}}

During the war, the Israeli military was increasingly active in the [[West Bank]]. According to Amnesty International, Israel violated international humanitarian law by using disproportionate force during arrest raids, blocking medical assistance to people with life-threatening injuries, attacking paramedics, and conducting unlawful killings.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel/OPT: Israel has unleashed wave of unlawful attacks on Palestinians in West Bank - new research |url=https://www.amnesty.org.uk/press-releases/israelopt-israel-has-unleashed-wave-unlawful-attacks-palestinians-west-bank-new |website=Amnesty International UK |access-date=6 February 2024 |archive-date=6 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240206050003/https://www.amnesty.org.uk/press-releases/israelopt-israel-has-unleashed-wave-unlawful-attacks-palestinians-west-bank-new |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Erika Guevara Rosas]], Amnesty's director of global research, stated, "These unlawful killings are in blatant violation of international human rights law and are committed with impunity".<ref>{{cite web |title=Shocking spike in use of unlawful lethal force by Israeli forces against Palestinians in the occupied West Bank |url=https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2024/02/shocking-spike-in-use-of-unlawful-lethal-force-by-israeli-forces-against-palestinians-in-the-occupied-west-bank/#:~:text=These%20unlawful%20killings%20are%20in,International%27s%20Director%20of%20Global%20Research%2C |website=Amnesty International |date=5 February 2024 |access-date=6 February 2024 |archive-date=5 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240205145134/https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2024/02/shocking-spike-in-use-of-unlawful-lethal-force-by-israeli-forces-against-palestinians-in-the-occupied-west-bank/#:~:text=These%20unlawful%20killings%20are%20in,International%27s%20Director%20of%20Global%20Research%2C |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Ben Saul]], UN special rapporteur on human rights, stated that a November 2023 IDF killing of two boys appeared to be a war crime.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Yeung |first1=Isabel |title=Israel accused of possible war crime over killing of West Bank boy |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cw07wgrwzywo?xtor=AL-72-%5Bpartner%5D-%5Bbbc.news.twitter%5D-%5Bheadline%5D-%5Bnews%5D-%5Bbizdev%5D-%5Bisapi%5D&at_link_type=web_link&at_link_id=83D388F6-0844-11EF-84E8-B6B516B552E7&at_campaign=Social_Flow&at_format=link&at_ptr_name=twitter&at_link_origin=BBCWorld&at_campaign_type=owned&at_bbc_team=editorial&at_medium=social |website=BBC |date=2 May 2024 |access-date=18 May 2024}}</ref> On 5 March 2024, the Palestinian Red Crescent stated that it had recorded 427 violations against its medical mission by Israel in the West Bank, terming these a violation of international humanitarian law.<ref>{{cite web |title=PRCS says Israel committed hundreds of violations against its medical teams in West Bank |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/5/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israeli-attacks-on-aid-seekers-continue?update=2750410 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=8 March 2024 |archive-date=8 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240308031640/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/5/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israeli-attacks-on-aid-seekers-continue?update=2750410 |url-status=live }}</ref>

Following the demolition of a Palestinian activist's family home in [[East Jerusalem]] — part of a broader wave of forced displacement in the [[West Bank]]{{efn|On 27 December 2023, UNOCHA stated that since 7 October, 1,208 people had been displaced due settler violence, 393 due to lacking Israeli building permits, 95 on punitive grounds, and 483 due to army demolitions.<ref name="Flash Update #77">{{cite web |title=Hostilities in the Gaza Strip and Israel Flash Update #77 |url=https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/hostilities-gaza-strip-and-israel-flash-update-77#:~:text=Since%207%20October%2C%20OCHA%20has,to%20property%20(46%20incidents). |website=ReliefWeb |date=27 December 2023 |publisher=UNOCHA |access-date=27 December 2023 |archive-date=27 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231227150543/https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/hostilities-gaza-strip-and-israel-flash-update-77#:~:text=Since%207%20October%2C%20OCHA%20has,to%20property%20(46%20incidents). |url-status=live }}</ref>}} — the [[European Union External Action Service]] stated, "Such acts are in violation of International Humanitarian Law".<ref>{{cite web |title=EU condemns demolition of Abu Diab's home in occupied East Jerusalem |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/15/israels-war-on-gaza-live-four-dead-as-israel-hits-city-in-lebanons-south?update=2710530 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=17 February 2024}}</ref> George Noll, head of the  U.S. Office of Palestinian Affairs, condemned the demolition.<ref>{{cite web |title=US official condemns demolition of Palestinian activist's home |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/6/israels-war-on-gaza-live-un-food-convoy-blocked-from-north-gaza-by-israel?update=2752516 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=9 March 2024}}</ref> Following the Israeli approval of around 3,500 new illegal settlements in the West Bank, UN human rights chief Volker Türk stated the transfer of Israel's population into the occupied territories was a "war crime under international law".<ref>{{cite web |title=Israeli settlements in Palestinian territories amount to 'war crime': UN |url=https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3254714/israeli-settlements-palestinian-territories-amount-war-crime-un |website=South China Morning Post |date=8 March 2024 |publisher=Agence France-Presse and Reuters |access-date=10 March 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Israeli settlements in Palestinian areas amount to a 'war crime' says UN rights office |url=https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/israeli-settlements-in-palestinian-areas-amount-to-a-war-crime-says-un-rights-office |website=PBS |date=8 March 2024 |publisher=Associated Press |access-date=10 March 2024}}</ref> Following the announcement that Israel was seizing 800 hectares of Palestinian land in the West Bank, the [[Federal Foreign Office]] stated, "The settlements violate international law and fuel further tensions in this extremely fragile situation."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Schrader |first1=Adam |title=German Foreign Ministry condemns illegal Israeli settlements |url=https://www.upi.com/Top_News/World-News/2024/03/24/germany-german-foreign-ministry-condemns-illegal-israel-settlements/7191711311409/ |website=UPI |access-date=27 March 2024}}</ref> French president [[Emmanuel Macron]] condemned the expanded settlements, stating they "are contrary to international law".<ref>{{cite web |title=France Threatens New Sanctions Against West Bank Settlers |url=https://www.barrons.com/amp/news/france-threatens-new-sanctions-against-west-bank-settlers-7d3157b4# |website=Barron's |publisher=Agence France Presse |access-date=28 April 2024}}</ref> The [[UN Human Rights Office]] stated they were "alarmed" by Israel's expanded settlements and stated they "fly in the face of international law".<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel's settlement expansion is alarming and flies in face of international law |url=https://www.un.org/unispal/document/israels-settlement-expansion-19aug24/ |website=United Nations |access-date=12 September 2024}}</ref>

[[BBC News]] reported in May 2024 that 11 soldiers of the [[Kfir Brigade]] (which is primarily active in the West Bank) posted on social media 45 photos and videos showing detained Palestinians; the Israeli Defence Forces did not respond when asked about the individual incidents or individual soldiers involved and identified, instead broadly stating: "In the event of unacceptable behavior, soldiers were disciplined and even suspended from reserve duty."<ref name=Merlyn>{{cite news |last1=Thomas |first1=Merlyn |last2=Ryan |first2=Jamie |last3=Brown |first3=Paul |title=Israel troops continue posting abuse footage despite pledge to act |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-69020237 |access-date=17 May 2024 |work=[[BBC News]] |date=17 May 2024}}</ref> BBC News further reported that the soldiers did not obscure their identities, with some of them posting under names of Yohai Vazana, Ofer Bobrov, Sammy Ben, and Ori Dahbash.<ref name=Merlyn/> According to BBC News, the "detained Palestinians are frequently shown blindfolded and restrained, having been forced to either lie on the floor, or squat, with their hands bound behind their backs", with some detainees being covered in Israeli flags.<ref name=Merlyn/> [[Jan Egeland]], the head of the [[Norwegian Refugee Council]], stated, "The failure to hold Israel accountable has allowed its forces to violate IHL [international humanitarian law] without consequence".<ref>{{cite web |title=Lack of accountability allows Israel to use 'excessive force' in West Bank: NRC chief |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/6/8/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israeli-army-to-be-added-to-un-child-harm-list?update=2960137 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=16 June 2024}}</ref>

In September 2024, Israeli soldiers pushed three corpses from a rooftop during a raid on [[Qabatiya]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Frankel |first1=Julia |title=Israeli soldiers pushed three apparently lifeless bodies from roofs during a West Bank raid |url=https://apnews.com/article/israel-palestinians-soldiers-qabatiya-west-bank-ae65d70f7da5db4603ba1b7c77f2ccd3 |website=Associated Press |date=19 September 2024 |access-date=22 September 2024}}</ref>

== Use of white phosphorus on civilians ==
Human Rights Watch and Amnesty International's Crisis Evidence Lab shared evidence that Israeli military units striking in Gaza and Lebanon have employed [[white phosphorus munitions|white phosphorus artillery rounds]]; Israel denied the report, calling the accusation "unequivocally false", although it has since admitted to its use.<ref name=TimeWP/><ref name="APNews White Phosphorus">{{cite web |last1=Chehayeb |first1=Kareem |title=Rights group accuses Israel of hitting residential buildings with white phosphorous in Lebanon |url=https://apnews.com/article/israel-lebanon-human-rights-watch-white-phosphorus-616984b69e1cbe1efc5bbee4cb3ba8ae |website=apnews.com |date=5 June 2024 |publisher=AP News |access-date=28 July 2024}}</ref> White phosphorus munitions are allowed on battlefields for specific purposes such as creating [[Smoke screen|smokescreens]], generating [[battlefield illumination|illumination]], and [[Targeting (warfare)|marking targets]]. They are not banned as chemical weapons under international conventions due to these legitimate uses.<ref name=TimeWP>{{Cite magazine|last=Serhan|first=Yasmeen|date=13 October 2023|title=Israel Accused of Using White Phosphorus in Gaza|url=https://time.com/6323482/israel-white-phosphorus-gaza-lebanon/|access-date=14 October 2023|magazine=[[Time (magazine)|TIME]]|language=en|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022011038/https://time.com/6323482/israel-white-phosphorus-gaza-lebanon/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{multiref|{{cite web|title=Israel: White Phosphorus Used in Gaza, Lebanon|website=[[Human Rights Watch]]|date=12 October 2023|url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/10/12/israel-white-phosphorus-used-gaza-lebanon|access-date=13 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022011547/https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/10/12/israel-white-phosphorus-used-gaza-lebanon|url-status=live}}|{{cite web|title=Amnesty International shares evidence that Israel used white phosphorus in Gaza|url=https://www.anews.com.tr/middle-east/2023/10/14/amnesty-international-shares-evidence-that-israel-used-white-phosphorus-in-gaza|website=A News|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231014235439/https://www.anews.com.tr/middle-east/2023/10/14/amnesty-international-shares-evidence-that-israel-used-white-phosphorus-in-gaza|access-date=14 October 2023|archive-date=14 October 2023}}|{{cite news|last1=Lyon|first1=Emmett|title=Israel accused of using controversial white phosphorus shells in Gaza amid war with Hamas|url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/israel-hamas-war-white-phosphorous-gaza-palestinians-amnesty-hrw-reports/|work=[[CBS News]]|access-date=14 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022011719/https://www.cbsnews.com/news/israel-hamas-war-white-phosphorous-gaza-palestinians-amnesty-hrw-reports/|url-status=live}}}}</ref> However, white phosphorus is also considered an [[Incendiary device|incendiary weapon]], and [[Protocol on Incendiary Weapons|Protocol III]] of the [[Convention on Certain Conventional Weapons]] prohibits their use against military targets located among civilians, although Israel is not a signatory.<ref>{{Cite news|date=13 October 2023|title=Human Rights Watch says Israel used white phosphorus in Gaza, Lebanon|language=en|work=[[Reuters]]|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/human-rights-watch-says-israel-used-white-phosphorous-gaza-lebanon-2023-10-12/|access-date=17 October 2023|archive-date=13 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231013003409/https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/human-rights-watch-says-israel-used-white-phosphorous-gaza-lebanon-2023-10-12/|url-status=live}}</ref> White phosphorus ignites when exposed to atmospheric oxygen, and on contact can [[White phosphorus munitions#Physiological effects|cause deep and severe injuries]], potentially leading to multiple organ failure, and even minor burns can be fatal. According to Human Rights Watch, the use of white phosphorus is "unlawfully indiscriminate when airburst in populated urban areas, where it can burn down houses and cause egregious harm to civilians", and "violates the requirement under international humanitarian law to take all feasible precautions to avoid civilian injury and loss of life".<ref>{{cite web|title=Israel: White Phosphorus Used in Gaza, Lebanon|url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/10/12/israel-white-phosphorus-used-gaza-lebanon|website=[[Human Rights Watch]]|date=12 October 2023|access-date=13 October 2023|archive-date=12 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231012235517/https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/10/12/israel-white-phosphorus-used-gaza-lebanon|url-status=live}}</ref> According to Amnesty International weapons investigator [[Brian Castner]], whether employing white phosphorus constitutes a war crime depends on the intended target and intended use, but that "generally, any attacks that fail to discriminate between civilians and military forces can potentially be a violation of the laws of war".<ref>{{cite news|last1=Kelly|first1=Meg|title=Israel appears to use white phosphorus in Gaza, video shows|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/10/12/white-phosphorus-israel-gaza-strike-video/|access-date=17 October 2023|newspaper=[[The Washington Post]]|archive-date=13 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231013003118/https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/10/12/white-phosphorus-israel-gaza-strike-video/|url-status=live}}</ref>

On 31 October 2023, after an investigation, Amnesty International stated that a 16 October Israeli white phosphorus attack was indiscriminate, unlawful, and "must be investigated as a war crime", due to its use on the populated Lebanese town of Dhayra, which injured at least nine civilians.<ref>{{Cite news |last=null |date=31 October 2023 |title=Israel-Hamas War: Update from Euan Ward |language=en-US |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2023/10/31/world/israel-hamas-war-gaza-news |access-date=31 October 2023 |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=31 October 2023 |title=Evidence of Israel's unlawful use of white phosphorus in southern Lebanon as cross-border hostilities escalate |url=https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2023/10/lebanon-evidence-of-israels-unlawful-use-of-white-phosphorus-in-southern-lebanon-as-cross-border-hostilities-escalate/ |access-date=31 October 2023 |website=Amnesty International |language=en}}</ref> On 2 November, Amnesty International stated its investigations into four incidents on  10, 11, 16 and 17 October showed Israel had used white phosphorus munitions.<ref>{{cite web |title=Amnesty International says Israel used white phosphorus in Gaza, Lebanon |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/2/israel-hamas-war-live-195-killed-120-missing-in-jabalia-strikes?update=2458373 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=2 November 2023}}</ref> In Lebanon, Israel's white phosphorus bombs have destroyed over 4.5 million sq m of forest in southern Lebanon with the economic loses being valued at nearly 20 million dollars.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Baaklini |first=Suzanne |date=8 November 2023 |title=Israel's phosphorous bombs destroyed over 4.5 million sq m of forest in southern Lebanon |work=L'Orient Today |url=https://today.lorientlejour.com/article/1356622/israels-phosphorous-bombs-destroyed-over-45-million-sq-m-of-forest-in-southern-lebanon.html}}</ref> An investigation by the ''Washington Post'' uncovered that white phosphorus used in an October attack that injured 9 people in Lebanon were supplied by the US.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Christou |first=William |date=11 December 2023 |title=Israel used U.S.-supplied white phosphorus in Lebanon attack |newspaper=The Washington Post |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2023/12/11/israel-us-white-phosphorus-lebanon/}}</ref>

In June 2024, Human Rights Watch verified the unlawful use of white phosphorus munitions over five populated residential municipalities.<ref>{{cite web |title=Lebanon: Israel's White Phosphorous Use Risks Civilian Harm |url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2024/06/05/lebanon-israels-white-phosphorous-use-risks-civilian-harm |website=Human Rights Watch |date=5 June 2024 |access-date=16 June 2024}}</ref> According to the Lebanese Health Ministry, at least 173 people have needed medical intervention for white phosphorus exposure.<ref name="APNews White Phosphorus" /> In October 2024, a leaked UN report stated the Israeli military entered a [[Unifil]] base and used white phosphorus, injuring 15 peacekeepers.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Jalabi |first1=Raya |title=Israel launched a dozen attacks on UN troops in Lebanon, says leaked report |url=https://www.ft.com/content/151eb482-6415-48a8-bf3f-baed00018c4e?shareType=nongift |website=Financial Times |date=23 October 2024 |access-date=27 October 2024|url-access=subscription}}</ref>

On 3 March 2026, Human Rights Watch reported that Israeli forces had used white phosphorus munitions over the southern Lebanese village of [[Yohmor, Nabatieh|Yohmor]], striking a residential neighborhood. The organisation noted that Israel had previously used white phosphorus in southern Lebanon between October 2023 and May 2024, which it said put civilians at risk.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Chehayeb |first1=Kareem |last2=Melzer |first2=Natalie |last3=Mroue |first3=Bassem |title=Lebanese parliament extends term by 2 years as Israel intensifies attacks on Lebanon |url=https://apnews.com/article/lebanon-israel-hezbollah-hrw-white-phosphorus-dcb94eb15145a3e9194f05727757822f |website=AP News |access-date=14 March 2026 |date=9 March 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Israel unlawfully used white phosphorus in Lebanon: HRW |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/9/israel-unlawfully-used-white-phosphorus-in-lebanon-hrw |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=14 March 2026 |date=9 March 2026}}</ref>

==Killing of surrendered people==

=== Surrendered Palestinians ===
On 10 October, the [[Israeli Defence Force]] published a video that appeared to show IDF soldiers shooting four surrendering Palestinians.<ref name="Israeli army tweets video that appears to show">{{cite web |last1=Naffakh |first1=Mahmoud |title=Israeli army tweets video that appears to show soldiers shooting Palestinians who surrendered |url=https://observers.france24.com/en/middle-east/20231013-israeli-army-tweets-video-that-appears-to-show-soldiers-shooting-palestinians-who-surrendered |website=The Observers |date=13 October 2023 |publisher=France24 |access-date=22 October 2023 |archive-date=16 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231016201330/https://observers.france24.com/en/middle-east/20231013-israeli-army-tweets-video-that-appears-to-show-soldiers-shooting-palestinians-who-surrendered |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=X post by Al Jazeera English |url=https://twitter.com/AJEnglish/status/1712907775301365989 |website=X |publisher=Al Jazeera English |access-date=22 October 2023 |archive-date=22 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022172824/https://twitter.com/AJEnglish/status/1712907775301365989 |url-status=live }}</ref> Footage analysis indicated the men appeared to be surrendering, with three men getting on the ground with their arms raised, one waving a piece of white clothing. None of them appeared to be armed at the time of the shooting, while a subsequent video showed the bodies had been moved, with weapons placed near them on the ground. The analysis concluded the four men were unarmed Palestinians who left Gaza through a breach in the separation wall.<ref name="Israeli army tweets video that appears to show" /> An IDF spokesman said he had no comment.<ref name="Israeli army tweets video that appears to show" /> Killing surrendered civilians or combatants is a war crime.<ref>{{cite web | last1=Gadzo | first1=Mersiha | last2=Rasheed | first2=Zaheena | last3=Rowlands | first3=Lyndal | last4=Regencia | first4=Ted | last5=Mohamed | first5=Hamza | last6=Pietromarchi | first6=Virginia | title=Israel-Hamas war updates: Hamas claims release of woman and children | website=Al Jazeera | date=10 October 2023 | url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/10/10/israel-hamas-war-live-us-redoubles-israel-support-as-bombs-rain-on-gaza | access-date=23 October 2023 | archive-date=22 October 2023 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022225033/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/10/10/israel-hamas-war-live-us-redoubles-israel-support-as-bombs-rain-on-gaza | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite tweet |user=EuroMedHR |number=1711987472358347201 |title=The crime scene has then been doctored & assault rifles appear to have been added to the bodies. These individuals may have been civilians who crossed the fence after its collapse. Their killing as they surrendered is an act of extrajudicial execution that constitutes a war crime}}</ref>

In video footage dated 8 December 2023, the Israeli military is seen killing two Palestinians from the West Bank's [[Far'a|Far'a refugee camp]] in what [[B'Tselem]] described as "illegal executions". One man holding a canister was shot, and was then gunned down while he laid bleeding on the ground. A second man, who was completely unarmed and hiding under a car, was shot and killed instantly. The Israeli military later said they would investigate the attacks.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Frankel |first=Julia |date=15 December 2023 |title=Israeli military opens probe after videos show Israeli forces killing 2 Palestinians at close range |url=https://apnews.com/article/israel-palestinians-west-bank-gaza-war-east-jerusalem-shooting-army-23338c903c08bdd3e5fade3e2a048ab1 |website=AP News}}</ref>

Human rights groups documented multiple instances of civilians in Gaza being shot by Israeli soldiers while waving [[white flags]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Srivastava |first1=Mehul |last2=England |first2=Andrew |title=Israeli soldiers kill hostages waving white flag after mistaking them for Hamas fighters |url=https://www.ft.com/content/2e299603-2fed-4855-9694-9801008c48dc?shareType=nongift |website=Financial Times |date=17 December 2023 |access-date=17 December 2023}}</ref> The Human Rights Watch Israel-Palestine director stated Israel had a "track record of unlawfully firing at unarmed people who pose no threat with impunity – even those waving white flags".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Madani |first1=Doha |title=Hostage killings underscore IDF's shoot-first practice, HRW director says |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/news/world/live-blog/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-rcna130129# |website=NBC News |access-date=17 December 2023}}</ref>{{efn|The director stated that in prior cases, "There were statements that they would be investigated but no one was held into account".<ref>{{cite web |title=Gaza shooting video shows 'flagrant disregard for Palestinian life' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/28/israels-war-on-gaza-live-unarmed-palestinians-killed-buried-by-bulldozer?update=2804167 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=2 April 2024}}</ref>}} In early January, a video surfaced dating to 12 November showing displaced Palestinians evacuating Gaza City, including a woman and her child.<ref>{{Cite web|title= Video Shows IDF Allegedly Killing Palestinian Woman With Child Waving White Flag|url= https://www.commondreams.org/news/gaza-civilian-casualties-2666920116|website=[[Common Dreams]]|date=10 January 2024|last=Wilkins|first=Brett|access-date=14 April 2026}}</ref> Despite the group clearly carrying white flags, the woman was reportedly shot and killed by an Israeli sniper.<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.jordannews.jo/Section-20/Middle-East/Video-shows-Israeli-sniper-killing-a-Palestinian-woman-with-white-flag-33501#:~:text=World%20Jordan%20News-,GAZA%20–%20On%20Monday%2C%20video%20footage%20was%20released%20documenting%20an%20Israeli,while%20holding%20a%20white%20flag. | title= Video shows Israeli sniper killing a Palestinian woman with white flag |work=Jordan News| date=8 January 2024 }}</ref>

On 24 January 2024, British network ''[[ITV (TV network)|ITV]]'' released footage of an Israeli sniper shooting and killing a man carrying a white flag whom the journalist had interviewed only moments before his death.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Irvine |first1=John |title=Moment innocent civilian brandishing white flag in Gaza 'safe zone' is shot dead in the street |url=https://www.itv.com/news/2024-01-23/moment-civilian-brandishing-white-flag-in-gaza-safe-zone-is-shot-dead |website=ITV |access-date=25 January 2024}}</ref> Both the [[Norwegian Refugee Council]] and Amnesty International termed it a possible war crime.<ref>{{cite web |title='It's a war crime': ITV News' Gaza clip sparks outrage from charities, US officials and Westminster |url=https://www.itv.com/news/2024-01-24/pm-questioned-over-itv-news-footage-of-man-with-white-flag-shot-dead-in-gaza |website=ITV |access-date=25 January 2024}}</ref> An IDF senior commander later stated, "There are mistakes, it is war."<ref>{{cite web |title='There are mistakes, it is war': Israeli commander indicates IDF were behind white flag shooting |url=https://www.itv.com/news/2024-01-30/senior-israeli-commander-indicates-idf-were-behind-gaza-white-flag-shooting |website=ITV |access-date=31 January 2024}}</ref>

According to a witness interviewed by ''Al Jazeera'', the corpses of 30 people were found on 31 January 2024 inside a schoolyard in northern Gaza, with the bodies reportedly blindfolded, and their legs and hands tied.<ref>{{cite web |title=Shocked to find dozens of dead bodies: Witness |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/1/31/israels-war-on-gaza-live-severe-hunger-in-gaza-as-aid-trucks-surrounded?update=2665536 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=1 February 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title="30 Palestinian Bodies Found In Gaza", Six-Week Ceasefire In New Israel-Hamas Hostage Deal? |url=https://www.news18.com/videos/world/30-palestinian-bodies-found-in-gaza-six-week-ceasefire-in-new-israel-hamas-hostage-deal-8761519.html |website=[[CNN-News18|News18]] |access-date=1 February 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Palestinian ngo calls for inquiry into forced disappearance after mass grave found in Gaza |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240201210701/https://www.laprensalatina.com/palestinian-ngo-calls-for-inquiry-into-forced-disappearance-after-mass-grave-found-in-gaza/|archive-date=1 February 2024|url=https://www.laprensalatina.com/palestinian-ngo-calls-for-inquiry-into-forced-disappearance-after-mass-grave-found-in-gaza/ |website=La Prensa |date=February 2024 |publisher=[[EFE]] |access-date=3 February 2024}}</ref> The [[Council on American-Islamic Relations]] said the incident should be probed and added to South Africa's ICJ case against Israel.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Allison |first1=Ismail |title=CAIR Says ICJ Should Probe Israeli Massacre of Bound Palestinians Dumped in Mass Grave |url=https://www.cair.com/press_releases/cair-says-icj-should-probe-israeli-massacre-of-bound-palestinians-dumped-in-mass-grave/ |website=Council on American-Islamic Relations |access-date=1 February 2024}}</ref> The [[Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Expatriates (State of Palestine)|Palestinian Ministry of Foreign Affairs]] called it a "violation of all relevant international norms and laws".<ref>{{cite web |title=Palestinian foreign affairs ministry calls for investigation after discovery of mass grave |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/1/31/israels-war-on-gaza-live-severe-hunger-in-gaza-as-aid-trucks-surrounded?update=2665444 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=1 February 2024}}</ref> The Canadian-Palestinian former peace negotiator [[Diana Buttu]] stated the incident was "clearly a war crime".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Zhang |first1=Sharon |title=Palestinians Uncover Dozens Killed Execution-Style in Schoolyard in Gaza |url=https://truthout.org/articles/palestinians-uncover-dozens-killed-execution-style-in-schoolyard-in-gaza/ |website=Truthout |date=2 February 2024 |access-date=3 February 2024}}</ref> In March 2024, a man in [[Zeitoun, Gaza|Zeitoun]] was deliberately run over by an Israeli tank while handcuffed, according to the Euro-Med Human Rights Monitor.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israeli tanks have deliberately run over dozens of Palestinian civilians alive |url=https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/israeli-tanks-have-deliberately-run-over-dozens-palestinian-civilians-alive-enar |website=ReliefWeb |date=4 March 2024 |publisher=Euro-Med Monitor |access-date=6 March 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Euro-Med Monitor: Israeli tanks ran over dozens of Palestinians |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/3/israels-war-on-gaza-live-every-minute-counts-as-hunger-kills-in-gaza?update=2745754 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=6 March 2024}}</ref>

Footage obtained by Al Jazeera English showed two men waving white flags being killed by Israeli forces, then buried by army bulldozers.<ref>{{cite web |title=More on shooting of two men in Gaza by Israeli forces |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/27/israels-war-on-gaza-live-rafah-bombing-intensifies-despite-un-truce-call?update=2802953 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=30 March 2024}}</ref> The IDF confirmed the killing of the two men, stating they had been acting in a "suspicious manner" and didn't respond to warning shots; they said they buried them with bulldozers as they feared they were carrying explosives.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Lister |first1=Tim |last2=Goodwin |first2=Allegra |last3=Mezzofiore |first3=Gianluca |last4=Salman |first4=Abeer |last5=Stambaugh |first5=Alex |last6=Murphy |first6=Paul P. |title=Israel admits killing 2 Palestinians and then burying them with a bulldozer after shocking video surfaces |url=https://www.cnn.com/middleeast/live-news/israel-hamas-war-gaza-news-03-29-24/h_ee1132d10e9161991d227bb90a32d120 |website=CNN |date=29 March 2024 |access-date=30 March 2024}}</ref> The Palestine Red Crescent Society condemned Israel's actions as "extrajudicial killings".<ref>{{cite web |title=PRCS says Israel must be held accountable after unarmed Palestinians shot in Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/28/israels-war-on-gaza-live-unarmed-palestinians-killed-buried-by-bulldozer?update=2803835 |access-date=2 April 2024}}</ref> The Council on American-Islamic Relations called the killings a "heinous war crime".<ref>{{cite web |title=CAIR calls for UN probe of unarmed Palestinians killed by Israeli army |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/28/israels-war-on-gaza-live-unarmed-palestinians-killed-buried-by-bulldozer?update=2803190 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=4 April 2024}}</ref>

On 27 November 2025, footage captured by journalists in [[Jenin]] showed two men, 26-year-old Al-Muntasir Mahmoud Qassem Abdullah and 37-year-old Youssef Ali Youssef Asasa, shot to death after surrendering themselves to Israeli forces during a "counterterrorism" operation in the city.<ref>{{cite news|title= Israeli military kills two men after they appeared to surrender during operation in West Bank |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2025/11/27/middleeast/jenin-west-bank-israeli-military-men-killed-intl-latam|work=CNN|date=27 November 2025|last1=Dahman|first1=Ibrahim|last2=Yosef|first2=Eugenia|last3=Danaher|first3=Caitlin|access-date=28 November 2025}}</ref> According to the [[Palestinian Islamic Jihad]] (PIJ), both men were fighters for its armed wing, [[Al-Quds Brigades]].<ref>{{cite news|title= Video shows Israeli forces shooting Palestinians dead moments after surrender|url= https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/nov/28/video-shows-israeli-forces-shooting-palestinians-dead-moments-after-surrender|work=The Guardian|date=28 November 2025|last=Borger|first=Julian|access-date=28 November 2025}}</ref> According to Palestinian journalist, [[Nour Odeh]], the men "pulled their shirts up, showing that they were unarmed" before the Israeli military told them to return into the building that they were holed up in.<ref>{{cite news|date=27 November 2025|title= Israeli troops kill two Palestinians in Jenin as they try to surrender|url= https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/11/27/israeli-troops-kill-two-palestinians-in-jenin-as-they-try-to-surrender|work=Al Jazeera|access-date=28 November 2025}}</ref> The Palestinian Authority accused Israel of committing a "war crime" and described the killings as "brutal field executions".<ref>{{cite news|title= Israeli troops kill two Palestinians after they appear to surrender|url= https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c8dyqzm0rp4o|work=BBC News|date=27 November 2025|last1=Donnison|first1=Jon|last2=Faulkner|first2=Doug|access-date=28 November 2025}}</ref> [[Husam Zomlot]], the Palestinian ambassador to the United Kingdom, stated on [[Twitter|X]], labelled the incident as "summary executions" and said that it was a "war crime part of a pattern across the occupied territory".<ref>{{cite news|date=28 November 2025|title= Video appears to show Israeli soldiers 'executing' two Palestinians in West Bank|url= https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-11-28/video-israeli-soldiers-executing-two-palestinians-in-west-bank/106076150|work=ABC News (Australia)|access-date=28 November 2025}}</ref>

=== Surrendered Israeli hostages ===
{{Further|Killing of Alon Shamriz, Yotam Haim, and Samer Talalka}}
On 15 December, the IDF released a statement announcing that they had killed three of their own hostages by [[friendly fire]]. According to the Israeli military, they "mistakenly identified three Israeli hostages as a threat" during operations in [[Shuja'iyya]] and subsequently fired at them, killing them.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Tabachnick |first1=Cara |date=15 December 2023 |title=3 hostages in Gaza were killed by friendly fire, Israeli military says - CBS News |work=www.cbsnews.com |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/3-hostages-in-gaza-killed-by-friendly-fire-israeli-military-says/ |access-date=15 December 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=15 December 2023 |title=Israel-Hamas war live updates: IDF says it mistakenly killed 3 Israeli hostages during fighting |language=en |work=NBC News |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/news/world/live-blog/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-rcna129901 |access-date=15 December 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=IDF troops mistakenly open fire and kill 3 hostages in northern Gaza battlefield |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/idf-troops-mistakenly-open-fire-and-kill-3-hostages-in-northern-gaza-battlefield/ |publisher=Times of Israel}}</ref> According to an Israeli military official on 16 December, the three hostages were shirtless and waving a [[white flag]]. The official claimed that one soldier responded to this by "open[ing] fire" and "declar[ing] that they're terrorists"; more Israeli forces fired, killing two hostages "immediately" and wounding the third hostage, who appealed for help in Hebrew.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Lubell |first1=Maayan |date=16 December 2023 |title=Israeli hostages killed in Gaza were holding white flag, official says |work=[[Reuters]] |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israeli-hostages-killed-mistakenly-gaza-were-holding-white-flag-official-says-2023-12-16/ |access-date=16 December 2023}}</ref> The wounded hostage was pursued into a nearby building by IDF soldiers, where he was killed despite continued pleas for help.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Beaumont |first=Peter |date=16 December 2023 |title=IDF says Israeli hostages it killed in Gaza were bare chested and waving white flag |language=en-GB |work=The Observer |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/16/idf-says-hostages-it-killed-were-bare-chested-and-waving-white-flag |access-date= |issn=0029-7712}}</ref> Though he claimed that the soldiers were "under pressure" when this happened, Lieutenant General [[Herzi Halevi]] also stated that "It is forbidden to shoot at someone who raises a white flag and seeks to surrender", a sentiment echoed by the former head of [[Mossad]], [[Danny Yatom]].<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Said |first1=Summer |last2=Cloud |first2=David S. |last3=Keller-Lynn |first3=Carrie |date=16 December 2023 |title=Israel Says Its Soldiers Killed Israeli Hostages as They Held Up White Flag |url=https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/israel-and-qatar-explore-revival-of-deal-for-gaza-hostages-ff7af151 |website=WSJ}}</ref> [[Nahum Barnea]] wrote that the killing of the hostages, unarmed and waving a white flag, was a "war crime" and that "international law is very clear on the issue".<ref>{{cite web | last=Erlanger | first=Steven | title=Gaza Hostage Deaths Weaken Netanyahu's Grip on Power | website=The New York Times | date=17 December 2023 | url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/17/world/middleeast/netanyahu-israel-gaza-hostages-politics.html | access-date=18 December 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite news | last=ברנע | first=נחום | title=בשג'אעיה זו לא הייתה רק טרגדיה | website=ynet | date=16 December 2023 | url=https://www.ynet.co.il/news/article/yokra13720297 | language=he | access-date=18 December 2023}}</ref> A preliminary IDF investigation found the soldiers were told to open fire on all fighting-age men who approached them, after a number of incidents where militants disguised themselves as civilians to approach soldiers.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Bohbot |first1=Amir |title=IDF troops who killed hostages told to shoot fighting-age men in Gaza - report |url=https://www.jpost.com/israel-hamas-war/article-778896 |website=The Jerusalem Post |date=25 December 2023 |access-date=27 December 2023}}</ref>

==Perfidy by the IDF==
{{Further|Perfidy}}

===Israeli forces disguised as civilians===
On 30 January 2024, Israeli forces entered the [[Ibn Sina Specialized Hospital|Ibn Sina hospital]] in [[Jenin]] disguised as medics and civilians while carrying concealed rifles.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Tufaha |first1=Aref |title=Israeli forces dressed as women and medics kill 3 militants in West Bank hospital |url=https://apnews.com/article/israel-hamas-war-news-01-30-2024-b1ba33c7c0c5c62f85932a20c2a0bc92 |website=Associated Press |date=30 January 2024 |access-date=31 January 2024}}</ref> After entering the hospital they drew their weapons and killed three militants — one member of [[Hamas]] and two members of Palestinian Islamic Jihad — one of whom was a patient.<ref>{{Cite magazine |date=30 January 2024 |title=IDF Storms Jenin Hospital, Killing 3 Palestinian Militants |url=https://time.com/6589954/israel-deadly-raid-ibn-sina-hospital/ |access-date=7 February 2024 |magazine=TIME |language=en |archive-date=6 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240206010808/https://time.com/6589954/israel-deadly-raid-ibn-sina-hospital/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Israeli Security Forces may have violated international law in West Bank hospital raid, experts say |url=https://abcnews.go.com/International/idf-may-have-violated-international-law-west-bank-hospital-raid/story?id=106810456 |access-date=7 February 2024 |website=ABC News |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Al-Shalchi |first1=Hadeel |title=Israeli forces raid a West Bank hospital, killing three Palestinians |url=https://www.npr.org/2024/01/30/1227832688/israeli-forces-raid-west-bank-hospital-jenin |access-date=31 January 2024 |website=NPR|date=30 January 2024 }}</ref> The International Committee of the Red Cross expressed concern that the raid was a violation of international humanitarian law.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Berg |first1=Raffi |title=Israeli forces kill three Palestinian fighters in West Bank hospital raid |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-68137050 |website=BBC |date=30 January 2024 |access-date=31 January 2024}}</ref> Aurel Sari, a professor at the [[University of Exeter]], stated, "By disguising themselves as civilians and as medical personnel, the Israeli forces involved in the operation appear to have resorted to [[perfidy]] in violation of the applicable rules."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Fahim |first1=Kareem |title=Israeli agents disguised as doctors, patients kill 3 at West Bank hospital |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2024/01/30/israel-forces-jenin-hospital-raid-west-bank/ |newspaper=The Washington Post |access-date=31 January 2024}}</ref> Tom Dannenbaum, a professor of international law, stated, "Someone who is paralyzed is incapacitated in that respect, so an attack on that individual would be prohibited. Violating that prohibition would be a war crime."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Kaufman |first1=Ellie |title=IDF may have violated international law in West Bank hospital raid, experts say |url=https://abcnews.go.com/International/idf-may-have-violated-international-law-west-bank-hospital-raid/story?id=106810456 |website=ABC News |access-date=31 January 2024}}</ref> The Palestinian Ministry of Foreign Affairs called the shootings a [[crime against humanity]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel undercover agents kill 3 Palestinians in West Bank hospital |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20240130-israel-undercover-agents-kill-3-palestinians-in-west-bank-hospital |website=France24 |date=30 January 2024 |access-date=31 January 2024}}</ref> [[The Independent Commission for Human Rights]] called the attack "an assault on an institution protected by international law".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Nobani |first1=Ayman |title=Assassination in Jenin hospital a 'war crime': Palestinian rights group |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/1/30/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israeli-forces-detain-dozens-in-un-shelter-raid?update=2663231 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=31 January 2024}}</ref> [[OHCHR]] stated it was a "seemingly planned [[extrajudicial execution]]."<ref>{{cite web |title=Israeli Forces Strike Northern and Southern Gaza Amid Push for New Halt in Fighting |url=https://www.voanews.com/a/israeli-forces-strike-northern-and-southern-gaza-amid-push-for-new-halt-in-fighting-/7464643.html |website=VOA |date=31 January 2024 |access-date=1 February 2024}}</ref>

The IDF initially said the raid had been a "joint IDF, ISA, and Israel Police counterterrorism activity", and later said that none of their soldiers were physically present during the raid.<ref>{{Cite web |date=30 January 2024 |title=Israeli Security Forces may have violated international law in West Bank hospital raid, experts say |url=https://abcnews.go.com/International/idf-may-have-violated-international-law-west-bank-hospital-raid/story?id=106810456 |website=ABC News}}</ref> A panel of human rights experts appointed by the [[UN Human Rights Council]] stated the raid could constitute a war crime and recommended an investigation.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel Undercover Killings In West Bank Hospital May Be War Crime: UN Experts |url=https://www.barrons.com/news/israel-undercover-killings-in-west-bank-hospital-may-be-war-crime-un-experts-1863421f?refsec=topics_afp-news |website=Barron's |publisher=Agence France Presse |access-date=11 February 2024}}</ref>

In June 2024, UN experts condemned Israel's use of perfidy during the [[Nuseirat refugee camp massacre]], stating Israeli forces "entered Nuseirat disguised as displaced persons and aid workers in a humanitarian truck. They violently raided the area, assaulting residents with intense ground and air attacks that spread terror, death and despair."<ref>{{cite web |title=UN experts condemn outrageous disregard for Palestinian civilians during Israel's military operation in Nuseirat |url=https://www.un.org/unispal/document/un-experts-gaza-condemnation-14jun24/#:~:text=On%208%20June%2C%20Israeli%20Occupation,spread%20terror%2C%20death%20and%20despair. |website=United Nations |access-date=16 June 2024}}</ref>

===Use of human shields===
{{further|Human shields in the Israeli–Palestinian conflict#2023–2024 Israel–Hamas war}}
On 17 January 2024, Israeli soldiers were recorded using a Palestinian shop-owner in [[Dura, Hebron]], West Bank, as a human shield.<ref>{{cite web |title=Palestinian shop-owner used as human shield by Israeli forces |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/program/newsfeed/2024/1/17/palestinian-shop-owner-used-as-human-shield-by-israeli-forces#:~:text=A%20Palestinian%20shop%2Downer%20was,there%20for%20almost%20two%20decades. |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=20 January 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Shawer |first1=Mosab |title=West Bank human shield describes '100 breathless minutes' held by Israel |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2024/1/31/west-bank-human-shield-describes-100-breathless-minutes-held-by-israel |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=3 February 2024}}</ref> In an interview with ''[[Reuters]]'', the shop-owner stated, "He (the first soldier) told me that he will use me as a human shield, that young people shouldn't hurl stones."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Holton |first1=Kate |title=Palestinian says Israeli soldiers used him as human shield in West Bank |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/palestinian-says-israeli-soldiers-used-him-human-shield-west-bank-2024-01-16/ |website=Reuters |access-date=20 January 2024}}</ref> On 9 February, the [[Palestinian Red Crescent Society]] stated that an ambulance crew in [[Beita, Nablus]], West Bank had been detained by Israeli forces and used as human shields.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Nobani |first1=Ayman |title=Palestinian ambulance crew 'detained' while trying to help victims of Israeli West Bank shooting |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/9/israels-war-on-gaza-live-fear-in-rafah-as-israel-prepares-ground-attack?update=2695221 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=11 February 2024}}</ref> A 21-year-old man from [[Gaza City]] stated to ''Al Jazeera'' that he had been used as a human shield by Israeli forces.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Humaid |first1=Maram |title='Beaten, stripped, used as human shield': Gaza victim recalls Israel terror |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2024/2/23/beaten-stripped-used-as-a-human-shield-gaza-man-recounts-israel-terror |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=24 February 2024}}</ref> In June 2024, Israeli forces tied a wounded man to the front of their jeep, eliciting condemnation for the IDF's use of Palestinian human shields.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Rahaman Sarkar |first1=Alisha |title=Israeli troops strap injured Palestinian to jeep in West Bank as strikes kill 39 in Gaza |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/middle-east/israel-military-tie-palestine-jeep-west-bank-gaza-b2567270.html |website=The Independent |access-date=2 July 2024}}</ref> In July 2024, footage showed Israeli soldiers apparently using Palestinian human shields to enter buildings.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Khoury |first1=Jack |title=Israeli Soldiers Filmed Using Detainees in Gaza as 'Human Shields' |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240702014501/https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2024-07-01/ty-article/report-israeli-soldiers-filmed-using-detainees-in-gaza-as-human-shields/00000190-6f2b-d6fc-afba-ef7b8ad20000|archive-date=2 July 2024|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2024-07-01/ty-article/report-israeli-soldiers-filmed-using-detainees-in-gaza-as-human-shields/00000190-6f2b-d6fc-afba-ef7b8ad20000 |website=Haaretz |access-date=9 July 2024}}</ref>

In August 2024, sources stated that Israeli forces were using Palestinians as human shields when they entered tunnels and buildings in Gaza.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Kobowitz |first1=Yaniv |last2=Hauser |first2=Michael |title=תחקיר "הארץ": צה"ל מפעיל אזרחים פלסטינים כמגינים אנושיים לסריקת מנהרות ומבנים בעזה |url=https://www.haaretz.co.il/news/magazine/2024-08-13/ty-article-magazine/.premium/00000191-4adf-d633-a393-cfff82830000 |website=Haaretz |language=he|access-date=17 August 2024}}</ref> An investigation found that Israeli regularly used Palestinian human shields in the Gaza Strip to avoid putting Israeli soldiers in danger.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Odenheimer |first1=Natan |last2=Shbair |first2=Bilal |last3=Kingsley |first3=Patrick |title=How Israel's Army Uses Palestinians as Human Shields in Gaza |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/14/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-military-human-shields.html |website=The New York Times |date=14 October 2024 |access-date=19 October 2024}}</ref>

In February 2025, according to a report by Israeli outlet 'the Hottest Place in Hell', in May 2024, an IDF officer used an 80-year-old Palestinian man as a human shield to inspect in Gaza for booby traps, while threatening to blow off his head by tying an IED command-wire to his neck. Later, the elderly man and his wife were shot dead by Israeli forces.<ref>{{cite news|title= IDF Reportedly Used Elderly Gazan as Human Shield, Tied Explosive Around His Neck|url= https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2025-02-16/ty-article/idf-reportedly-used-elderly-gazan-as-human-shield-tied-explosive-around-his-neck/00000195-0e56-d1b4-a7fd-cf7742bf0000|work=Haaretz|date=16 February 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title= Israeli soldiers used an 80-year-old Gazan as a human shield. Then they killed him|url= https://www.972mag.com/gaza-human-shield-mosquito/|website=+972 Magazine|last=Pe'ery|first=Illy|date= 16 February 2025|access-date=16 February 2025}}</ref>

According to ''Haaretz'', an anonymous senior IDF officer revealed that the Israeli army used Palestinians as human shields at least six times per day and stressed that each brigade has at least 36 human shields.<ref>{{cite web|title= In Gaza, Almost Every IDF Platoon Keeps a Human Shield, a Sub-army of Palestinian Slaves|url= https://www.haaretz.com/opinion/2025-03-30/ty-article-opinion/.premium/in-gaza-almost-every-idf-platoon-keeps-a-human-shield-a-sub-army-of-palestinian-slaves/00000195-e627-deaf-a397-f6674e390000?lts=1743398343406|website=Haaretz|access-date=30 March 2025}}</ref>

