==Arms transfers==
{{see also|Nicaragua v. Germany}}
States transferring weapons to Israel faced charges of violations of international law. In February 2024, a group of more than a dozen [[United Nations special rapporteur]]s stated that any export of weapons or munitions to Israel was "likely to violate international humanitarian law."<ref>{{Cite news |title=UN rights officials call for Israel arms embargo; FM: They're cooperating with Hamas |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/un-rights-officials-call-for-israel-arms-embargo-fm-theyre-cooperating-with-hamas/ |website=[[The Times of Israel]] |access-date=4 March 2024 |issn=0040-7909}}</ref> The UN experts stated that parties signed to the [[Arms Trade Treaty]] have additional obligations to deny arms exports if the weapons could be used for serious violations of international humanitarian law.<ref name="OHCHR230224"/> The group called for an [[arms embargo]].<ref>{{cite web |title=UN Experts Call for Arms Embargo Against Israel Over Gaza War |url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2024-02-24/ty-article/un-experts-call-for-arms-embargo-against-israel-over-gaza-war/0000018d-dba2-d47b-a1af-dff6bda60000 |website=Haaretz |access-date=4 March 2024}}</ref> In a statement, [[Human Rights Watch]] stated that the [[United Kingdom]]'s refusal to suspend arms transfer to Israel put it "at risk of failing to prevent and being complicit in serious violations of international law, including war crimes and crimes against humanity".<ref>{{cite web |title=UK Government's Public Position on Weapons Licences to Israel Inconsistent, Explanation Requested |url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2024/02/28/uk-governments-public-position-weapons-licences-israel-inconsistent-explanation |website=Human Rights Watch |date=28 February 2024 |access-date=4 March 2024}}</ref> In March 2024, [[Government of Nicaragua|Nicaragua]] filed a [[Nicaragua v. Germany|lawsuit]] at the [[International Court of Justice]] against [[Government of Germany|Germany]], stating that its financial and military support to Israel was facilitating genocide in Gaza.<ref>{{cite web |title=Nicaragua says Germany facilitates genocide by aiding Israel |url=https://www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-says-germany-facilitates-genocide-by-aiding-israel/a-68422846 |website=DW |access-date=4 March 2024}}</ref>

Canadian Foreign Minister [[Melanie Joly]] was sued by the Canadian Lawyers for International Human Rights group for authorizing the export of weapons used by Israel to violate international law.<ref name="Yousif050324">{{cite web |last1=Yousif |first1=Nadine |title=Canada faces lawsuit over military exports to Israel |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-us-canada-68451085 |website=BBC |date=5 March 2024 |access-date=8 March 2024}}</ref> Soon after, Joly stated the Canadian government was no longer issuing new weapons export licenses to the Israeli military.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Ljunggren |first1=David |title=Canadian freeze on new arms export permits to Israel to stay |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/canadian-freeze-new-arms-export-permits-israel-stay-2024-03-20/ |website=Reuters |access-date=24 March 2024}}</ref> The [[Government of Denmark]] was sued by Oxfam, Amnesty International, Action Aid, and Al-Haq for their arms transfers to Israel, with the organizations stating, "Denmark violates international rules on arms trade and risks becoming complicit in violations of international humanitarian law – including war crimes – and a plausible genocide."<ref>{{cite web |title=Denmark: NGOs sue the Danish state to stop arms exports to Israel |url=https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2024/03/denmark-ngos-sue-the-danish-state-to-stop-arms-exports-to-israel/ |website=Amnesty International |date=12 March 2024 |access-date=15 March 2024}}</ref> In March 2024, Human Rights Watch and [[Oxfam]] stated that Israel was committing violations of international humanitarian law with weapons provided by the United States.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israeli Assurances to Use US Arms Legally Are Not Credible |url=https://www.hrw.org/news/2024/03/19/israeli-assurances-use-us-arms-legally-are-not-credible |website=Human Rights Watch |date=19 March 2024 |access-date=22 March 2024}}</ref>

In March 2024, the [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservative Party]] [[Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office|UK Foreign Office]] minister [[Andrew Mitchell]] stated Israeli compliance with international humanitarian law was under review. UK shadow foreign secretary [[David Lammy]] stated arms export licenses should be denied if "there is a clear risk that the items might be used to commit or facilitate a serious violation of international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Wintour |first1=Patrick |title=Cameron urged to publish Foreign Office legal advice on Israel's war in Gaza |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/22/david-cameron-urged-publish-foreign-office-legal-advice-israel-war-gaza |website=The Guardian |date=22 March 2024 |access-date=24 March 2024 |ref=none}}</ref> 600 UK lawyers, including three former justices of the [[Supreme Court of the United Kingdom]], stated the UK's arming of Israel was a breach of international law.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Siddique |first1=Haroon |last2=Courea |first2=Eleni |last3=Wintour |first3=Patrick |title=Former supreme court judges say UK arming Israel breaches international law |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/03/former-supreme-court-judges-say-uk-arming-israel-breaches-international-law |website=The Guardian |date=3 April 2024 |access-date=6 April 2024 |ref=none}}</ref> Following reports that month that the UK Foreign Office found Israel had violated international humanitarian law, [[Geoffrey Nice]] stated, "Countries supplying arms to Israel may now be complicit in criminal warfare."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Helm |first1=Toby |title=UK government lawyers say Israel is breaking international law, claims top Tory in leaked recording |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/30/uk-government-lawyers-say-israel-is-breaking-international-law-claims-top-tory-in-leaked-recording |website=The Guardian |date=30 March 2024 |access-date=6 April 2024}}</ref>

In May 2024, [[Amnesty International]] called on all states to cease weapons transfers to Israel and Palestine while there is "a risk they could be used to commit or facilitate serious violations of international law".<ref>{{cite web |title=Amnesty calls on 'all states' to halt weapons transfers to Israel, Palestinian groups |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/5/9/israels-war-on-gaza-live-biden-admits-israel-used-us-bombs-on-civilians?update=2890729 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=14 May 2024}}</ref> In June 2024, a group of thirty UN experts stated arms and ammunitions manufacturers transferring weapons to Israel may be complicit in violations of international law.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Tétrault-Farber |first1=Gabrielle |title=UN experts say firms sending arms to Israel could be complicit in abuses |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/un-experts-say-firms-sending-arms-israel-could-be-complicit-abuses-2024-06-20/#:~:text=GENEVA%2C%20June%2020%20(Reuters),and%20violations%20of%20international%20law. |website=Reuters |access-date=29 June 2024}}</ref>

== International reactions ==
{{See also|International reactions to the Gaza war}}

===Governments===
====Heads of state====
Numerous [[heads of state]] criticized Israel's war crimes. Turkish president Recep Tayyip Erdoğan criticized Western countries for their complicity as Israel committed war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/turkeys-erdogan-says-israels-netanyahu-will-be-tried-war-criminal-2023-12-04/ |title=Turkey's Erdogan says Israel's Netanyahu 'will be tried as war criminal' |agency=Reuters |date=4 December 2023 | quote=...([[OIC]]) committee meeting in Istanbul, Erdogan said the Western nations supporting Israel were giving it 'unconditional support to kill babies' and were complicit in its crimes. |access-date=23 April 2025}}</ref> Colombian President [[Gustavo Petro]] termed Israel's campaign as a genocide.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Rueda |first1=Manuel |title=Israel suspends military exports to Colombia over its president's criticism of Gaza siege |work=[[Associated Press]] |url=https://apnews.com/article/colombia-israel-petro-suspend-defense-exports-a92effbb531ea4631d25a8c1d32ede28 |url-status=live |access-date=20 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022012058/https://apnews.com/article/colombia-israel-petro-suspend-defense-exports-a92effbb531ea4631d25a8c1d32ede28 |archive-date=22 October 2023}}</ref> Egyptian President [[Abdel Fattah al-Sisi]] and [[King Abdullah II]] of Jordan both condemned the collective punishment of Gaza.<ref>{{cite web |title=Egypt's Sisi, Jordan King Condemn 'Collective Punishment' In Gaza |url=https://www.barrons.com/news/egypt-s-sisi-to-host-jordan-king-on-thursday-presidency-dfd741c6 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022012058/https://www.barrons.com/news/egypt-s-sisi-to-host-jordan-king-on-thursday-presidency-dfd741c6 |archive-date=22 October 2023 |access-date=21 October 2023 |website=Barron's |publisher=Agence France Presse}}</ref> Irish President [[Michael D. Higgins]] demanded the [[al-Ahli Arab Hospital explosion]] be investigated as a war crime.{{efn|The perpetrator of this alleged war crime is disputed. While not a definitive conclusion, as of 23 October 2023, independent analysts asserted the explosion was caused by an errant rocket fired from within Gaza.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Danner |first=Chas |date=23 October 2023 |title=Everything We Know About the Gaza City Hospital Blast |url=https://nymag.com/intelligencer/2023/10/israel-hamas-war-everything-we-know-about-the-gaza-hospital-blast.html |access-date=27 October 2023 |website=Intelligencer |language=en |archive-date=27 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231027104051/https://nymag.com/intelligencer/2023/10/israel-hamas-war-everything-we-know-about-the-gaza-hospital-blast.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Logan |first=Nick |date=26 October 2023 |title=Why open-source intelligence can help and hinder understanding of what's happening in Gaza, Israel |url=https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/israel-gaza-what-is-osint-1.7008509 |website=CBC |access-date=27 October 2023 |archive-date=27 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231027184953/https://www.cbc.ca/amp/1.7008509 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=23 October 2023 |title=Ep 38 - Fog of War |url=https://www.abc.net.au/mediawatch/episodes/war/103011298 |access-date=27 October 2023 |website=Media Watch |publisher=abc.net.au |language=en-AU |archive-date=27 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231027175156/https://www.abc.net.au/mediawatch/episodes/war/103011298 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}<ref>{{cite news |last1=O’Leary |first1=Naomi |last2=McGreevy |first2=Ronan |title=Gaza hospital explosion should be 'investigated as a war crime' - Michael D Higgins |url=https://www.irishtimes.com/ireland/2023/10/18/gaza-hospital-explosion-should-be-investigated-as-a-war-crime-higgins-says/ |newspaper=The Irish Times |access-date=21 February 2024}}</ref> Chilean President [[Gabriel Boric]] condemned Israel's "collective punishment" the Gazan civilian population.<ref>{{cite web|title=Chile recalls its ambassador to Israel over 'unacceptable' violations in Gaza|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/1/israel-hamas-war-live-anger-grows-over-israeli-attack-on-gaza-refugee-camp?update=2453013|publisher=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]] |access-date=1 November 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/chile-recalls-israel-ambassador-talks-after-gaza-attacks-2023-11-01/ |title=Chile recalls Israel ambassador for talks after Gaza attacks |date=1 November 2023 |agency=Reuters |access-date=19 April 2025}}</ref> South African President [[Cyril Ramaphosa]] condemned the collective punishment of Gaza.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Ramaphosa |first1=Cyril |title=Peace will not be possible until Palestinians are free |url=https://www.thepresidency.gov.za/from-the-desk-of-the-president/desk-president-monday%2C-16-october-2023 |access-date=25 October 2023 |website=The Presidency of the Republic of South Africa |archive-date=5 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231205102331/https://www.thepresidency.gov.za/from-the-desk-of-the-president/desk-president-monday%2C-16-october-2023 |url-status=dead }}</ref> Brazilian President [[Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva]] stated, "It's not a war, it's a genocide."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Verdélio |first1=Andreia |title=President Lula says war in the Middle East is genocide |url=https://agenciabrasil.ebc.com.br/en/politica/noticia/2023-10/president-lula-says-war-middle-east-genocide |access-date=26 October 2023 |website=Agência Brasil|date=25 October 2023 }}</ref>

Belgian deputy Prime Minister [[Petra De Sutter]] called for sanctions against Israel and an EU ban on countries responsible for war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |title=Deputy PM calls on Belgian government to sanction Israel |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/8/israel-hamas-war-live-humanitarian-aid-targeted-amid-gaza-bombardment?update=2472173 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=8 November 2023}}</ref> On 10 November 2023, Norwegian prime minister [[Jonas Gahr Støre]] stated Israel's actions violated international laws of war.<ref>{{cite web |title=Norwegian prime minister questions how Gaza war will create long-term security |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/10/israel-hamas-war-live-fears-grow-for-palestinians-at-gaza-hospitals?update=2477481 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=10 November 2023}}</ref> Spanish Prime Minister [[Pedro Sanchez]] described the Israeli actions in Gaza as "indiscriminate killing" and stated he had "serious doubts" Israel was following international law.<ref>{{cite news |title=Spain PM Sanchez angers Israel with comments on Gaza again |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/spain-pm-sanchez-says-he-doubts-israel-respects-humanitarian-law-2023-11-30 |website=Reuters |date=30 November 2023 |access-date=1 December 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Spain PM urges Israel to end 'indiscriminate killing' in Gaza |url=https://www.tbsnews.net/world/israeli-army-detaining-200-palestinians-al-shifa-739882 |website=The Business Standard |date=15 November 2023 |access-date=16 November 2023}}</ref> Palestinian president [[Mahmoud Abbas]] called Israel actions in Gaza a genocide.<ref>{{cite web |title=Abbas: Israel's war on Gaza is 'genocide' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/15/israel-hamas-war-live-israel-says-it-plans-to-raid-al-shifa-ministry?update=2488711 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=16 November 2023}}</ref> Irish PM [[Leo Varadkar]] stated Israel was committing collective punishment.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Everett |first1=Mariamne |title=As Israel bombs Gaza, Ireland's enduring support of Palestine gets stronger |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/11/17/as-israel-bombs-gaza-irelands-enduring-support-of-palestine-gets-stronger |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=17 November 2023}}</ref> Qatari prime minister [[Mohammed bin Abdulrahman bin Jassim Al Thani]] called for an international investigation into Israeli war crimes.<ref>{{cite news |title=Qatar PM demands investigation into Israeli 'crimes' |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2023/12/03/israel-hamas-war-latest-news1/ |website=The Telegraph |date=3 December 2023 |access-date=4 December 2023 |last1=Barber |first1=Harriet }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Qatar PM demands investigation into Israeli 'crimes' |url=https://www.ynetnews.com/article/hjjl00mcbp |newspaper=Ynetnews |date=3 December 2023 |access-date=4 December 2023}}</ref> On 12 December 2023, [[Joe Biden]] described Israel's attacks as "indiscriminate".<ref>{{cite news |last1=Kim |first1=Victoria |title=The U.S. criticizes Israel for 'indiscriminate' bombing in Gaza. |work=The New York Times |date=13 December 2023 |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/13/world/middleeast/us-criticizes-israel-for-indiscriminate-bombing-in-gaza.html |access-date=13 December 2023}}</ref>

====Foreign ministers====
Chinese Foreign Minister [[Wang Yi (politician)|Wang Yi]] stated Israel was collectively punishing Gaza.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Burke |first1=Jason |title=China and Russia harden positions on Gaza as war stirs geopolitical tensions |work=[[The Guardian]] |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/16/china-russia-harden-positions-gaza-war-geopolitical-tensions |url-status=live |access-date=20 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022012058/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/16/china-russia-harden-positions-gaza-war-geopolitical-tensions |archive-date=22 October 2023}}</ref> Indonesian Foreign Minister [[Retno Marsudi]] described Israeli actions in Gaza as crimes against humanity.<ref>{{cite web |title=Indonesia Urges UN Security Council to Immediately End War in Gaza |url=https://kemlu.go.id/portal/en/read/5422/berita/indonesia-urges-un-security-council-to-immediately-end-war-in-gaza |access-date=25 October 2023 |website=Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Indonesia}}</ref> [[Abdulla Shahid]], Foreign Minister of the Maldives, warned the [[evacuation of northern Gaza]] could amount to the "war crime of forcible transfer".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Shahid |first1=Abdulla |title=X post by Abdulla Shahid |url=https://twitter.com/abdulla_shahid/status/1713009833887277425?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1713009833887277425%7Ctwgr%5E0348de3b57b6843dc7710f22f71cc2e0b410c9ad%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fthediplomaticinsight.com%2Fmaldives-reiterates-support-for-palestine%2F |access-date=25 October 2023 |website=X}}</ref> [[Iran]]ian Foreign Minister [[Hossein Amirabdollahian]] described the events as genocide and a crime against humanity.<ref>{{cite web |title=Iranian FM writes to UN Human Rights Chief, calls for measures to stop "Gaza genocide" |url=https://en.mfa.ir/portal/newsview/732546/Iranian-FM-writes-to-UN-Human-Rights-Chief-calls-for-measures-to-stop-“Gaza-genocide |access-date=26 October 2023 |website=Islamic Republic of Iran Ministry of Foreign Affairs}}</ref> Russian Foreign Minister [[Sergei Lavrov]] criticized Israel's "indiscriminate" force and "flagrant" violations of international humanitarian law, stating the conflict risked creating a crisis that would last "many decades, if not centuries".<ref>{{cite web |title=Russia says Israeli bombardment of Gaza is against international law |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/10/28/russia-says-israeli-bombardment-of-gaza-is-against-international-law |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=28 October 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Russia calls for 'immediate end to bloodshed' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/16/israel-hamas-war-live-israel-rejects-un-security-council-gaza-resolution?update=2491771 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=16 November 2023}}</ref>

In October 2023, [[Faisal Mekdad]], Foreign Minister in Syria’s [[Assad regime]], termed Israeli actions as a genocide.<ref>{{cite web |title=Syria denounced Western support for Israel's massacre in Gaza |url=https://www.plenglish.com/news/2023/10/26/syria-denounced-western-support-for-israels-massacre-in-gaza/#:~:text=Damascus%2C%20Oct%2026%20(Prensa%20Latina,led%20by%20the%20United%20States. |access-date=26 October 2023 |website=Prensa Latina| date=26 October 2023 }}</ref> In a joint statement, the Foreign Ministers of nine Arab countries — the [[United Arab Emirates]], Jordan, [[Bahrain]], [[Saudi Arabia]], [[Oman]], [[Qatar]], [[Kuwait]], [[Egypt]] and [[Morocco]] — described Israeli actions as collective punishment.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Magid |first1=Jacob |title=9 Arab nations – including Saudi Arabia, Bahrain, Morocco – accuse Israel of 'collective punishment' |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/9-arab-nations-including-saudi-arabia-bahrain-morocco-accuse-israel-of-collective-punishment/ |access-date=26 October 2023 |website=The Times of Israel}}</ref> Oman's Foreign Minister, [[Sayyid Badr Albusaidi]], called for a war crimes investigation into Israeli action in Gaza.<ref>{{cite web |title=Oman calls for war crimes investigation into Israel |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/4/israel-hamas-war-live-20-dead-in-israeli-attack-on-school-ministry?update=2461488 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=4 November 2023}}</ref> Qatari foreign minister, Mohammed bin Abdulrahman bin Jassim Al Thani, stated Israel's Al-Shifa Hospital siege was a "war crime and a blatant violation of international laws".<ref>{{cite web |title=Qatar Calls For International Probe Into Israeli Raids On Gaza Hospitals |url=https://www.barrons.com/news/qatar-calls-for-international-probe-into-israeli-raids-on-gaza-hospitals-f6035c47 |website=Barron's |publisher=Agence France Presse |access-date=15 November 2023}}</ref> [[Ayman Safadi]], the Jordanian foreign minister, stated Israel's actions fit within the legal definition of genocide.<ref>{{cite news |title=Jordan's foreign minister: events in Gaza qualify as genocide |url=https://www.ynetnews.com/article/rkomyxzbt# |newspaper=Ynetnews |date=27 November 2023 |agency=Reuters |access-date=28 November 2023}}</ref> The [[Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Egypt)|Egyptian Foreign Ministry]] stated Israel was engaged in collective punishment through its sieges, indiscriminate targeting of civilians, and starvation.<ref>{{cite web |title=Egypt warns of Rafah invasion dangers |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/17/israels-war-on-gaza-live-13-aid-trucks-reach-north-malnutrition-doubles?update=2778470 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=19 March 2024}}</ref>

On 9 January 2024, [[David Cameron]], the British foreign secretary, stated he was "worried" Israel had breached international law in Gaza.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Francis |first1=Sam |title=David Cameron worried Israel may have broken international law in Gaza |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-politics-67929003 |website=BBC |date=9 January 2024 |access-date=10 January 2024}}</ref> On 14 January 2024, Cameron said that "Israel is acting in self-defence" and denied that Israel is committing war crimes in Gaza.<ref>{{cite news |title=Lord Cameron denies suggesting Israel has committed war crimes in Gaza |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/israel-cameron-international-court-of-justice-gaza-mps-b2478376.html |work=The Independent |date=14 January 2024}}</ref> On 14 February, Italian foreign minister [[Antonio Tajani]] described Israel's attack on Gaza as disproportionate.<ref>{{cite web |title=Italy says Israeli response to Hamas 'disproportionate' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/13/israels-war-on-gaza-live-jordans-king-urges-ceasefire-in-biden-meeting?update=2705128 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=15 February 2024}}</ref> [[Pietro Parolin]], the Vatican's [[Cardinal Secretary of State|Secretary of State]], described Israel's response as disproportionate.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel complains after Vatican denounces 'carnage' and disproportionate response |url=https://abcnews.go.com/International/wireStory/israel-complains-after-vatican-denounces-carnage-disproportionate-response-107254263 |website=ABC News |publisher=Associated Press |access-date=16 February 2024}}</ref> Quoting [[Giora Eiland]], the EU's top diplomat [[Josep Borrell]] stated Israel's objective appeared to be to "turn Gaza into a place that is temporarily or permanently impossible to live in".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Borrell |first1=Josep |title=Gaza: starvation and bloodbath |url=https://www.eeas.europa.eu/eeas/gaza-starvation-and-bloodbath_en |website=European Union External Action |publisher=European Union |access-date=10 March 2024}}</ref> Borrell later suggested the EU should consider sanctions on Israeli ministers [[Bezalel Smotrich]] and [[Itamar Ben-Gvir]] for "incitement to war crimes".<ref>{{cite web |title=EU's Borrell: Consider sanctions on Ben Gvir, Smotrich for 'incitement to war crimes' |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/eus-borrell-consider-sanctions-on-ben-gvir-smotrich-for-incitement-to-war-crimes/ |website=The Times of Israel |access-date=25 August 2024}}</ref> [[Micheál Martin]], the Irish foreign minister, stated the 7 October attacks and Israel's actions in Gaza both "represents the blatant violation of international humanitarian law on a mass scale".<ref>{{cite news |last1=Specia |first1=Megan |title=Ireland to Intervene in South Africa's Genocide Case Against Israel at the World Court |work=The New York Times |date=28 March 2024 |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/03/28/world/middleeast/ireland-south-africa-israel-genocide-icj.html#:~:text=“But%20I%20want%20to%20be,law%20on%20a%20mass%20scale.” |access-date=30 March 2024}}</ref>

====Other officials====
[[Ione Belarra]], the Spanish [[Ministry of Social Affairs (Spain)|minister of social rights]], accused the EU and the US of "being complicit in Israel's war crimes."<ref>{{cite web |title=Spanish Minister suggests taking Israel to ICC for 'war crimes' |url=https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20231016-spanish-minister-suggests-taking-israel-to-icc-for-war-crimes/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022012059/https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20231016-spanish-minister-suggests-taking-israel-to-icc-for-war-crimes/ |archive-date=22 October 2023 |access-date=20 October 2023 |website=[[Middle East Monitor]]|date=16 October 2023 }}</ref> Belarra further called for Israel to be denounced before the International Criminal Court for genocide in the Gaza Strip.<ref>{{multiref|{{cite web|url=https://www.commondreams.org/news/spain-netanyahu-war-crimes|title=Spanish Minister Says Netanyahu Should Be Brought Before ICC for War Crimes|date=16 October 2023|last=Johnson|first=Jake|work=[[Common Dreams]]|access-date=21 October 2023|archive-date=20 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231020213440/https://www.commondreams.org/news/spain-netanyahu-war-crimes|url-status=live}}|{{cite web|url=https://www.trt.net.tr/espanol/espana-y-america-latina/2023/10/16/belarra-netanyahu-debe-ser-juzgado-en-la-corte-penal-internacional-2051531|title=Belarra: ''Netanyahu debe ser juzgado en la Corte Penal Internacional''|trans-title=Belarra: ''Netanyahu must be tried at the International Criminal Court''|date=16 October 2023|language=Spanish|work=[[Turkish Radio and Television Corporation|TRT Español]]|access-date=21 October 2023|archive-date=17 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231017014411/https://www.trt.net.tr/espanol/espana-y-america-latina/2023/10/16/belarra-netanyahu-debe-ser-juzgado-en-la-corte-penal-internacional-2051531|url-status=live}}|{{cite web|url=https://www.sport.es/es/noticias/nacional/belarra-pide-sanchez-llevar-netanyahu-93388828|title=Belarra pide a Sánchez llevar a Netanyahu a la Corte Penal Internacional para juzgarle por crímenes de guerra|trans-title=Belarra asks Sánchez to take Netanyahu to the International Criminal Court to try him for war crimes|date=16 October 2023|language=Spanish|work=[[Sport.es]]|last=Cabanillas|first=Ana|access-date=21 October 2023|archive-date=19 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231019183738/https://www.sport.es/es/noticias/nacional/belarra-pide-sanchez-llevar-netanyahu-93388828|url-status=live}}}}</ref> Brazil’s [[Workers' Party (Brazil)|Workers Party]] officially classified Israeli actions in Gaza as genocide.<ref>{{Cite web |date=16 October 2023 |title=PT classifica como "genocídio" ação de Israel na Faixa de Gaza |url=https://www.poder360.com.br/partidos-politicos/pt-classifica-como-genocidio-acao-de-israel-na-faixa-de-gaza/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022012656/https://www.poder360.com.br/partidos-politicos/pt-classifica-como-genocidio-acao-de-israel-na-faixa-de-gaza/ |archive-date=22 October 2023 |access-date=17 October 2023 |website=Poder360 |language=pt-br}}</ref> The [[Parliament of Sri Lanka]] sent a letter to the UN secretary general, stating, Israel's "indiscriminate bombings in hospitals, amounts to a war crime under international law and the Geneva Convention."<ref>{{cite web |title='Brutal Israeli onslaught': Sri Lankan MPs call for ceasefire in Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/14/israel-hamas-war-live-israeli-attacks-displace-700000-children-in-gaza?update=2485448 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=14 November 2023}}</ref> U.S. officials reported alarm at Israeli claims of the "inevitability" of civilian deaths, after they used the [[atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki]] as historical examples.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Jobain |first1=Najib |last2=Kullab |first2=Samya |last3=Nessman |first3=Ravi |date=19 October 2023 |title=Gaza awaits aid from Egypt as Israel readies troops for ground assault |language=en |work=[[AP News]] |url=https://apnews.com/article/israel-palestinians-gaza-hamas-war-b084e9c453cc99f7bec6f66d7b5913d9 |access-date=21 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231019205146/https://apnews.com/article/israel-palestinians-gaza-hamas-war-b084e9c453cc99f7bec6f66d7b5913d9 |archive-date=19 October 2023}}</ref> On 20 December 2023, ''[[HuffPost]]'' reported US officials were urging Switzerland against a Geneva Convention conference.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Shahid Ahmed |first1=Akbar |title=Amid U.N. Security Council Intrigue, U.S. Privately Moves To Block Another Option For International Accountability For Gaza |url=https://www.huffpost.com/entry/un-security-council-us-block-accountability-international-gaza_n_6583338ce4b04da984257b9c#:~:text=The%20Biden%20administration%20is%20finalizing,violations%20of%20the%20Geneva%20Conventions. |website=HuffPost |date=20 December 2023 |access-date=21 December 2023}}</ref> Eran Etzion, the former deputy head of Israel's [[National Security Council (Israel)|National Security Council]], stated, "If a soldier or an officer is expected to commit something that might be suspected as a war crime, they must refuse."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Keane |first1=Fergal |title=IDF soldiers should refuse orders that may be war crimes, Israeli ex-security adviser tells BBC |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx24ngy9g70o |website=BBC News |date=23 October 2024 |access-date=27 October 2024}}</ref>

U.S. Senator [[Chris Van Hollen]] accused Israel of committing "textbook war crimes".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Suter |first1=Tara |title=Senate Democrat accuses Israel of 'textbook war crime' in Gaza |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4465080-senate-democrat-accuses-israel-textbook-war-crime-gaza/ |website=The Hill |date=13 February 2024 |access-date=4 March 2024}}</ref> French Senator [[Guillaume Gontard]] stated that the Israeli prime minister was "using hunger as a weapon" in Gaza.<ref>{{cite web |title=Netanyahu will go down in history for 'using hunger as a weapon' in Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/21/israels-war-on-gaza-live-more-than-100-palestinians-killed-in-24-hours?update=2786955 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=24 March 2024}}</ref> Australian Senator [[Mehreen Faruqi]] stated, "Israel is committing war crime after war crime in broad daylight and is getting away with it."<ref>{{cite web |title='Israel committing war crime after war crime in broad daylight': Australian senator |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/4/2/israels-war-on-gaza-live-five-aid-workers-killed-after-delivering-food?update=2812453 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=10 April 2024}}</ref>

[[Vanessa Frazier]], the Maltese ambassador to the UN, stated Israel's blocking of humanitarian aid "may amount to a crime against humanity and a war crime".<ref>{{cite web |title=Malta: denying aid 'may amount to crime against humanity' |url=https://www.newarab.com/news/least-100-killed-israeli-airstrikes-across-gaza |website=The New Arab |date=19 December 2023 |access-date=20 December 2023}}</ref> Qatari diplomat Sheikha [[Alya Ahmed Saif Al-Thani]] stated the Al-Shifa Hospital siege was a war crime.<ref>{{cite web |title=Qatar affirms bombing of Qatar Committee for Reconstruction of Gaza Headquarters will not deter it from providing assistance to the Strip |url=https://www.gulf-times.com/article/672015/qatar/qatar-affirms-bombing-of-qatar-committee-for-reconstruction-of-gaza-headquarters-will-not-deter-it-from-providing-assistance-to-the-strip |website=Gulf Times |date=18 November 2023 |access-date=18 November 2023}}</ref> [[Nicolas de Rivière]], the French ambassador to the United Nations, called for an immediate ceasefire, stating, "It has to stop. What’s happening right now is totally contrary to the Geneva Conventions."<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel's Rafah operation a 'red line'; must be in UN resolution: France |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/22/israels-war-on-gaza-live-the-choice-is-clear-a-2-state-solution?update=2791005 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=24 March 2024}}</ref> In a confidential memo, the Dutch defense attaché stated Israel was violating international law by "deliberately causing massive destruction to the infrastructure and civilian centers" of Gaza to restore deterrence against Iran and Hezbollah.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Chiappa |first1=Claudia |title=Israel wants to obliterate Gaza to deter Iran, Hezbollah, says Dutch memo |url=https://www.politico.eu/article/israel-hamas-war-dutch-memo-gaza-disproportionate-force-iran-hezbollah/ |website=Politico |date=14 November 2023 |access-date=12 October 2024}}</ref>

===Humanitarian organizations===
On 6 December, Oxfam stated the international community, and in particular, Israel's allies, were "complicit in the mass death, [[forcible displacement]], starvation and deprivation being inflicted upon more than 2 million people."<ref>{{cite web |title=Abject failure to forge ceasefire means international community complicit in unfolding catastrophe in Gaza |url=https://www.oxfam.org/en/press-releases/abject-failure-forge-ceasefire-means-international-community-complicit-unfolding# |website=Oxfam |date=6 December 2023 |access-date=7 December 2023}}</ref> The [[International Federation for Human Rights]] stated Israel's actions in Gaza constituted an unfolding genocide and called for the arrest of Israeli government officials.<ref>{{cite web |title=The unfolding genocide against the Palestinians must stop immediately |url=https://www.fidh.org/en/region/north-africa-middle-east/israel-palestine/the-unfolding-genocide-against-the-palestinians-must-stop-immediately |website=International Federation for Human Rights |access-date=13 December 2023}}</ref> A group of 31 Palestinian human rights organizations, led by [[Al-Haq]], wrote to UN chief António Guterres stating UN aid agencies were in breach of international law by aiding Israel's war objectives.<ref>{{cite web |title=Aiding Israel's War Objectives Practices of UN Aid Agencies in Gaza in Breach of International Humanitarian Law |url=https://www.alhaq.org/advocacy/22428.html |website=Al-Haq |access-date=23 December 2023}}</ref> The [[Norwegian Refugee Council]] stated any push of Gazans into Egypt would be a war crime or crime against humanity.<ref>{{cite web |title=Pushing people from Gaza into Egypt would constitute an 'atrocity crime': NRC |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/12/27/israel-hamas-war-live-israel-vows-to-intensify-gaza-fighting?update=2582515 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=27 December 2023}}</ref> The [[Non-Aligned Movement]], a body of 120 countries, issued a statement calling Israel's war on Gaza "illegal".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Kasasira |first1=Risdel |title=The Non-Aligned Movement calls Israel's war in Gaza illegal and condemns attacks on Palestinians |url=https://apnews.com/article/uganda-non-aligned-movement-israel-gaza-palestinian-22c852bd408cda0a904431d913728f32 |website=Associated Press |date=20 January 2024 |access-date=22 January 2024}}</ref>

In February 2024, [[Amnesty International]] warned that states arming Israel risked violating international law, stating, "By providing arms to Israel, EU states and the US are violating their responsibility to prevent genocide and contributing to war crimes and crimes against humanity."<ref>{{cite web |title=Amnesty says countries sending arms to Israel contributing to war crimes |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/13/israels-war-on-gaza-live-jordans-king-urges-ceasefire-in-biden-meeting?update=2705664 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=14 February 2024}}</ref> [[Agnes Callamard]], the head of Amnesty, wrote for ''[[Foreign Affairs]]'', stating international law was in its "death throes" due to the "culmination of years of erosion of the international rule of law and global human rights system".<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Callamard |first1=Agnès |title=Gaza and the End of the Rules-Based Order |url=https://www.foreignaffairs.com/israel/gaza-and-end-rules-based-order |journal=Foreign Affairs |date=15 February 2024 |access-date=17 February 2024}}</ref> The Israel-Palestine director for [[Human Rights Watch]] stated that years of no accountability for Israel had led to "this flagrant disregard for the most basic principles" of international law.<ref>{{cite web |title=Human Rights Watch says international law being 'demolished' in Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/13/israels-war-on-gaza-live-jordans-king-urges-ceasefire-in-biden-meeting?update=2705591 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=15 February 2024}}</ref> In March 2024, the [[Palestinian Centre for Human Rights]] stated that Europe and the U.S. were allowing Israel to commit crimes "with the absence of mechanisms that would compel it to abide by the rules of international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite web |title=US, European nations allow Israel to act with impunity: Rights group |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/9/israels-war-on-gaza-live-ceasefire-by-ramadan-looking-tough-biden-says?update=2761004 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=11 March 2024}}</ref> [[Physicians for Human Rights–Israel]] stated it was preparing to take the Israeli military to court for its "indiscriminate" [[bombing of Gaza]], stating Israel was failing to fulfill its "obligation according to international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite web |title=Despite ICJ measures, Israel continues 'indiscriminate' bombings |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/12/israels-war-on-gaza-live-2000-medical-staff-starving-in-north-ministry?update=2767611 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=15 March 2024}}</ref>

In May 2024, the [[World Council of Churches]] condemned Israel's "violations of international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite web |title=World Council of Churches condemns Israel's conduct in Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/5/29/israels-war-on-gaza-live-tent-cities-attacked-as-tanks-roll-into-rafah?update=2934128 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=8 June 2024}}</ref> The [[International Committee of the Red Cross]] urged adherence to the Geneva Conventions in August 2024, stating they were being ignored in Gaza and elsewhere.<ref>{{cite web |title=Red Cross urges adherence to Geneva Conventions, 75 years on |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/program/newsfeed/2024/8/12/red-cross-urges-adherence-to-geneva-conventions-75-years-on#:~:text=NewsFeed-,Red%20Cross%20urges%20adherence%20to%20Geneva%20Conventions%2C%2075%20years%20on,Sudan%2C%20Myanmar%20and%20the%20DRC. |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=25 August 2024}}</ref>

===United Nations===
[[United Nations special rapporteur|Independent United Nations experts]]{{efn|[[Francesca Albanese]], [[Pedro Arrojo-Agudo]], {{interlanguage link|Balakrishnan Rajagopal|de}}, Aua Baldé, Gabriella Citroni, [[Angkhana Neelaphaijit|Angkhana Neelapaijit]], Grażyna Baranowska, Ana Lorena Delgadillo Pérez, [[Reem Alsalem]], [[Mama Fatima Singhateh]], {{interlanguage link|Morris Tidball-Binz|de}}, {{interlanguage link|Ian Fry|de}}, [[Javaid Rehman]], [[Siobhán Mullally]], [[Ashwini K.P.|Ashwini K. P.]], Tomoya Obokata, {{interlanguage link|Fernand de Varennes|de}}, [[Michael Fakhri]], [[Irene Khan]], [[Mary Lawlor (human rights advocate)|Mary Lawlor]], [[Dorothy Estrada-Tanck]], {{interlanguage link|Ivana Radačić|hr}}, [[Elizabeth Broderick]], Meskerem Geset Techane, [[Melissa Upreti]], [[Farida Shaheed]], {{interlanguage link|Mohamed Abdelsalam Babiker|de}}, [[Clément Nyaletsossi Voule]], [[Attiya Waris]], [[Vitit Muntarbhorn]], {{interlanguage link|Barbara G. Reynolds|de}}, [[Bina D'Costa]], Catherine S. Namakula, Dominique Day, Miriam Ekiudoko, [[Isha Dyfan]], [[Alexandra Xanthaki]], [[José Francisco Calí Tzay]], [[Richard Bennett (UN)|Richard Bennett]], Obiora C. Okafor, [[David Richard Boyd]], Livingstone Sewanyana, [[Alice Jill Edwards]], [[Muluka-Anne Miti-Drummond]], Ravindran Daniel, Sorcha MacLeod, Chris Kwaja, Carlos Salazar Couto, and {{interlanguage link|Surya Deva|de}}.<ref name="UNexpertsOct12" />}} condemned the IDF's actions in Gaza, saying Israel had resorted to "indiscriminate military attacks" and "[[collective punishment]]".<ref name="UN experts"/> Israeli authorities said that the airstrikes are intended to degrade the military infrastructure that is frequently constructed in close proximity to residential areas and civilian establishments.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/25/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-airstrikes.html |title=Israel's Strikes on Gaza Are Some of the Most Intense This Century |date=25 October 2023 |work=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref> They also denounced the "deliberate and widespread killing and hostage-taking of innocent civilians" by Hamas, calling them "heinous violations of international law and international crimes".<ref name="UNexpertsOct12">{{#invoke:cite|web|date=12 October 2023 |title=Israel/occupied Palestinian territory: UN experts deplore attacks on civilians, call for truce and urge international community to address root causes of violence |url=https://www.un.org/unispal/document/un-experts-statement-gaza-israel-12oct2023/ |publisher=[[Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights]]}}</ref> Israel's [[Evacuation of northern Gaza|forced evacuation of northern Gaza]] also drew international condemnation. On 13 October 2023, Paula Gaviria Betancur, UN Special Rapporteur on the human rights of [[internally displaced person]]s, called it a "crime against humanity".<ref name="ohchr-rescind">{{Cite web|date=13 October 2023|title=Israel must rescind evacuation order for northern Gaza and comply with international law: UN expert|url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2023/10/israel-must-rescind-evacuation-order-northern-gaza-and-comply-international|publisher=OHCHR|access-date=22 October 2023|archive-date=14 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231014175126/https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2023/10/israel-must-rescind-evacuation-order-northern-gaza-and-comply-international|url-status=live}}</ref> On 14 October, [[Francesca Albanese]], the [[United Nations Special Rapporteur on the occupied Palestinian territories]], characterized it as a "repeat of the 1948 [[Nakba]]", noting Israeli public officials' open advocacy for another Nakba.<ref name="OHCHR102023"/> On 16 November, UN experts reported that "grave violations" committed by Israeli forces against the Palestinians of Gaza "point to a genocide in the making" and called on the international community to prevent this unfolding genocide.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2023/11/gaza-un-experts-call-international-community-prevent-genocide-against |title=Gaza: UN experts call on international community to prevent genocide against the Palestinian people |date=16 November 2023 |website=[[OHCHR]] |access-date=22 December 2023 |quote=Grave violations committed by Israel against Palestinians in the aftermath of 7 October, particularly in Gaza, point to a genocide in the making, UN experts said today. They illustrated evidence of increasing genocidal incitement, overt intent to "destroy the Palestinian people under occupation", loud calls for a 'second Nakba' in Gaza and the rest of the occupied Palestinian territory, and the use of powerful weaponry with inherently indiscriminate impacts, resulting in a colossal death toll and destruction of life-sustaining infrastructure. |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231224050530/https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2023/11/gaza-un-experts-call-international-community-prevent-genocide-against |archive-date=24 December 2023}}</ref> The [[OHCHR]] expressed concern regarding reports of "mass detentions, ill-treatment and enforced disappearances of possibly thousands of Palestinians" in the north of Gaza.<ref name="detainees from Gaza">{{cite web |date=20 December 2023 |title=Urgently investigate inhumane treatment and enforced disappearance of Palestinians detainees from Gaza |url=https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2023/12/urgently-investigate-inhumane-treatment-and-enforced-disappearance-of-palestinians-detainees-from-gaza/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231222015304/https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2023/12/urgently-investigate-inhumane-treatment-and-enforced-disappearance-of-palestinians-detainees-from-gaza/ |archive-date=22 December 2023 |website=[[Amnesty International]] |access-date=22 December 2023}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|date=16 December 2023 |title=UN Human Rights Office – OPT: Disturbing reports from the north of Gaza of mass detentions, ill-treatment and enforced disappearances of possibly thousands of Palestinians – occupied Palestinian territory |url=https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/un-human-rights-office-opt-disturbing-reports-north-gaza-mass-detentions-ill-treatment-and-enforced-disappearances-possibly-thousands-palestinians |access-date=22 December 2023 |website=[[ReliefWeb]]}}</ref>

On 23 February 2024, the OHCHR stated that any transfer of weapons to Israel must be halted immediately as their use in Gaza is "likely to violate international humanitarian law".<ref name="OHCHR230224">{{cite web|url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2024/02/arms-exports-israel-must-stop-immediately-un-experts|title=Arms exports to Israel must stop immediately: UN experts |date=23 February 2024|website=[[OHCHR]] |access-date=25 February 2024 |archive-date=25 February 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240225012016/https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2024/02/arms-exports-israel-must-stop-immediately-un-experts|url-status=live}}</ref> On 27 March, Albanese stated that there are "reasonable grounds" to believe that Israel is committing genocide in Gaza through the use of unlawful weaponry, the destruction of civilian infrastructure and man made starvation, which has been accompanied by "a pervasive anti-Palestinian narrative and dehumanization emanating from the uppermost tiers of Israeli society."<ref>{{cite news |last=Mian|first=Louis |date=27 March 2024 |title='Reasonable grounds' to believe Israel is committing genocide in Gaza, UN rights expert says|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/03/27/middleeast/israel-committing-genocide-in-gaza-un-rights-expert-says-intl/index.html|work=CNN |location= |access-date=28 March 2024}}</ref> In March 2024, Betancur stated the world "must abandon the fiction that Israel will respect the principles of international humanitarian and human rights law in its military operations".<ref>{{cite web |title=Gaza: Israel's dehumanisation of displaced persons must end, says UN expert |url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2024/03/gaza-israels-dehumanisation-displaced-persons-must-end-says-un-expert |website=OHCHR |publisher=United Nations |access-date=10 March 2024}}</ref> {{interlanguage link|Balakrishnan Rajagopal|de}}, the UN special rapporteur on the right to adequate housing, stated Israel's destruction of housing and civilian infrastructure amounted to a war crime and crime against humanity.<ref>{{cite web |title='War crimes' as Gaza homes 'systematically destroyed': UN expert |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/8/israel-hamas-war-live-humanitarian-aid-targeted-amid-gaza-bombardment?update=2472003 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=8 November 2023}}</ref>{{efn|Rajagopal stated, "If the International Criminal Court does not act very soon, we need a special tribunal for Gaza and action by States".<ref>{{cite web |title=Events in Gaza stem from 'institutionalised impunity' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/12/24/israel-hamas-war-live-israeli-bombardments-hunger-spread-in-gaza?update=2577125 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=24 December 2023}}</ref>}} UN Human Rights chief Volker Türk stated Israel's collective punishment and forcible evacuation of Gazans were both war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |title=At Rafah crossing, Türk says both Israel and Hamas have committed war crimes |url=https://news.un.org/en/story/2023/11/1143362 |website=UN News |date=8 November 2023 |publisher=United Nations |access-date=9 November 2023}}</ref>

According to [[UNRWA]], its staff faced "torture, ill-treatment, abuse, and sexual exploitation" at the hands of Israeli authorities. The organization also accused Israel of extracting forced confessions from its staff of being involved with Hamas through torture.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Massoud |first=Adla |date=4 March 2024 |title=Israel accuses UNRWA of hiring hundreds of 'terrorists' as agency claims torture of staff |url=https://www.thenationalnews.com/world/us-news/2024/03/04/israel-accuses-unrwa-of-hiring-hundreds-of-terrorists-as-agency-claims-torture-of-staff/ |access-date=9 March 2024 |website=The National |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=9 March 2024 |title=UNRWA report says Israel coerced some agency employees to falsely admit Hamas links |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/unrwa-report-says-israel-coerced-some-agency-employees-falsely-admit-hamas-links-2024-03-08 |access-date=9 March 2023 |website=[[Reuters]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=8 March 2024 |title=Israel abused Gaza war detainees, UN report alleges |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-68514816 |access-date=9 March 2024 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref>

A group of UN experts warned of "a genocide in the making" in Gaza.<ref>{{cite web |title=Gaza: UN experts call on international community to prevent genocide against the Palestinian people |url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2023/11/gaza-un-experts-call-international-community-prevent-genocide-against#:~:text=We%20are%20also%20profoundly%20concerned,prevent%20genocide%2C”%20they%20said. |website=OHCHR |publisher=United Nations |access-date=16 November 2023}}</ref> [[Pedro Arrojo-Agudo]], the UN special rapporteur on water and sanitation, stated that under Article 7 of the Rome Statute, cutting off basic supplies, such as water, was a crime against humanity.<ref>{{cite web |title=Cutting off clean water is crime against humanity: UN expert |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/17/israel-hamas-war-live-thousands-in-danger-of-death-amid-hospital-siege?update=2495050 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=17 November 2023}}</ref> [[Martin Griffiths]] stated the [[2023 Gaza humanitarian crisis|humanitarian crisis in Gaza]] was intolerable and that "international humanitarian law appears to have been turned on its head".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Griffiths |first1=Martin |title=Mr. Martin Griffiths, Under-Secretary-General for Humanitarian Affairs and Emergency Relief Coordinator - Informal Plenary Meeting of the General Assembly on the Humanitarian Situation in the Gaza Strip - Virtual, Friday, 17 November 2023 |url=https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/mr-martin-griffiths-under-secretary-general-humanitarian-affairs-and-emergency-relief-coordinator-informal-plenary-meeting-general-assembly-humanitarian-situation-gaza-strip-virtual-friday-17-november-2023 |website=UNOCHA |date=17 November 2023 |access-date=17 November 2023}}</ref> Philippe Lazzarini called Israel's killing of United Nations workers a "blatant disregard of international humanitarian law".<ref>{{cite web |title=Transcript: Phillippe Lazzarini, UNRWA commissioner general, on "Face the Nation," Nov. 26, 2023 |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/phillippe-lazzarini-unrwa-commissioner-general-face-the-nation-transcript-11-26-2023/ |website=CBS News |date=26 November 2023 |publisher=Face the Nation |access-date=27 November 2023}}</ref> The United Nations special rapporteurs on extrajudicial executions and torture signed a joint statement urging a war crimes investigation.<ref>{{cite web |title=UN Experts Urge War Crimes Probe In Israel, Palestinian Territories |url=https://www.barrons.com/news/un-experts-urge-war-crimes-probe-in-israel-palestinian-territories-17c8c4a2# |publisher= Agence France Presse |website=Barron's |access-date=28 November 2023}}</ref> The OHCHR stated it had "serious concerns" about Israel's compliance with international law.<ref>{{cite web |title=UN's Türk urges probe into alleged sexual violence during Hamas terror attacks |url=https://news.un.org/en/story/2023/12/1144432 |website=UN News |date=6 December 2023 |publisher=United Nations |access-date=6 December 2023}}</ref> [[Tlaleng Mofokeng]], the special rapporteur on health, stated Israel had violated special medical protections in an "unrelenting war" on health.<ref>{{cite web |title=UN expert condemns 'unrelenting war' on health system amid airstrikes on hospitals and health workers |url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2023/12/gaza-un-expert-condemns-unrelenting-war-health-system-amid-airstrikes |website=UNHRC |publisher=United Nations |access-date=7 December 2023}}</ref>

Speaking about Israel's planned [[Rafah offensive]], the UN secretary-general [[Antonio Guterres]] stated, "International humanitarian law lies in tatters".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Nichols |first1=Michelle |title=UN chief calls for Gaza truce, massive lifesaving aid deliveries |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/un-chief-calls-gaza-truce-massive-lifesaving-aid-deliveries-2024-03-11/ |website=Reuters |access-date=14 March 2024}}</ref> A week later, Guterres condemned Israel's blocking of humanitarian aid, stating, "Nothing justifies the collective punishment of the Palestinian people".<ref>{{cite web |title=UN Chief Assails Israel for Blocking Gaza Aid Trucks |url=https://www.voanews.com/a/un-chief-assails-israel-for-blocking-gaza-aid-trucks-/7540563.html |website=VOA |date=24 March 2024 |access-date=25 March 2024}}</ref> In September 2024, Guterres stated Israel had committed "very dramatic violations of the international humanitarian law" and described a "total absence of an effective protection of civilians."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Nichols |first1=Michelle |title=UN chief says lack of accountability on UN staff killings in Gaza 'unacceptable' |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/un-chief-says-lack-accountability-un-staff-killings-gaza-unacceptable-2024-09-11/ |website=Reuters |access-date=17 September 2024}}</ref>

On 8 June 2024, the United Nations added Israel, Hamas, and the Palestinian Islamic Jihad to a blacklist of countries and organizations that have committed abuses against children in armed conflict.<ref>{{cite news |agency=Associated Press |title=UN will describe Israel and Hamas as violating children's rights in armed conflict |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2024/06/07/un-israel-hamas-war-childrens-rights-00162370 |access-date=June 8, 2024 |work=[[Politico]] |date=June 7, 2024}}</ref> Regarding Israel being put on the list, President Netanyahu said the United Nations had put itself on the "blacklist of history".<ref>{{cite news |author=<!--not stated--> |title=Israel military on UN failing to protect children list |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c8883ndp2lko |access-date=June 8, 2024 |work=[[BBC News]] |date=June 7, 2024}}</ref> [[Permanent Representative of Israel to the United Nations|Israel-UN Reperesentative]] [[Gilad Erdan]] also condemned the designation, describing it as "simply outrageous and wrong", despite Israel being responsible for overwhelming majority of civilian fatalities in the war, and having killed over 15,500 children by June.<ref>{{cite news |author=Al Jazeera staff |title=UN adding Israel to 'blacklist' of countries harming children in conflict |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/6/7/un-adding-israel-to-blacklist-of-countries-harming-children-in-conflict |access-date=8 June 2024 |work=[[Al Jazeera]] |date=7 June 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |author1=<!--not stated--> |title=UN spokesman blasts Erdan for 'shocking' decision to release video of call informing him Israel on 'list of shame' |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/un-spokesman-blasts-erdan-for-shocking-decision-to-release-video-of-call-informing-him-israel-on-list-of-shame/ |access-date=June 8, 2024 |date=June 7, 2024}}</ref> [[Chris Sidoti]], a member of the independent [[Independent International Commission of Inquiry on the Occupied Palestinian Territory|United Nations Commission of Inquiry]],  stated, "The only conclusion you can draw is that the Israeli army is one of the most criminal armies in the world".<ref>{{cite web |title=Independent rights probe highlights Israeli 'destruction and dislocation' tactics in Gaza |url=https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/06/1151211 |website=UN News |date=19 June 2024 |publisher=United Nations |access-date=29 June 2024}}</ref>

==Lawsuits and investigations==
===Investigations===
The UK's [[Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office]] opened an investigation into Israeli violations of international humanitarian law.<ref>{{cite web |title=UK unable to conclude Israel followed international law in Gaza, court documents show |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/1/20/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israel-denied-70-of-aid-to-north-gaza-says-un?update=2635267 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=21 January 2024}}</ref> Court documents cited by Amnesty International indicated the UK office was unable to determine if Israel was in compliance with international law, but concluded there were "serious concerns" about legal breaches.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Wintour |first1=Patrick |title=Foreign Office lawyers 'unable to conclude if Israeli bombing was lawful' |url=https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/jan/19/foreign-office-lawyers-unable-conclude-israeli-bombing-lawful#:~:text=UK%20Foreign%20Office%20legal%20advisers,of%20Gaza%2C%20court%20documents%20reveal. |website=The Guardian |date=19 January 2024 |access-date=21 January 2024 |ref=none}}</ref> In February 2024, the U.S. State Department announced it was investigating the [[31 October 2023 Jabalia refugee camp airstrike]] and Israel's possible use of white phosphorus in Lebanon.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Nissenbaum |first1=Dion |title=U.S. Probes Israeli Strikes That Killed Civilians in Gaza, Possible Use of White Phosphorus in Lebanon |url=https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/u-s-probes-israeli-strikes-that-killed-civilians-in-gaza-possible-use-of-white-phosphorus-in-lebanon-b8fb043b?mod=browser_push |newspaper=WSJ |access-date=14 February 2024}}</ref> [[Alice Jill Edwards]], the [[United Nations Special Rapporteur on Torture and Other Cruel, Inhuman or Degrading Treatment or Punishment|United Nations Special Rapporteur on Torture]], stated she was investigating torture and mistreatment of Palestinian detainees by the Israeli army.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Tétrault-Farber |first1=Gabrielle |title=U.N. expert on torture examines treatment of Palestinian detainees |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/un-expert-torture-examines-treatment-palestinian-detainees-2024-03-08/ |website=Reuters |access-date=10 March 2024}}</ref>

Following the release of footage showing airstrikes killing five Palestinian men walking along a dirt road in Gaza, the IDF announced the incident was being investigated by its "fact finding" body for potential crimes by its forces.<ref>{{cite web |title=Israel to investigate airstrike that killed five men walking in Gaza |url=https://news.sky.com/story/israel-gaza-hamas-latest-middle-east-live-updates-sky-news-blog-12978800?postid=7423428#liveblog-body |website=Sky News |access-date=24 March 2024}}</ref> A US State Department official said, "Israel has an obligation to investigate credible allegations of law of war violations".<ref>{{cite web |title=US says video showing Israeli drone killing 4 Palestinians 'disturbing' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/3/23/israels-war-on-gaza-live-netanyahu-brushes-off-blinken-over-rafah-attack?update=2792714 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=25 March 2024}}</ref> In April 2024, the U.S. Secretary of State denied it had "double-standards" regarding Israel, stating the U.S. was "looking at" alleged violations of international humanitarian law.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Pamuk |first1=Humeyra |last2=Landay |first2=Jonathan |title=Blinken denies US double standard over alleged Israeli rights abuses |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israels-gaza-war-has-negatively-impacted-human-rights-says-us-report-2024-04-22/ |website=Reuters |access-date=24 April 2024}}</ref> In an internal U.S. State Department memo, senior officials stated they did not find Israel's assurances that it's using U.S. weapons in accordance with international humanitarian law "credible or reliable".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Pamuk |first1=Humeyra |title=Some US officials say in internal memo Israel may be violating international law in Gaza |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/some-us-officials-say-internal-memo-israel-may-be-violating-international-law-2024-04-27/ |website=Reuters |access-date=30 April 2024}}</ref> On 29 April, the United States reported a finding that five Israeli units committed human rights violations before the Gaza war.<ref>{{cite news |last=Borger |first=Julian |title=US finds Israeli units committed human rights abuses before Gaza war
|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/29/idf-human-rights-violation-gaza-us-state-department |website=The Guardian |date=29 April 2024 |access-date=1 May 2024}}</ref> In May 2024, the U.S. State Department found it was "reasonable to assess" that U.S. made weapons had been used by Israel "in instances inconsistent" with international humanitarian law.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Pamuk |first1=Humeyra |title=US says Israel's use of weapons may have violated international law |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-says-it-was-reasonable-assess-israel-used-us-weapons-inconsistent-with-2024-05-10/ |website=Reuters |access-date=16 May 2024}}</ref> In June 2024, Israel's top military lawyer stated 70 possible legal violations were under investigation.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Maanit |first1=Chen |title=Top Israeli Military Lawyer Investigating About 70 Possible Legal Violations During Gaza War |url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2024-05-27/ty-article/.premium/top-idf-lawyer-investigating-about-70-possible-violations-during-gaza-war/0000018f-b9cb-df13-a3af-bddf0d610000 |website=Haaretz |access-date=17 June 2024}}</ref> The military did not disclose the full list of investigations.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Frankel |first1=Julia |last2=Jeffery |first2=Jack |title=The Israeli army says it investigates itself. Where do those investigations stand? |url=https://abcnews.go.com/International/wireStory/israeli-army-investigates-investigations-stand-110749914 |website=ABC News |publisher=Associated Press |access-date=17 June 2024}}</ref>

In July 2024, Israeli state prosecutors stated they were seeking a probe into National Security minister [[Itamar Ben-Gvir]], as a measure to show the International Court of Justice it was complying with its orders to investigate individuals responsible for inciting genocide.<ref>{{cite web |title=State prosecutor seeking probe of Ben Gvir for anti-Gazan incitement |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/state-prosecutor-seeking-probe-of-ben-gvir-for-anti-gazan-incitement-report/# |website=The Times of Israel |access-date=13 July 2024}}</ref> In September 2024, ''[[:he:בחדרי חרדים|Behadrei Haredim]]'', an Israeli Orthodox news site, reported that Israeli officials had shared its investigatory findings related to 7 October with the United States, except for evidence collected from IDF soldiers, fearing the evidence could be used in The Hague.<ref>{{cite web |last1=לפקוביץ |first1=ישראל |title=ישראל העבירה לארה"ב עדויות מהטבח, מלבד של החיילים |url=https://www.bhol.co.il/news/1673169 |language=he|website=Behadrei Haredim |date=5 September 2024 |access-date=13 September 2024}}</ref> In October 2024, Belgium opened an investigation of one of its dual citizens suspected of committing war crimes in the Gaza Strip.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Giordano |first1=Elena |title=Belgium opens war crime probe into Brussels man fighting for Israel in Gaza |url=https://www.politico.eu/article/belgium-opens-war-crimes-probe-belgian-soldier-fighting-israel-in-gaza-refaim-unit/ |website=Politico |date=18 October 2024 |access-date=21 October 2024}}</ref>

According to five former US officials on November 7, 2025, last year, Israeli military lawyers reported that evidence might be sufficient to support Israeli's accusations of war crimes. US decided that its support for Israel was still legal because the US had not collected its own evidence of this kind.<ref>{{cite news |title=Exclusive: US intel found Israeli military lawyers warned there was evidence of Gaza war crimes, former US officials say |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-intel-found-israeli-military-lawyers-warned-there-was-evidence-gaza-war-2025-11-07/|work=Reuters|date=7 November 2025}}</ref>

===Lawsuits===
====ICC lawsuits====
{{Further|International Criminal Court arrest warrants for Israeli figures}}
On 9 November 2023, three Palestinian civil rights groups filed a lawsuit against Israel with the International Criminal Court.<ref>{{cite web |title=Three rights groups file ICC lawsuit against Israel over Gaza 'genocide' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/11/9/three-rights-groups-file-icc-lawsuit-against-israel-over-gaza-genocide |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=9 November 2023}}</ref> The groups charged Israel with war crimes, [[apartheid]], and genocide, calling for the ICC to issue arrest warrants for top Israeli officials.<ref>{{cite web |title=ICC suit filed against Israel over 'genocide' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/9/israel-gaza-war-live-day-34?update=2474380 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=9 November 2023}}</ref> On 10 November, President Gustavo Petro announced Colombia was cosponsoring an [[Algeria]]n ICC suit charging Israel with war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |last1=El-Assasy |first1=Ahmad |title=Colombia Confirms Support Algeria's Lawsuit against Netanyahu |url=https://see.news/colombia-confirms-support-algerias-lawsuit-against-netanyahu |website=[[Sada El-Balad]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231110144248/https://see.news/colombia-confirms-support-algerias-lawsuit-against-netanyahu |access-date=10 November 2023|archive-date=10 November 2023 }}</ref> On 14 November, Human Rights Watch called on the ICC to investigate Israeli attacks on hospitals and ambulances.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Iordache |first1=Ruxandra |title=Human Rights Watch calls for investigation into Israeli hostilities against Gaza Strip hospitals |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2023/11/14/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-latest-news-from-gaza.html |website=CNBC |date=14 November 2023 |access-date=14 November 2023}}</ref> A group of lawyers representing victims of Israeli attacks filed a suit in the ICC, charging Israel with genocide.<ref>{{cite web |title=Lawyers for Gaza victims file case at International Criminal Court |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/11/15/lawyers-for-gaza-victims-file-case-at-international-criminal-court |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=16 November 2023}}</ref> South African foreign minister [[Naledi Pandor]] called on the ICC to speed up its investigation of Israeli war crimes, crimes against humanity, and genocide, and stated warrants of arrest should be issued for Benjamin Netanyahu.<ref>{{cite web |title=Netanyahu should be arrested: South Africa's foreign minister |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/12/israel-gaza-war-live-israeli-army-surrounding-al-quds-hospital?update=2480833 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=12 November 2023}}</ref> On 16 November, South African president Cyril Ramaphosa stated South Africa had referred Israel to the ICC for war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Magome |first1=Mogomotsi |title=South Africa refers Israel to ICC over Gaza attacks as pressure mounts to cut diplomatic ties |url=https://news.yahoo.com/south-africa-refers-israel-icc-111827954.html |website=Yahoo! News |date=16 November 2023 |publisher=Associated Press |access-date=16 November 2023}}</ref> On 17 November, Karim Ahmad Khan stated the ICC had received a joint request by South Africa, [[Bangladesh]], [[Bolivia]], [[Comoros]], and [[Djibouti]] to investigate alleged Israeli war crimes.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Israel is committing war crimes in Palestinian territories, five nations charge |url=https://www.jpost.com/breaking-news/article-773802# |website=[[The Jerusalem Post]] |date=17 November 2023 |access-date=17 November 2023 |issn=0792-822X}}</ref> On 28 November, Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan stated Israeli officials should stand trial in international courts for war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Gumrukcu |first1=Tuvan |title=Erdogan tells UN chief Israel must be tried in international courts for Gaza crimes |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/erdogan-tells-uns-guterres-that-israel-must-be-tried-international-courts-over-2023-11-28/ |website=Reuters |access-date=21 February 2024}}</ref> On 20 December, [[Democracy for the Arab World Now|DAWN]] provided the ICC prosecutor with a list of 40 Israeli commanding officers to be charged with war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |title=DAWN submits to ICC Prosecutor List of 40 Israeli Commanding Officers Executing and Planning Gaza Assault |url=https://dawnmena.org/international-criminal-court-investigate-these-israeli-suspects-in-war-crimes-crimes-against-humanity-probe/ |website=DAWN |date=20 December 2023 |access-date=21 December 2023}}</ref>

On 22 December 2023, [[Reporters Without Borders]] filed an ICC complaint against Israel for "probable war crimes".<ref>{{cite web |title=Reporters Without Borders files second Gaza complaint to ICC |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/12/22/israel-hamas-war-live-un-security-council-to-vote-on-gaza-resolution?update=2573869 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=23 December 2023}}</ref> On 6 January, a group of 100 Chilean lawyers filed a complaint at the ICC accusing Netanyahu of committing war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |title=100 Chilean lawyers accuse Netanyahu of war crimes, file complaint at ICC: Report |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/1/6/israel-war-on-gaza-live-israeli-forces-raid-occupied-west-bank-towns?update=2600731 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=6 January 2024}}</ref> On 18 January, the foreign ministries of [[Secretary of Foreign Affairs (Mexico)|Mexico]] and [[Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Chile)|Chile]] referred Israel to the ICC for potential war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Madry |first1=Kylie |title=Mexico, Chile refer Israel-Hamas conflict to ICC over potential crimes |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/mexico-chile-refer-israel-hamas-conflict-court-over-possible-crimes-2024-01-18/ |website=Reuters |access-date=19 January 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Mexico and Chile ask International Criminal Court to investigate possible crimes in Gaza |url=https://abcnews.go.com/International/wireStory/mexico-chile-international-criminal-court-investigate-crimes-gaza-106495506 |website=ABC News |publisher=Associated Press |access-date=19 January 2024}}</ref>{{efn|Both countries representatives stated the referral was in part due to the increased violence and previous numerous reports from the United Nations.}} In October 2024, a Dutch lawyer submitted the names of 1,000 IDF soldiers to the ICC, stating they had participated in war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |title=Dutch lawyer submits case against 1,000 Israeli soldiers to ICC |url=https://www.newarab.com/news/dutch-lawyer-submits-case-against-1000-israeli-soldiers-icc |website=The New Arab |access-date=14 October 2024}}</ref>

In April 2024, the government of Israel indicated concern that the ICC might soon issue arrest warrants for senior Israeli officials for alleged violations of international humanitarian law in Gaza.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Macaskill |first1=Andrew |title=Israel concerned over possible ICC arrest warrants related to Gaza war |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israel-concerned-over-possible-icc-arrest-warrants-related-gaza-war-2024-04-29/ |website=Reuters |access-date=2 May 2024}}</ref> In May 2024, prosecutors from the ICC reportedly interviewed two medics from [[Al-Shifa Hospital]] and [[Nasser Hospital]] about possible crimes committed in Gaza.<ref>{{cite web |last1=van den Berg |first1=Stephanie |title=Gaza hospital staff questioned by ICC war crimes prosecutors |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/gaza-hospital-staff-questioned-by-icc-war-crimes-prosecutors-sources-say-2024-04-29/#:~:text=THE%20HAGUE%2C%20April%2029%20(Reuters,crimes%20in%20the%20Gaza%20Strip. |website=Reuters |access-date=7 May 2024}}</ref> Later the same month, Reporters Without Borders filed its third Gaza complaint at the ICC.<ref>{{cite web |title=RSF files third complaint with ICC about Israeli war crimes against journalists in Gaza |url=https://rsf.org/en/rsf-files-third-complaint-icc-about-israeli-war-crimes-against-journalists-gaza |website=Reporters Without Borders |date=27 May 2024 |access-date=5 June 2024}}</ref> The ICC chief prosecutor requested arrest warrants for Israeli prime minister [[Benjamin Netanyahu]] and defense minister [[Yoav Gallant]] in May 2024; however, the court accepted ''[[amicus curiae]]'' observations on jurisdictional issues.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Haque |first1=Adil Ahmad |title="With Utmost Urgency": Arrest Warrants and Amicus Observations at the International Criminal Court |url=https://www.justsecurity.org/99916/icc-utmost-urgency-arrest-warrants/ |website=Just Security |date=9 September 2024 |access-date=13 September 2024}}</ref> In November 2024, it was announced that the ICC had issued arrest warrants for Netanyahu, Gallant, and a senior Hamas official, accusing them of war crimes during and after the October 7 attacks.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lister |first=Abbas Al Lawati, Nadeen Ebrahim, Dana Karni, Tim |date=2024-11-21 |title=International Criminal Court issues arrest warrant for Israeli Prime Minister |url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/11/21/middleeast/international-criminal-court-issues-arrest-warrant-for-israeli-prime-minister-intl/index.html |access-date=2024-11-21 |website=CNN |language=en}}</ref>

====ICJ lawsuit====
{{main|South Africa v. Israel (Genocide Convention)}}
{{Excerpt|Allegations of genocide in the 2023 Israeli attack on Gaza#International Court of Justice application}}

In May 2024, the ICJ ordered Israel to avoid any attack on Rafah which threatened the people of Gaza in whole or in part. After Israel continued with its offensive on Rafah, Norway’s Foreign Minister [[Espen Barth Eide]] stated it was in "material breach" of the ICJ ruling and international humanitarian law.<ref>{{cite web |title=Continued attacks on Rafah are 'in breach of international humanitarian law': Norway's FM |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/5/27/israels-war-on-gaza-live-news-35-killed-in-rafah-tent-bombings?update=2928769 |website=Al Jazeera |access-date=5 June 2024}}</ref>

====CCR lawsuit against Joe Biden====
{{main|Defense for Children International – Palestine et al v. Biden et al}}
{{see also|Accusations of United States complicity in Israeli war crimes in the Gaza Strip}}
On 13 November 2023, the New York-based [[Center for Constitutional Rights]] (CCR) sued Joe Biden for allegedly failing in his duties, defined under national and international laws, to prevent Israel committing genocide in Gaza.<ref name="GuardianBiden">{{Cite news |last=McGreal |first=Chris |date=13 November 2023 |title=US rights group sues Biden for alleged 'failure to prevent genocide' in Gaza |language=en-GB |work=The Guardian |url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/13/biden-lawsuit-alleged-failure-prevent-genocide-israel-palestine |access-date=23 November 2023 |issn=0261-3077}}</ref> The complaint, filed on behalf of Palestinians in Gaza and the US, alleged that Israel's "mass killings", targeting of civilian infrastructure and forced expulsions amounted to genocide.<ref name="GuardianBiden" /><ref name="TIMEBiden">{{Cite magazine |last=Mansoor |first=Sanya |date=21 November 2023 |title=Pro-Palestinian Americans Are Pushing Biden to Pivot |url=https://time.com/6337911/biden-israel-policy-palestine-pressure/ |access-date=23 November 2023 |magazine=TIME |language=en |archive-date=2 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240102191717/https://time.com/6337911/biden-israel-policy-palestine-pressure/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> The CCR said that the US and other countries had a duty to do all they could to stop the killing. "As Israel's closest ally and strongest supporter, being its biggest provider of military assistance by a large margin and with Israel being the largest cumulative recipient of US foreign assistance since World War II, the United States has the means available to have a deterrent effect on Israeli officials now pursuing genocidal acts against the Palestinian people in Gaza," the complaint argued.<ref name="GuardianBiden" />

The suit, filed in federal court in California, asked the court to bar the US from providing weapons, money and diplomatic support to Israel.<ref name="GuardianBiden" /> It also sought a declaration that the president, the secretary of state, Antony Blinken, and the defense secretary, [[Lloyd Austin]], were required "to take all measures within their power to prevent Israel's commission of genocidal acts against the Palestinian people of Gaza." Genocide scholar William Schabas said in a declaration in the lawsuit that in his view there was a "serious risk of genocide" and that the US was "in breach of its obligation" under the 1948 Genocide Convention and international law.<ref name="TIMEBiden" /><ref name="CNSBiden">{{Cite web |last=Hanson |first=Natalie |date=23 November 2023 |title=Palestinians file lawsuit accusing Biden administration of violating Genocide Convention |url=https://www.courthousenews.com/palestinians-file-lawsuit-accusing-biden-administration-of-violating-genocide-convention/ |website=[[Courthouse News Service]]}}</ref>

On 31 January 2024, the case was dismissed. The judge said that the [[Constitution of the United States|US Constitution]] limited his actions, that he would have preferred to have issued the injunction and urged President Biden to rethink U.S. policy, writing "it is plausible that Israel's conduct amounts to genocide."<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/31/world/middleeast/joe-biden-israel-support.html|title=A federal judge dismisses a suit to block U.S. support of Israel — but urges Biden to re-examine his approach.|first=Shawn|last=Hubler|work=The New York Times |date=1 February 2024|via=NYTimes.com}}</ref>

====Hague lawsuit====

On 4 December 2023, Human rights organisations [[Oxfam]] Novib, PAX Nederland, and The Rights Forum had taken the Dutch State to court to stop the export of parts for F-35 fighter jets arguing that they contribute to violations of international law in Gaza. Oxfam argued that the export "made the Netherlands complicit in violations of the laws of war and the collective punishment of the civilian population of Gaza".<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 December 2023 |title=Rights orgs sue Netherlands over F-35 parts to Israel |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20231204-rights-orgs-sue-netherlands-over-f-35-parts-to-israel |access-date=12 February 2024 |website=France 24 |language=en}}</ref> On 15 December 2023, The Hague ruled that the state could keep exporting arms to Israel.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Netherlands can keep delivering F-35 parts to Israel, court rules {{!}} NL Times |url=https://nltimes.nl/2023/12/15/netherlands-can-keep-delivering-f-35-parts-israel-court-rules |access-date=12 February 2024 |website=nltimes.nl |date=15 December 2023 |language=en}}</ref> On 12 February 2024, the court of appeal in The Hague ruled that "There is a clear risk that Israel's F-35 fighter jets might be used in the commission of serious violations of international humanitarian law." The judges wrote, "Israel does not take sufficient account of the consequences of its attacks for the civilian population. Israel's attacks on Gaza have resulted in a disproportionate number of civilian casualties, including thousands of children" and that, " The Netherlands is a party to several international regulations which stipulate that if a clear risk of serious violations of international humanitarian law exists, the Netherlands has the obligation to prevent the export of military equipment." The court ordered that deliveries must stop within seven days.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Appeals court orders Netherlands to stop delivering F-35 fighter jet parts to Israel {{!}} NL Times |url=https://nltimes.nl/2024/02/12/appeals-court-orders-netherlands-stop-delivering-f-35-fighter-jet-parts-israel |access-date=12 February 2024 |website=nltimes.nl |date=12 February 2024 |language=en}}</ref>

====High Court lawsuit====

On 6 December 2023, Palestinian human rights organisation Al-Haq and UK-based [[Global Legal Action Network]] (GLAN) have commenced legal proceedings against the UK after written requests to suspend arms sales to Israel, citing alleged breaches of international law and UK rules, were repeatedly ignored. The filed papers detail allegations of indiscriminate attacks on civilians, starvation, forced displacement, and the serious risk of genocide, including statements from members of the Knesset and military leaders. The action is supported by the [[International Centre of Justice for Palestinians]] (ICJP) and a press briefing was held with GLAN, Al-Haq and ICJP and with [[Campaign Against Arms Trade]] (CAAT) and a member from Oxfam.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Legal and human rights groups take UK government to High Court over arms exports to Israel |url=https://www.alhaq.org/advocacy/22299.html |access-date=31 January 2024 |website=Al-Haq {{!}} Defending Human rights in Palestine since 1979 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Abdul |first=Geneva |date=6 December 2023 |title=UK government faces legal challenge over arms exports to Israel |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/06/uk-government-faces-legal-challenge-over-arms-exports-to-israel |access-date=31 January 2024 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref> The NGOs' lawyers submitted more than 100 pages of witness statements to the High Court in August 2024.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Wintour |first1=Patrick |title=Lawyers seeking arms export ban submit claims of Israeli war crimes to UK court |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/19/lawyers-seeking-arms-export-ban-submit-claims-israeli-war-crimes-uk-court |website=The Guardian |date=19 August 2024 |access-date=11 September 2024 |ref=none}}</ref>

====Federal Court of Australia lawsuit====

On 5 December 2023, Palestinian human rights groups, Al-Haq, [[Al Mezan Center for Human Rights]] and the [[Palestinian Centre for Human Rights]] (PCHR) have launched legal action in the [[Federal Court of Australia]]. The human rights groups seek access to all permits allowing the export of arms and weapons to Israel that have been granted by the [[Minister for Defence (Australia)|Minister for Defence]] since 7 October 2023. The application is supported by the [[Australian Centre for International Justice]] (ACIJ).<ref>{{Cite web |date=5 November 2023 |title=Joint Media Release: Palestinian human rights organisations launch court action to reveal 'secret' arms exports from Australia to Israel |url=https://acij.org.au/joint-media-release-palestinian-human-rights-organisations-launch-court-action-to-reveal-secret-arms-exports-from-australia-to-israel/ |access-date=31 January 2024 |website=Australian Centre for International Justice |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Canales |first=Sarah Basford |date=5 November 2023 |title=Legal action attempts to force Australia to reveal if arms exports are supporting Israel assault on Gaza |url=https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/nov/06/legal-action-attempts-to-force-australia-to-reveal-if-arms-exports-are-supporting-israel-assault-on-gaza |access-date=31 January 2024 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>

====Canadian Global Affairs Ministry lawsuit====
On 5 March 2024, Canadian Lawyers for International Human Rights (CLIHR), Al-Haq and a group of Palestinian-Canadians, have sued the Global Affairs Ministry for exporting military goods and technology to Israel during the Gaza conflict. They argue that the exports could be used in alleged human rights violations against Palestinians. The legal action accuses Canada's Foreign Minister Mélanie Joly of authorising the export of military goods and technology to Israel, amounting to at least at least C$28.5m ($21m), that could be used to commit violations of international law.<ref name="Yousif050324"/>

====Other====
In June 2024, a group of South Korean civil society organizations sued top Israeli government officials for genocide, crimes against humanity, and war crimes.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Benson |first1=Chris |title=South Korean lawsuit levels charges against Israeli officials for alleged war crimes in Gaza |url=https://www.upi.com/Top_News/World-News/2024/06/24/south-korea-Israel-genocide-Benjamin-Netanyahu-Peoples-Solidarity-for-Participatory-Democracy/9881719261585/ |website=UPI |access-date=4 July 2024 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250419080524/https://www.upi.com/Top_News/World-News/2024/06/24/south-korea-Israel-genocide-Benjamin-Netanyahu-Peoples-Solidarity-for-Participatory-Democracy/9881719261585/ |archive-date=19 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

The [[Hind Rajab Foundation]] has brought legal action in several countries against Israeli soldiers allegedly responsible for war crimes.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Karni |first=Dana |last2=Lister |first2=Tim |date=5 January 2025 |title=Israeli soldiers face growing risk of arrest abroad after Gaza service |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2025/01/05/world/israel-gaza-soldiers-arrest-war-crimes-intl/index.html |access-date=7 January 2025 |website=[[CNN]]}}</ref>

